RE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg9qiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAIHoQAHWOYmWgE/CkfUIK6nxstAMv\n1y6bQgItHT1VbwngOM5aXahwLNYXnOyq9Bn4Gx6CGRufcvYGPPY+UpVZj5OPIxVk\nNBXVCnLaGrxxcuL+osW19UDz7sPLZ2GqZmZcvVAed1IjJyAZsj0uRRhli8InbcXd\n+zcJDYdtd0vMVAz4/Qt+jkonQCm8NZdt+E65Kh1H5Xjjdv2qI5W9N/V7Qf4dGQly\nBPkP213+jvKO/0wEKmPkOjtwERvlYlbqID+eiGKBy7lwdzBJMc7vOzXB6Gu2Y2aA\nO/qDCNHmpj5A14q5Hl3mFGF/NQBRjRcH9YNisGZrwrw5pSyam3lBlz3bVz88T6j4\nkpYTYk7z70guF94njj8GZNNOpXIGpjsBvtcxr15Uj+sx1ZGr9f4AHuHso1eJEjQe\nd+2E094sPYVNjXvY1GmRruBiZwSUOEGMlj5qvLc4pQYnXScx/+unc+YQT59NR6dm\nQVXw6OofUJnnaheShyKtrtafz9iT9iCX2iSInmJJnfLk3bPkZO3FvZhCNndts+pn\nlH/sZb8OSGGIr10vhqFobmS2rSO9L+0TlTRfVtnghvLIcgWHzTNDsyd0HfTrG8mK\n/zYp7mV4CzWQlHX2RYrN8KFhqjknQ/x3fucOBvWOCs9nyX5mcMrM0O6YuAFEmD0v\nMXMYlBh2VKBXJpEojXNL\n=TTSh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c7bb7692c46adec6a0b22a58b5489cbe9fe64f84\nparent f4f138db65484d4938ef3759cb26cec1e789357d\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787026082 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787026082 -0400\n\nhotfix(code): wait for terminal resize layout (#5576)\n\nWaits for Textual to process the queued resize and layout cycle before\nthe chat-input resize regression test reads the applied composer height.\nThis removes the timing race that can observe the pre-resize 17-row\nvalue instead of the 5-row constrained value.","verified_at":"2026-08-18T04:08:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/00b8f3ab91dca4f81780ad985f560f577d90f5e9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/00b8f3ab91dca4f81780ad985f560f577d90f5e9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/00b8f3ab91dca4f81780ad985f560f577d90f5e9/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f4f138db65484d4938ef3759cb26cec1e789357d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f4f138db65484d4938ef3759cb26cec1e789357d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f4f138db65484d4938ef3759cb26cec1e789357d"}]},{"sha":"f4f138db65484d4938ef3759cb26cec1e789357d","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGY0ZjEzOGRiNjU0ODRkNDkzOGVmMzc1OWNiMjZjZWMxZTc4OTM1N2Q","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T03:56:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T03:56:10Z"},"message":"fix(code): bind Auto-mode \"yes\" to the paired `ask_user` question (#5038)\n\nWhen Auto mode asks you to confirm a specific high-risk action with\n`ask_user` — for example, \"Force-push `feature-x` to `origin`?\" — and\nyou answer \"yes\", Auto now approves that exact action. Before, Auto\ndenied it until you typed the full command again.\n\n---\n\n### The problem\n\nYou tell dcode to do a specific risky task. dcode shows the exact action\nin an `ask_user` prompt. You answer **\"yes\"**. dcode then proposes the\nexact `git push --force origin feature-x` call.\n\nBefore this change, Auto denied the call. The classifier saw only the\nanswer text (\"yes\"), which does not name an action or a target. You had\nto type the full command again to approve your own approval.\n\n### The fix: attach the \"yes\" to the paired question\n\nConsent has two parts: an action and a target. A bare \"yes\" has no\ntarget, so it must not approve anything on its own.\n\nThe fix pairs each server-validated answer with the exact question that\ndcode showed in the same `ask_user` call. The pairing is safe for three\nreasons specific to `ask_user`:\n\n1. The question text comes from the tool call arguments that the client\nalready validated against the receipt. It is not model prose from the\nassistant's chat message.\n2. The receipt confirms the answer count matches the question count for\nthat exact `tool_call_id`, so dcode aligns each question to its answer\nby index.\n3. Only one `ask_user` call in this turn can hold that `tool_call_id`,\nso the mapping is unambiguous.\n\nAuto trusts the question only as the action-and-target description that\nits own paired answer attaches to. The question alone approves nothing.\nThe answer alone approves nothing. Only the pair, matched to a tool call\nby canonical arguments, approves the call.\n\nThe invariant stays the same:\n\n> short affirmative **+ paired question that names action+target** ≥\nexplicit action+target for those exact calls. A short affirmative\n**alone** is not consent.\n\n### Scope of the binding\n\nAuto approves a call only when all of these are true:\n\n- The paired question names the action and the material target.\n- The answer is a short affirmative, for example: \"yes\", \"y\",\n\"approved\", \"go ahead\", \"lgtm\", \"do it\".\n- The tool call's canonical arguments match the action and target that\nthe question names.\n\nThe approval does not extend to a different target, a more destructive\nvariant (for example a force-push when the question asked about an\nordinary push), or extra tools in the same batch that the question did\nnot cover.\n\nAuto also handles polarity. If the question asks you to skip, avoid, or\nkeep rather than delete, an affirmative agrees with that negation. Auto\ndoes not invert the polarity to approve the destructive action.\n\n### How the change works\n\n`_same_turn_user_answers` now reads the `questions` list from the\nsame-turn `ask_user` arguments and emits a `question` field next to each\n`answer`. If the list is missing, malformed, or a different length than\nthe answers, the function returns no rows and the classifier falls back\nto the prior \"answer alone grants nothing\" behavior.\n\n`_CLASSIFIER_POLICY` is rewritten to describe the attachment model, the\ncanonical-argument match, the polarity rule, and the scope limits above.\n\nNo change to the `ask_user` receipt or schema, no cross-turn state, no\napproval-UI or public-API change. The new `question` field is internal\nand applies only to the current turn.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/6b48ff9d-e08c-711e-d526-9ccf88069d3b)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/6b48ff9d-e08c-711e-d526-9ccf88069d3b/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"dd824d3fb03a34a858ff59cc98341705c27b8f18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/dd824d3fb03a34a858ff59cc98341705c27b8f18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f4f138db65484d4938ef3759cb26cec1e789357d","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg9faCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAc3MQAHgh1hFE+emwDD0rnTpa+j9B\nnzjgQi6d2+/U7zyyXq/VDN7SRxY8PpaU5L2QgUdaJYcM3TXz/bsIBrbkEAUzplkU\ndGOj3HZcAHpNxLsuAL4ffSaI532Hs4aS9UeLGf2L9OZJ6p8hIorD8WQmthJU4MjL\nvMvm7fVZm3sLlaU3DosL04QQ4KXH/rV8pX3qAWL7WbgvQQ3GyXiES5W5smEsmDQY\nHwL2haUW+3AO+ugJRdN1ehCgOh9ylxp8fWcEEZA/xOOEsDFfdztuX5yoQwsO1Jyl\naIrDNbDFavC+L54tFKb3Gdbz6fSYqbG/wR2kfLfj6O0WZB98aWbm0HS9m1L5juhF\nScEmy/fTK24q+3m7f0XkGCUDNIzqFhoBIjYJKf0PRuAJLgbXJjFLFrJN70agOpdx\ntWY5Su8xbVgXnNAX60H4SXvkJv1/rg/Rs3LZZt6uWRpP9zCNRdU7UZ5UITPMNf27\nQPpL9mOGhe14lxjZUgn+HMSmobFvUlWZI55I/jTZw9QV47p7mbx/ulUOcrQ6P0/3\nGkLWqwCN6jpbVsa0z61VHysHSdk6y5f4Wb0rnzTvaHXXovCcK2ovlNjztFIF4SkT\no/+UUPUjeJLMRBvYfeKQKPeaCEasEDDYkD4wuRC3ttagrRgB3xxOoBRdsvBDi8KU\nJK7MQZghKAneeUebbKx2\n=mFcv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree dd824d3fb03a34a858ff59cc98341705c27b8f18\nparent 107980e387b3fa060c2b33e9bd31b57c387eddb6\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787025370 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787025370 -0400\n\nfix(code): bind Auto-mode \"yes\" to the paired `ask_user` question (#5038)\n\nWhen Auto mode asks you to confirm a specific high-risk action with\n`ask_user` — for example, \"Force-push `feature-x` to `origin`?\" — and\nyou answer \"yes\", Auto now approves that exact action. Before, Auto\ndenied it until you typed the full command again.\n\n---\n\n### The problem\n\nYou tell dcode to do a specific risky task. dcode shows the exact action\nin an `ask_user` prompt. You answer **\"yes\"**. dcode then proposes the\nexact `git push --force origin feature-x` call.\n\nBefore this change, Auto denied the call. The classifier saw only the\nanswer text (\"yes\"), which does not name an action or a target. You had\nto type the full command again to approve your own approval.\n\n### The fix: attach the \"yes\" to the paired question\n\nConsent has two parts: an action and a target. A bare \"yes\" has no\ntarget, so it must not approve anything on its own.\n\nThe fix pairs each server-validated answer with the exact question that\ndcode showed in the same `ask_user` call. The pairing is safe for three\nreasons specific to `ask_user`:\n\n1. The question text comes from the tool call arguments that the client\nalready validated against the receipt. It is not model prose from the\nassistant's chat message.\n2. The receipt confirms the answer count matches the question count for\nthat exact `tool_call_id`, so dcode aligns each question to its answer\nby index.\n3. Only one `ask_user` call in this turn can hold that `tool_call_id`,\nso the mapping is unambiguous.\n\nAuto trusts the question only as the action-and-target description that\nits own paired answer attaches to. The question alone approves nothing.\nThe answer alone approves nothing. Only the pair, matched to a tool call\nby canonical arguments, approves the call.\n\nThe invariant stays the same:\n\n> short affirmative **+ paired question that names action+target** ≥\nexplicit action+target for those exact calls. A short affirmative\n**alone** is not consent.\n\n### Scope of the binding\n\nAuto approves a call only when all of these are true:\n\n- The paired question names the action and the material target.\n- The answer is a short affirmative, for example: \"yes\", \"y\",\n\"approved\", \"go ahead\", \"lgtm\", \"do it\".\n- The tool call's canonical arguments match the action and target that\nthe question names.\n\nThe approval does not extend to a different target, a more destructive\nvariant (for example a force-push when the question asked about an\nordinary push), or extra tools in the same batch that the question did\nnot cover.\n\nAuto also handles polarity. If the question asks you to skip, avoid, or\nkeep rather than delete, an affirmative agrees with that negation. Auto\ndoes not invert the polarity to approve the destructive action.\n\n### How the change works\n\n`_same_turn_user_answers` now reads the `questions` list from the\nsame-turn `ask_user` arguments and emits a `question` field next to each\n`answer`. If the list is missing, malformed, or a different length than\nthe answers, the function returns no rows and the classifier falls back\nto the prior \"answer alone grants nothing\" behavior.\n\n`_CLASSIFIER_POLICY` is rewritten to describe the attachment model, the\ncanonical-argument match, the polarity rule, and the scope limits above.\n\nNo change to the `ask_user` receipt or schema, no cross-turn state, no\napproval-UI or public-API change. The new `question` field is internal\nand applies only to the current turn.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/6b48ff9d-e08c-711e-d526-9ccf88069d3b)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/6b48ff9d-e08c-711e-d526-9ccf88069d3b/plan\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T03:56:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f4f138db65484d4938ef3759cb26cec1e789357d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f4f138db65484d4938ef3759cb26cec1e789357d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f4f138db65484d4938ef3759cb26cec1e789357d/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"107980e387b3fa060c2b33e9bd31b57c387eddb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/107980e387b3fa060c2b33e9bd31b57c387eddb6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/107980e387b3fa060c2b33e9bd31b57c387eddb6"}]},{"sha":"107980e387b3fa060c2b33e9bd31b57c387eddb6","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDEwNzk4MGUzODdiM2ZhMDYwYzJiMzNlOWJkMzFiNTdjMzg3ZWRkYjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T03:49:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T03:49:55Z"},"message":"feat(code): trust user-declared endpoints for cold-cache policies (#5462)\n\nDepends on #5439\n\n[Docs](https://github.com/langchain-ai/docs/pull/5524)\n\nSome users don't talk to model providers directly — they go through a\ngateway or corporate proxy (for example, LangSmith's gateway, or a\ncompany-internal relay). The cold-cache warning from #5439 stays silent\nfor all of them, because it only trusts the provider's official API\naddress. This PR adds a setting to say \"my endpoint plays by the\nprovider's rules,\" turning the warnings back on:\n\n```toml\n[warnings]\ntrusted_cache_endpoints = [\"smith.langchain.com\"]\n```\n\nOne entry covers every provider routed through that endpoint — no need\nto repeat it per provider.\n\n---\n\n**Why trust is per-endpoint, not global.** The warning's dollar\nestimates are only accurate if the thing sitting between you and the\nprovider passes your cache settings through untouched and keeps cached\ndata for as long as the provider documents. A proxy that quietly drops\nthose settings would make the warning's numbers fiction. So instead of\none blanket \"trust everything\" switch, you name the specific endpoints\nyou've verified, and everything else stays silent.\n\n**One case stays silent even on a trusted endpoint.** LangSmith's\ngateway can translate between API formats — for example, you can send an\nOpenAI-shaped request and have it answered by an Anthropic model. During\nthat translation, your cache settings get rewritten to a generic\n5-minute cache (or dropped entirely), so the provider's documented cache\nbehavior no longer applies and any estimate would be a guess. When dcode\ncan see a request will take one of these translated routes (the model\nname carries a cross-provider prefix like\n`openai:anthropic/claude-...`), it skips the warning rather than show\nnumbers built on wrong assumptions. Requests that stay in their own\nformat — the normal case — are forwarded by the gateway byte-for-byte\n(verified against the gateway source), so their warnings remain exactly\nas accurate as going direct.\n\n<details><summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Unit tests cover trusted-endpoint policy resolution, gateway\nsame-format vs cross-format routes, lookalike-host rejection\n(`notsmith.langchain.com`, `smith.langchain.com.evil.example`), and\nmalformed config tolerance.\n- App-level tests confirm a trusted gateway endpoint allows the warning\nthrough, and a cross-format gateway route suppresses it even when\ntrusted.\n- Lint, type check, and the cold-cache/manifest suites pass.\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"c116f719c1c056a2022179ccc8f127c88ca95ae0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c116f719c1c056a2022179ccc8f127c88ca95ae0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/107980e387b3fa060c2b33e9bd31b57c387eddb6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg9ZjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAnTwQADxBp3KViTnhgyvZWisLuq2B\nKA57dQRqbHfT4rKYKmnsBA6EXRQFAvNv0wv+/4GZWLllA4yuaPPwW1oROtTBNaKZ\nu5vnBCV9cTs4bZnx9gdhpMGmkF/0xfUxAfVwNdWnrY1riQfUdVqHPIjpIgoSnxUq\nFvZM/Xsqh+grcljRKjDuOKsLdzzcfo34wTz7f4zJmomHeP878tHZuNapvLeFNkyG\n3KbAKm6lOOZ5fR/SV4mpJSlfnMMW0hbqyVvjoCV3CPqzNQcGgYe9aFKA+pYWoK0i\n0az1UbQUfQqThke8zoUt20oe6HwpPlOk0nzGL67uJYpZ3EmF1H+X9g200J3AI/lu\ndh6Cjc22W3Bc0ZY4y9Ee/+GRsfOUCxDR9eyQtZaFHmMn0+rvnY6WpjP5oZlqqxsK\nwbvGuQt4J1sxsEEe57djf8K+fhWcRwEBQTIBzhtPdZ6oGE4mu6hHNSgu/lsPWEkQ\nA4po+gcYSdyAm+bPb7r1y6s0GQ0NJztY4rnl9GcAKgQn/TcqK8aFopBDd1dHt2jL\nWVMj2KxvF/2/cUtMy8SgmnNRBmTPSdrGZiR7iU0Twb+8Hqe4u9U4myybCxnb5DeD\nSOr0k2VPk6qQEgthv43EFTNSKCCibKvQfg/Yhack2jGdcIz+a4V/ednLgI3J++8c\nGowDeLypbaCoig1xRjDf\n=wVI/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c116f719c1c056a2022179ccc8f127c88ca95ae0\nparent 5d806c88cf2a8b10d9b13b832540151491c13e19\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787024995 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787024995 -0400\n\nfeat(code): trust user-declared endpoints for cold-cache policies (#5462)\n\nDepends on #5439\n\n[Docs](https://github.com/langchain-ai/docs/pull/5524)\n\nSome users don't talk to model providers directly — they go through a\ngateway or corporate proxy (for example, LangSmith's gateway, or a\ncompany-internal relay). The cold-cache warning from #5439 stays silent\nfor all of them, because it only trusts the provider's official API\naddress. This PR adds a setting to say \"my endpoint plays by the\nprovider's rules,\" turning the warnings back on:\n\n```toml\n[warnings]\ntrusted_cache_endpoints = [\"smith.langchain.com\"]\n```\n\nOne entry covers every provider routed through that endpoint — no need\nto repeat it per provider.\n\n---\n\n**Why trust is per-endpoint, not global.** The warning's dollar\nestimates are only accurate if the thing sitting between you and the\nprovider passes your cache settings through untouched and keeps cached\ndata for as long as the provider documents. A proxy that quietly drops\nthose settings would make the warning's numbers fiction. So instead of\none blanket \"trust everything\" switch, you name the specific endpoints\nyou've verified, and everything else stays silent.\n\n**One case stays silent even on a trusted endpoint.** LangSmith's\ngateway can translate between API formats — for example, you can send an\nOpenAI-shaped request and have it answered by an Anthropic model. During\nthat translation, your cache settings get rewritten to a generic\n5-minute cache (or dropped entirely), so the provider's documented cache\nbehavior no longer applies and any estimate would be a guess. When dcode\ncan see a request will take one of these translated routes (the model\nname carries a cross-provider prefix like\n`openai:anthropic/claude-...`), it skips the warning rather than show\nnumbers built on wrong assumptions. Requests that stay in their own\nformat — the normal case — are forwarded by the gateway byte-for-byte\n(verified against the gateway source), so their warnings remain exactly\nas accurate as going direct.\n\n<details><summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Unit tests cover trusted-endpoint policy resolution, gateway\nsame-format vs cross-format routes, lookalike-host rejection\n(`notsmith.langchain.com`, `smith.langchain.com.evil.example`), and\nmalformed config tolerance.\n- App-level tests confirm a trusted gateway endpoint allows the warning\nthrough, and a cross-format gateway route suppresses it even when\ntrusted.\n- Lint, type check, and the cold-cache/manifest suites pass.\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T03:49:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/107980e387b3fa060c2b33e9bd31b57c387eddb6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/107980e387b3fa060c2b33e9bd31b57c387eddb6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/107980e387b3fa060c2b33e9bd31b57c387eddb6/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5d806c88cf2a8b10d9b13b832540151491c13e19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5d806c88cf2a8b10d9b13b832540151491c13e19","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5d806c88cf2a8b10d9b13b832540151491c13e19"}]},{"sha":"5d806c88cf2a8b10d9b13b832540151491c13e19","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDVkODA2Yzg4Y2YyYThiMTBkOWIxM2I4MzI1NDAxNTE0OTFjMTNlMTk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T03:49:11Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T03:49:11Z"},"message":"fix(code): report total context after `/offload` (#5488)\n\n`/offload` now reports the change in total context (system prompt, tool\nschemas, and conversation) instead of passing off a conversation-only\nestimate as \"Context\".\n\n---\n\nThe previous report computed both sides of the before/after with\n`count_tokens_approximately` over conversation messages only, then\nlabeled the result `Context:`. For a coding agent the fixed overhead\n(system prompt plus tool schema) is the dominant term, so the reported\ntotals and the percentage reduction were both misleading — an offload\nthat freed mostly conversation looked like it had freed the whole\nwindow.\n\n- When a provider-reported total is persisted from the last ordinary\nturn, the report subtracts only the conversation *delta* from it,\nkeeping both figures on the provider's scale. The before figure prints\nexact; the after figure carries a `~` because the delta is estimated.\n- Subtracting the delta (rather than rebuilding the total as `overhead +\nconversation_after`) matters: the local estimator need only overshoot\nthe provider count by a token for an `overhead = max(0, reported -\nconversation_before)` clamp to collapse the overhead to zero, which\nwould silently report the entire system prompt and tool schema as freed\ncontext.\n- With no usable provider total (never set, or a stale checkpoint\nvalue), the report falls back to the conversation-only estimate and\nlabels it `Conversation:` so the two metrics are not mistaken for one\nanother — percentages are not comparable across the two labels.\n- The percentage is floored at zero: a summary can come out larger than\nthe messages it replaced, and a negative \"decrease\" should never render.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"429a74a8efe053ba3d607fabc94a86965ae171b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/429a74a8efe053ba3d607fabc94a86965ae171b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5d806c88cf2a8b10d9b13b832540151491c13e19","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg9Y3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzSAQAHvpMm332/eUc3wUGNMQ5LHN\n7JChRv63pkRTo69c0pKCI4CNRpIJ2D+gFpToLdmnGND2nFmDyLloQDAdJG8psYqn\n0Azk9mn8PwejGvjNlm7azmJadU50sUBvfp1hooWoyWMgVnHMrvyekcZLX7R3BrdQ\n/r112W6utMPH/f+L/TJWOBq47K6H0ZjaNciKRLLBKahZJwf6Qvok7xOGdFhQvN1c\nGFS5batdUk13JuPoBUUKPOya3Bjdaaagup8ZZlBa9/99VGGdlAKecdiJ8LVqT5MM\nG3vQa6T+5uQvDhqOI95RnLBqisfxaidqQWWdiowsmOQLnSNcjNTnHNEBoNJG6QXJ\nM68Ham9EaBNRiQXphbdUSBUiZUXOUqfCOUdhKan7+y5Mop+bS4Pw/ORrQqtBMQHO\nERiNen4CIsjqV+a8zbo3bFUYrOSNw7ylrNvK+UcPVdmjrhaSAKOc5XOc88uFJvuI\n/bTtONuWH90lt3vHbp9V/lYIs2uQFlQ6zO7z5OAJTV5Fim+B+spE1JERBqFn460v\n9Qth+LbgrzG9EpMylush0sVmSE52KV7lHzuyAzr5mw2qjY+SwPvHJhUcIyv8sww7\nqKpAkrrZX8s2EU5DEtLTfJLd5yDYAcR5/HdWBUaaB6Du2lcARL2mUselO15PV7lh\nI/mSbVfAPFQ9Mm4Qc+rj\n=9KA1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 429a74a8efe053ba3d607fabc94a86965ae171b6\nparent 8d2298ff54797e224233349e4baf68e19b110040\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787024951 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787024951 -0400\n\nfix(code): report total context after `/offload` (#5488)\n\n`/offload` now reports the change in total context (system prompt, tool\nschemas, and conversation) instead of passing off a conversation-only\nestimate as \"Context\".\n\n---\n\nThe previous report computed both sides of the before/after with\n`count_tokens_approximately` over conversation messages only, then\nlabeled the result `Context:`. For a coding agent the fixed overhead\n(system prompt plus tool schema) is the dominant term, so the reported\ntotals and the percentage reduction were both misleading — an offload\nthat freed mostly conversation looked like it had freed the whole\nwindow.\n\n- When a provider-reported total is persisted from the last ordinary\nturn, the report subtracts only the conversation *delta* from it,\nkeeping both figures on the provider's scale. The before figure prints\nexact; the after figure carries a `~` because the delta is estimated.\n- Subtracting the delta (rather than rebuilding the total as `overhead +\nconversation_after`) matters: the local estimator need only overshoot\nthe provider count by a token for an `overhead = max(0, reported -\nconversation_before)` clamp to collapse the overhead to zero, which\nwould silently report the entire system prompt and tool schema as freed\ncontext.\n- With no usable provider total (never set, or a stale checkpoint\nvalue), the report falls back to the conversation-only estimate and\nlabels it `Conversation:` so the two metrics are not mistaken for one\nanother — percentages are not comparable across the two labels.\n- The percentage is floored at zero: a summary can come out larger than\nthe messages it replaced, and a negative \"decrease\" should never render.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T03:49:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5d806c88cf2a8b10d9b13b832540151491c13e19","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5d806c88cf2a8b10d9b13b832540151491c13e19","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5d806c88cf2a8b10d9b13b832540151491c13e19/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8d2298ff54797e224233349e4baf68e19b110040","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8d2298ff54797e224233349e4baf68e19b110040","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8d2298ff54797e224233349e4baf68e19b110040"}]},{"sha":"8d2298ff54797e224233349e4baf68e19b110040","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhkMjI5OGZmNTQ3OTdlMjI0MjMzMzQ5ZTRiYWY2OGUxOWIxMTAwNDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T03:41:47Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T03:41:47Z"},"message":"feat(code): warn before expensive cold-cache turns (#5439)\n\n[Docs](https://github.com/langchain-ai/docs/pull/5524)\n\nWhen an interactive chat message reaches the front of the queue, dcode\nnow warns before sending it to the model if its prompt cache may need\nre-warming, showing the estimated cold-input cost and warm-cache delta.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[\"Queued message reaches front of queue\"] --> B{\"Qualifying message?\"}\n    B -- \"No (e.g. using a slash command, ACP mode)\" --> S[\"Send the message\"]\n    B -- \"Yes - sent inside the interactive TUI and not a slash command\" --> C[\"Load checkpointed last request time + model identity\"]\n    C -- \"Missing or malformed:\\nlog a warning and treat as cold (see Fig. 1 for specifics)\" --> D\n    C -- \"Loaded\" --> D{\"Known cache policy for current model + endpoint?\"}\n    D -- \"No (e.g. custom endpoint or other provider)\" --> S\n    D -- Yes --> E{\"Idle past window, age unknown, or cache-affecting params changed?\"}\n    E -- \"No: within window\" --> S\n    E -- Yes --> E2{\"Context ≥ minimum cacheable tokens?\"}\n    E2 -- \"No: tiny context\" --> S\n    E2 -- Yes --> F{\"Re-warm price delta ≥ threshold?\"}\n    F -- \"No: below threshold or unpriceable\" --> S\n    F -- Yes --> M[\"Show blocking warning modal\"]\n    M -- \"Keep draft (Esc)\" --> R[\"Restore draft to chat input\"]\n    M -- \"Cannot be shown (render failure, or another prompt owns the modal slot)\" --> R\n    M -- \"Send anyway\" --> S\n    M -- \"Send + don't warn again this session\" --> SS[\"Mute until restart (in memory)\"] --> S\n    M -- \"Send + don't warn again ever\" --> SP[\"Persist to warnings.suppress in config.toml\"] --> S\n```\n\n<details><summary><b>Fig. 1</b> — the \"treat as cold\" fallback</summary>\n\nThe main flow compares the *checkpointed* identity (what last warmed the\ncache) against the *current* model (what's about to run). Policy and\ncost always come from the current model, which is known from live config\n— so a missing checkpointed identity doesn't need its own policy; it\njust forces the comparison to \"changed\":\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph P[\"Checkpointed identity (written by middleware after each completed model call)\"]\n        P1 -- \"Request time bad, absent, or in the future\" --> P2[\"Log, discard time:\\nthe age is unknown, not zero\"]\n        P1 -- \"Model spec bad\" --> P3[\"Log warning, discard spec\"]\n    end\n    subgraph Q[\"Current identity (from live config)\"]\n        Q1[\"Effective model spec\\n(always resolvable)\"] --> Q2[\"Resolve policy + price against this model\"]\n    end\n    P2 -- \"No age to compare against a window\" --> OUT2[\"Continue down the cold-cache path:\\nreason = age_unknown\"]\n    P3 -- \"Discarded spec reads as the model having changed in last vs. current\" --> OUT[\"Continue down the cold-cache path:\\nidentity_changed = true\"]\n    Q2 --> OUT\n    Q2 --> OUT2\n```\n\nThe three causes are kept distinct because each gets its own modal copy,\nand reporting one as another states something untrue about the user's\nconfiguration. In particular an unknown age is never reported as a model\nchange, which would claim a change that never happened.\n\n</details>\n\nThe retention windows come from documented provider policies:\n\n| Provider | Condition | Retention window | Warning wording |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Anthropic | any | 5m | \"expired\" |\n| OpenAI | `prompt_cache_retention: in_memory` | 1h | \"expired\" |\n| OpenAI | `prompt_cache_retention: 24h` | 24h | \"expired\" |\n| OpenAI | GPT-5.6 or newer, no explicit retention | 30m minimum | \"may\nbe cold\" (provider may retain longer) |\n\nThe window is either a documented **maximum** or a documented\n**minimum**, and the wording follows from which. Anthropic's TTL and\nOpenAI's `prompt_cache_retention` ceilings are maximums, so once the\nwindow passes the entry is gone (\"expired\"). GPT-5.6+'s 30 minutes is a\nguaranteed minimum that the provider may exceed, so past it the cache\ncan only be called \"may be cold\".\n\nThe two OpenAI knobs are independent, which is why the table is ordered\nas it is: `prompt_cache_retention` states a maximum lifetime while the\nGPT-5.6+ guarantee states a minimum one, so an explicitly configured\nretention is the later and firmer bound and takes precedence on those\nmodels too. Warning a user who asked for `24h` at the 30-minute mark\nwould contradict their own configuration.\n\nAnthropic is always 5m regardless of a configured `cache_control.ttl`.\n`AnthropicPromptCachingMiddleware` runs inside\n`ConfigurableModelMiddleware` and rewrites\n`model_settings[\"cache_control\"]` with its own TTL (5m, which this stack\nnever overrides), so a user-supplied `1h` never reaches the API.\nTreating it as an hour would suppress the warning for 55 minutes of a\ncache that died at five.\n\nThe warning combines three sources of information:\n\n1. **Provider retention policies** (from the table above) — how long\neach provider keeps cache entries\n2. **Checkpointed timing** — when you last sent a request to this model\n3. **Pricing overrides** — your configured cost per token\n\nIf the estimated re-warm cost reaches your threshold, a modal appears\nbefore sending with four keyboard-driven choices. Cost is estimated by\npricing two synthetic usage payloads — one billed as a full cache read,\none as a cold request — through the ordinary cost-tracking path, so the\npricing catalog stays the single source of truth. Both figures are upper\nbounds and are rounded upward so the displayed estimate never reads\nlower than the modelled spend.\n\nHow a miss is priced follows the model: Anthropic carries a write\npremium over plain input, GPT-5.6+ bills a miss as a cache write, and\nOpenAI before 5.6 charges no write surcharge at all, so those misses\nprice at the plain input rate. Tagging a pre-5.6 miss as a write would\napply a premium the provider never charges and overstate both the\ndisplayed cost and the threshold comparison.\n\n<img width=\"614\" height=\"357\" alt=\"Screenshot\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4bdb5ef4-8ee4-47ed-b624-c87ac4a71722\"\n/>\n\nThe model identity check looks at the model name plus the invocation\nparameters that actually select or invalidate a cache entry —\n`prompt_cache_retention`, `prompt_cache_key`, `prompt_cache_options`,\nand `cache_control`. A change to any of them invalidates the prefix, so\nit warns regardless of how recent the last turn was. Unrelated knobs are\ndeliberately excluded: `/effort` rewrites `reasoning_effort` wholesale,\nand `temperature` or `max_tokens` are just as inert for caching, so\ncomparing whole parameter maps would open the modal asserting that the\ncached prefix \"cannot be reused\" when nothing about the prefix moved.\n\nAnything that prevents the confirmation from being shown keeps the draft\nrather than sending: if the modal fails to render, or another prompt\nalready owns the modal slot, the message is not dispatched and the text\nis restored to the chat input. A warning that cannot be presented must\nnot become an implicit authorization to spend. Where a draft genuinely\ncannot be put back — the input already holds different text, or the\nactive thread changed while the modal was open — the notification says\nthe message was not sent and points at history recall rather than\nimplying it was merely deferred.\n\nOnly interactive chat submissions are checked — prompts sent\nprogrammatically (e.g. via ACP from an editor client), slash commands,\nrequests to custom endpoints, and requests without pricing information\nall skip this warning entirely. The default threshold is $0.50; adjust\nit with `warnings.cold_cache_min_delta_usd`.\n\nThe request time is kept fresh from two directions. A completed turn\nreads it back from the checkpoint; a turn that reached the model but\nended without a readable checkpoint — an interrupt, say — stamps it\nlocally instead. Without that second path the field would never advance\npast its initial value, and every send after the first would open the\nmodal reporting no record of a turn that plainly happened.\n\nIf the checkpointed request time or model identity cannot be loaded (for\nexample, a checkpoint written by a newer version, or a malformed value),\ndcode logs a warning naming the affected channel and proceeds down the\ncold-cache path rather than silently assuming the cache is warm: an\nunusable request time makes the age unknown, and a missing model\nidentity is treated as a model change. A request time in the future — a\ncorrected clock, or a thread synced from a skewed machine — is treated\nas unknown age too, since clamping it to zero would place it inside\nevery retention window and suppress the warning outright.\n\nSkipping the warning means sending at full cold-cache price, so the\npaths that skip it on failure are made visible rather than left to the\nlog alone: if the evaluation itself fails, the session says once that\ncost checks are unavailable; an unparseable configured `base_url` warns\nwhere it is parsed, since it silently disables warnings for that\nprovider; and a pricing catalog that produces a non-finite figure is\nreported as a data defect rather than reading as \"no price published\". A\nfailed persistent suppression names its cause — a malformed `[warnings]`\ntable needs one line of TOML, not the `chmod` that a generic \"check file\npermissions\" would send the user to.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f30f3674-c02d-e6cd-6bf2-89df728709cb)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f30f3674-c02d-e6cd-6bf2-89df728709cb/plan\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"bd0b3cbd437475ccc4a184f92257505ce1f3af21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/bd0b3cbd437475ccc4a184f92257505ce1f3af21"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8d2298ff54797e224233349e4baf68e19b110040","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg9R7CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAfF4QALIw/snDE+t+hj9pMwOFHgQZ\nd4UsJtptiNTon2XGkVbpYiRoUTxlU8riBOCHeMve8FVU+EQU69ZrkAuTTbdeujdB\nlAIllPBmvtCPd546zqpqLdMlgXYMbx/OePfHh8mAQOFClN4h9le8pAVWSfx5+Ef2\nVOK9oPnrQm4RecW3NtLmMfVascYb12PJAUCtxBMnPiNbU7Np+0NBj80KngFOkanL\n6y414tvVCXuOco0RdcgqsTQ3Qar7emhHtqMwRKVvQPACNUwhhLk7xeXZOkiU2H3O\njSPrtxVe9ATpRqZhRWqtlpwWDMcFqMvcQbSEWOOrOd73w0Fehz8NtM3CMfvA0OdK\n+VtW4f0ObG8lsY9QVtg6dVKl0GbJ+07f0sxzXunXCAihEtIXRgVo/8OVpVAl1cEC\nqYx1JZhbqeYKpVpEmCyC13Avzk6mc3Giox4nk2NOphw75HOJHwbojpXlvH8rRu2B\nR3Y9YotN9zeh1bL49L2RCOYhlK/TpIsXbm0qvE19D3U2kKVsHDNVyOqy5ddHORgu\nqKh0xOpRZID+9iVcIAnMRg8jbZLLez5slCZhE2VqxaaG4UNGSkB0PwfC4hqqx0b+\nLXFK7pFWI2eDkXqaxrPXHRjxCo/dRjNs7BYtBt4UEybGwrpgFPDZJUGSQFbjd/B1\n3Q6oWM6UQXV834MgHUvQ\n=lNkv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bd0b3cbd437475ccc4a184f92257505ce1f3af21\nparent 3dd4fe5cdc548f5408d5b74b82084d9d4c01a664\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787024507 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787024507 -0400\n\nfeat(code): warn before expensive cold-cache turns (#5439)\n\n[Docs](https://github.com/langchain-ai/docs/pull/5524)\n\nWhen an interactive chat message reaches the front of the queue, dcode\nnow warns before sending it to the model if its prompt cache may need\nre-warming, showing the estimated cold-input cost and warm-cache delta.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[\"Queued message reaches front of queue\"] --> B{\"Qualifying message?\"}\n    B -- \"No (e.g. using a slash command, ACP mode)\" --> S[\"Send the message\"]\n    B -- \"Yes - sent inside the interactive TUI and not a slash command\" --> C[\"Load checkpointed last request time + model identity\"]\n    C -- \"Missing or malformed:\\nlog a warning and treat as cold (see Fig. 1 for specifics)\" --> D\n    C -- \"Loaded\" --> D{\"Known cache policy for current model + endpoint?\"}\n    D -- \"No (e.g. custom endpoint or other provider)\" --> S\n    D -- Yes --> E{\"Idle past window, age unknown, or cache-affecting params changed?\"}\n    E -- \"No: within window\" --> S\n    E -- Yes --> E2{\"Context ≥ minimum cacheable tokens?\"}\n    E2 -- \"No: tiny context\" --> S\n    E2 -- Yes --> F{\"Re-warm price delta ≥ threshold?\"}\n    F -- \"No: below threshold or unpriceable\" --> S\n    F -- Yes --> M[\"Show blocking warning modal\"]\n    M -- \"Keep draft (Esc)\" --> R[\"Restore draft to chat input\"]\n    M -- \"Cannot be shown (render failure, or another prompt owns the modal slot)\" --> R\n    M -- \"Send anyway\" --> S\n    M -- \"Send + don't warn again this session\" --> SS[\"Mute until restart (in memory)\"] --> S\n    M -- \"Send + don't warn again ever\" --> SP[\"Persist to warnings.suppress in config.toml\"] --> S\n```\n\n<details><summary><b>Fig. 1</b> — the \"treat as cold\" fallback</summary>\n\nThe main flow compares the *checkpointed* identity (what last warmed the\ncache) against the *current* model (what's about to run). Policy and\ncost always come from the current model, which is known from live config\n— so a missing checkpointed identity doesn't need its own policy; it\njust forces the comparison to \"changed\":\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph P[\"Checkpointed identity (written by middleware after each completed model call)\"]\n        P1 -- \"Request time bad, absent, or in the future\" --> P2[\"Log, discard time:\\nthe age is unknown, not zero\"]\n        P1 -- \"Model spec bad\" --> P3[\"Log warning, discard spec\"]\n    end\n    subgraph Q[\"Current identity (from live config)\"]\n        Q1[\"Effective model spec\\n(always resolvable)\"] --> Q2[\"Resolve policy + price against this model\"]\n    end\n    P2 -- \"No age to compare against a window\" --> OUT2[\"Continue down the cold-cache path:\\nreason = age_unknown\"]\n    P3 -- \"Discarded spec reads as the model having changed in last vs. current\" --> OUT[\"Continue down the cold-cache path:\\nidentity_changed = true\"]\n    Q2 --> OUT\n    Q2 --> OUT2\n```\n\nThe three causes are kept distinct because each gets its own modal copy,\nand reporting one as another states something untrue about the user's\nconfiguration. In particular an unknown age is never reported as a model\nchange, which would claim a change that never happened.\n\n</details>\n\nThe retention windows come from documented provider policies:\n\n| Provider | Condition | Retention window | Warning wording |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Anthropic | any | 5m | \"expired\" |\n| OpenAI | `prompt_cache_retention: in_memory` | 1h | \"expired\" |\n| OpenAI | `prompt_cache_retention: 24h` | 24h | \"expired\" |\n| OpenAI | GPT-5.6 or newer, no explicit retention | 30m minimum | \"may\nbe cold\" (provider may retain longer) |\n\nThe window is either a documented **maximum** or a documented\n**minimum**, and the wording follows from which. Anthropic's TTL and\nOpenAI's `prompt_cache_retention` ceilings are maximums, so once the\nwindow passes the entry is gone (\"expired\"). GPT-5.6+'s 30 minutes is a\nguaranteed minimum that the provider may exceed, so past it the cache\ncan only be called \"may be cold\".\n\nThe two OpenAI knobs are independent, which is why the table is ordered\nas it is: `prompt_cache_retention` states a maximum lifetime while the\nGPT-5.6+ guarantee states a minimum one, so an explicitly configured\nretention is the later and firmer bound and takes precedence on those\nmodels too. Warning a user who asked for `24h` at the 30-minute mark\nwould contradict their own configuration.\n\nAnthropic is always 5m regardless of a configured `cache_control.ttl`.\n`AnthropicPromptCachingMiddleware` runs inside\n`ConfigurableModelMiddleware` and rewrites\n`model_settings[\"cache_control\"]` with its own TTL (5m, which this stack\nnever overrides), so a user-supplied `1h` never reaches the API.\nTreating it as an hour would suppress the warning for 55 minutes of a\ncache that died at five.\n\nThe warning combines three sources of information:\n\n1. **Provider retention policies** (from the table above) — how long\neach provider keeps cache entries\n2. **Checkpointed timing** — when you last sent a request to this model\n3. **Pricing overrides** — your configured cost per token\n\nIf the estimated re-warm cost reaches your threshold, a modal appears\nbefore sending with four keyboard-driven choices. Cost is estimated by\npricing two synthetic usage payloads — one billed as a full cache read,\none as a cold request — through the ordinary cost-tracking path, so the\npricing catalog stays the single source of truth. Both figures are upper\nbounds and are rounded upward so the displayed estimate never reads\nlower than the modelled spend.\n\nHow a miss is priced follows the model: Anthropic carries a write\npremium over plain input, GPT-5.6+ bills a miss as a cache write, and\nOpenAI before 5.6 charges no write surcharge at all, so those misses\nprice at the plain input rate. Tagging a pre-5.6 miss as a write would\napply a premium the provider never charges and overstate both the\ndisplayed cost and the threshold comparison.\n\n<img width=\"614\" height=\"357\" alt=\"Screenshot\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4bdb5ef4-8ee4-47ed-b624-c87ac4a71722\"\n/>\n\nThe model identity check looks at the model name plus the invocation\nparameters that actually select or invalidate a cache entry —\n`prompt_cache_retention`, `prompt_cache_key`, `prompt_cache_options`,\nand `cache_control`. A change to any of them invalidates the prefix, so\nit warns regardless of how recent the last turn was. Unrelated knobs are\ndeliberately excluded: `/effort` rewrites `reasoning_effort` wholesale,\nand `temperature` or `max_tokens` are just as inert for caching, so\ncomparing whole parameter maps would open the modal asserting that the\ncached prefix \"cannot be reused\" when nothing about the prefix moved.\n\nAnything that prevents the confirmation from being shown keeps the draft\nrather than sending: if the modal fails to render, or another prompt\nalready owns the modal slot, the message is not dispatched and the text\nis restored to the chat input. A warning that cannot be presented must\nnot become an implicit authorization to spend. Where a draft genuinely\ncannot be put back — the input already holds different text, or the\nactive thread changed while the modal was open — the notification says\nthe message was not sent and points at history recall rather than\nimplying it was merely deferred.\n\nOnly interactive chat submissions are checked — prompts sent\nprogrammatically (e.g. via ACP from an editor client), slash commands,\nrequests to custom endpoints, and requests without pricing information\nall skip this warning entirely. The default threshold is $0.50; adjust\nit with `warnings.cold_cache_min_delta_usd`.\n\nThe request time is kept fresh from two directions. A completed turn\nreads it back from the checkpoint; a turn that reached the model but\nended without a readable checkpoint — an interrupt, say — stamps it\nlocally instead. Without that second path the field would never advance\npast its initial value, and every send after the first would open the\nmodal reporting no record of a turn that plainly happened.\n\nIf the checkpointed request time or model identity cannot be loaded (for\nexample, a checkpoint written by a newer version, or a malformed value),\ndcode logs a warning naming the affected channel and proceeds down the\ncold-cache path rather than silently assuming the cache is warm: an\nunusable request time makes the age unknown, and a missing model\nidentity is treated as a model change. A request time in the future — a\ncorrected clock, or a thread synced from a skewed machine — is treated\nas unknown age too, since clamping it to zero would place it inside\nevery retention window and suppress the warning outright.\n\nSkipping the warning means sending at full cold-cache price, so the\npaths that skip it on failure are made visible rather than left to the\nlog alone: if the evaluation itself fails, the session says once that\ncost checks are unavailable; an unparseable configured `base_url` warns\nwhere it is parsed, since it silently disables warnings for that\nprovider; and a pricing catalog that produces a non-finite figure is\nreported as a data defect rather than reading as \"no price published\". A\nfailed persistent suppression names its cause — a malformed `[warnings]`\ntable needs one line of TOML, not the `chmod` that a generic \"check file\npermissions\" would send the user to.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f30f3674-c02d-e6cd-6bf2-89df728709cb)\n\n## References\n- Plan:\nhttps://openswe.vercel.app/agents/f30f3674-c02d-e6cd-6bf2-89df728709cb/plan\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T03:41:48Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8d2298ff54797e224233349e4baf68e19b110040","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8d2298ff54797e224233349e4baf68e19b110040","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8d2298ff54797e224233349e4baf68e19b110040/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3dd4fe5cdc548f5408d5b74b82084d9d4c01a664","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3dd4fe5cdc548f5408d5b74b82084d9d4c01a664","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3dd4fe5cdc548f5408d5b74b82084d9d4c01a664"}]},{"sha":"3dd4fe5cdc548f5408d5b74b82084d9d4c01a664","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDNkZDRmZTVjZGM1NDhmNTQwOGQ1Yjc0YjgyMDg0ZDlkNGMwMWE2NjQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T03:17:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T03:17:41Z"},"message":"feat(code): show conversation turns alongside message counts (#5571)\n\n`/offload` feedback and the Debug Console now show conversation turns\ntogether with raw message counts.\n\n---\n\nMessage counts are hard to interpret. One user prompt can become several\nprovider messages (a tool call, a tool result, and a follow-up model\nturn), and the count changes from provider to provider. Conversation\nturns — the user prompts the model actually saw — do not change between\nproviders. This makes them a better unit for comparing offloads.\n\nChanges:\n\n- The offload report now shows both units, for example `Offloaded 4\nolder messages (2 conversation turns)` and `6 messages (3 conversation\nturns) kept`. The turn count excludes internal human messages\n(goal-state notices and `[SYSTEM]` interruptions) that collect below the\ncutoff.\n- The Debug Console `Messages` field shows `N messages (M rendered), K\nturns`, with correct singular and plural labels.\n- The new `MessageStore.turn_count` property counts `USER` and `SKILL`\nrows. A `/skill` invocation creates one `SKILL` row instead of a `USER`\nrow, so each skill use counts as one turn. It counts all rendered rows,\nincluding local-only flows such as `!shell` and most slash commands.\nThat is a broader set than the offload report's turn count, which comes\nfrom graph state; the property's docstring describes the difference.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"ef340f45297b48100e6bc525523f09a09b5a3154","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/ef340f45297b48100e6bc525523f09a09b5a3154"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/3dd4fe5cdc548f5408d5b74b82084d9d4c01a664","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg87VCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALPwQAKUITRsm5JlicYHl4BAUSOhV\nUTTIuWTY4DoMvC72gMAHc+xVevJ1GFVHtOZlRDnVTrU7pduJK5Vrove5ltSl3V4z\nWw0JXxc5ghGk48yu5cnwfrS4Z4YnVXF2jkGKaSYC8n0xHnmQqw8DGfOqtDivnS8t\n7yGGnz/0Vw24fBDRF5hHAFmX67kP2eGWi33OwfrOUcrefW4e1I+75q5v4S+E29bn\nVjS1kmfBQzp6oT9duVKu0sbw+7VMdjh34WFrV6qn5AsRTuS4T6LYpYSeruA0Hr8T\npueScPo1U5DKAWWmvEdJppMFjQvrKQ5846TRRUmILlaWn4dfiIywheFi+/hUYV2Y\nv5rLkPilJJbGww8fuqc/U4dNO222d4EN70nx+8IN4iea2DVKze0Yn36Bi7SdF0OT\nX9XEBU1kX1UfNpqFEtLVtyzsGNajlsu5himIJrg3bUIgcti5W4lPGfNiSlmtpBnL\nqQkueAD2I1pfv/PHA+QpAMV9xMWMB6Yv5bTyF/E9Q/uaKrLslmjFoiCyeLp/UQeY\nf/qv4eUS/y2sqS+8bLeq1lKYs5DKWUBBp8xmngHvMj43srrs45uRLuNIS+X23iZm\nojgaGtnMLD03lxPf7cqkNIDTF3GxPrMMxlRkQjR+4CTTPaadADot/liCehKGcfIE\n4oh4Oc93eA0p6Q2zyjpp\n=KBK/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree ef340f45297b48100e6bc525523f09a09b5a3154\nparent 41395c586d9743550c27073260539724a4bfedd3\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787023061 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787023061 -0400\n\nfeat(code): show conversation turns alongside message counts (#5571)\n\n`/offload` feedback and the Debug Console now show conversation turns\ntogether with raw message counts.\n\n---\n\nMessage counts are hard to interpret. One user prompt can become several\nprovider messages (a tool call, a tool result, and a follow-up model\nturn), and the count changes from provider to provider. Conversation\nturns — the user prompts the model actually saw — do not change between\nproviders. This makes them a better unit for comparing offloads.\n\nChanges:\n\n- The offload report now shows both units, for example `Offloaded 4\nolder messages (2 conversation turns)` and `6 messages (3 conversation\nturns) kept`. The turn count excludes internal human messages\n(goal-state notices and `[SYSTEM]` interruptions) that collect below the\ncutoff.\n- The Debug Console `Messages` field shows `N messages (M rendered), K\nturns`, with correct singular and plural labels.\n- The new `MessageStore.turn_count` property counts `USER` and `SKILL`\nrows. A `/skill` invocation creates one `SKILL` row instead of a `USER`\nrow, so each skill use counts as one turn. It counts all rendered rows,\nincluding local-only flows such as `!shell` and most slash commands.\nThat is a broader set than the offload report's turn count, which comes\nfrom graph state; the property's docstring describes the difference.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T03:17:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3dd4fe5cdc548f5408d5b74b82084d9d4c01a664","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3dd4fe5cdc548f5408d5b74b82084d9d4c01a664","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3dd4fe5cdc548f5408d5b74b82084d9d4c01a664/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"41395c586d9743550c27073260539724a4bfedd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/41395c586d9743550c27073260539724a4bfedd3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/41395c586d9743550c27073260539724a4bfedd3"}]},{"sha":"41395c586d9743550c27073260539724a4bfedd3","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDQxMzk1YzU4NmQ5NzQzNTUwYzI3MDczMjYwNTM5NzI0YTRiZmVkZDM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T02:58:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T02:58:52Z"},"message":"fix(code): avoid duplicate Auto denial notices (#5501)\n\nAuto mode no longer repeats tool denial and classifier-unavailable\nreasons as standalone transcript messages.\n\n---\n\nDenied tool calls already render their authoritative error `ToolMessage`\non the tool row. Custom Auto transcript events are now limited to\nfallback and warning control-state notices.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/c7617e04-48bd-8951-73a7-c3ea7f4e4d49)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e4f04154df11f0655279deeba3e61c3f45557b49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e4f04154df11f0655279deeba3e61c3f45557b49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/41395c586d9743550c27073260539724a4bfedd3","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg8psCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUuEQAKJEJNUEehP9tcgloP50e4W4\nheaRFePu0oyBDQ7WZu3RUybLAnA0wLtkk+xb/NS/f9OH+Z8/mufbRaEx3RZ69VXZ\nFs8gq1/C2MV8mq3VZ289ICEIN8W/j462PWQluBb9ksXDML6F8imUrzIK7+7/HJii\nvXMwsObiThN+Bz3wFbkiLghgJWtRmXR6CcwJOuSNfmnqTMqjtClTX0VAcLEniLmg\nhGhQmr+GZvC6u8a0bvy0G8zAuNQDVAvXKUxfB22BwnJSjK6qd9kBc5KYByT/3ycN\nG8vkgdXrBlUV+ABUfZTtmBnND9nZap+qGXh1AjvIVuGplpeudZHNhT/CmsupgJI4\nlj4aNiy4FUrIvsNSFF9FnTTPsB3LU0677s6evDY0DORiVMjmtNPBaIBh2nTjKItK\nV8kWGL5j0AihIK8zh7Y/VfBo3ozyWBm8Fvj2aTC5AWc/tMGac6dVESxFoHfNEo/5\n8DxPA0EmHcAhOuHbA33Oky1A/DJYnnDgLTS/pb/jR8M7KLc05VG/Wx4J4s0NAOHA\nx/cIVaJKbsfsEWks8tnBAG510MHd8f9OQoEam12i7lauTZKmHfrgmQoL2+64YMbg\nAjZjDp7n7jhOm1yfzI5MGWqUw1CstAuKzAFHYwh6Km5ixFC3E2vH/iMlrJePXK0T\n+m0IrBztk/zTcnVrCulO\n=HLn0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e4f04154df11f0655279deeba3e61c3f45557b49\nparent 3c8cae6fa44d4e12062fdb10421b48587925eade\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787021932 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787021932 -0400\n\nfix(code): avoid duplicate Auto denial notices (#5501)\n\nAuto mode no longer repeats tool denial and classifier-unavailable\nreasons as standalone transcript messages.\n\n---\n\nDenied tool calls already render their authoritative error `ToolMessage`\non the tool row. Custom Auto transcript events are now limited to\nfallback and warning control-state notices.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/c7617e04-48bd-8951-73a7-c3ea7f4e4d49)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T02:58:52Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/41395c586d9743550c27073260539724a4bfedd3","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/41395c586d9743550c27073260539724a4bfedd3","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/41395c586d9743550c27073260539724a4bfedd3/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3c8cae6fa44d4e12062fdb10421b48587925eade","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3c8cae6fa44d4e12062fdb10421b48587925eade","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3c8cae6fa44d4e12062fdb10421b48587925eade"}]},{"sha":"3c8cae6fa44d4e12062fdb10421b48587925eade","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDNjOGNhZTZmYTQ0ZDRlMTIwNjJmZGIxMDQyMWI0ODU4NzkyNWVhZGU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T02:41:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T02:41:56Z"},"message":"fix(code): avoid transcript hydration lag (#5479)\n\nResumed transcripts now load quickly and scroll smoothly without\nblocking on message hydration.\n\n---\n\nTextual reapplies styles across the mounted DOM whenever history widgets\nare inserted. This made on-demand hydration stutter even in small\nbatches, especially because collapsed tool rows still retained their\nfull widget trees.\n\nThis mounts a small initial history window, warms it in bounded batches,\nprefetches relative to virtual spacer boundaries, coalesces hydration\nwork, and delays pruning until scrolling settles. Restored successful\ntool runs are represented by lazy data-backed summaries whose detail\nwidgets mount only when expanded.\n\nOn a 681-message local thread, restored history compacted to 265 display\nrows, initial loading took about 0.9 seconds, and background warmup\ncompleted the transcript before backward scrolling required hydration.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- 623 focused tests passed\n- Ruff passed on changed files\n- `ty` passed on changed production files\n\n</details>\n\n## Video\n### New (left) - Old (right)\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3f0d472d-5874-47f4-b247-92833f20c47d\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"bd84faa9ee65e14d4ddbe07ac9f11a2207c93de2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/bd84faa9ee65e14d4ddbe07ac9f11a2207c93de2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/3c8cae6fa44d4e12062fdb10421b48587925eade","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg8Z0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5lsQAFScCgut9tTjt7wmi6K4yaWZ\narRPAuL64TpErwHciQkz9AxhLbZEtaRLl2RzGI5BK8iWg0aH6j1MF51oGVf+9aQS\nxGbru+NKYJUTTmNosKRjE7Mr1almYZ7tG9AiDBuiwE227tKjkD/GwuhcIYmerdxl\nLQwgZEU5BpqhPQ6QaId79mEtQPkDFwS6Onbp/k3901vQgWWOnYeLrhtfxiDWAzwj\ntcpoEKiNPARX3v+9XKG8nYcMgYRNHjxefRJ1tmLaz3avKWFT3hWQZvNaWa9POzAW\n9oXNc6KOoDyUtoaB+S89WjvFSL5YXBZiYe/4ObtG/0o1qsMEfLHyyHZCqByyh885\nGIyw4HQvqzL/tPdvppebUHSGzA0fBFCLCJMsJRS4FPPCmAMFcPmOkExIgVzz4NbB\nG9KwE2PZ1bbtV1ra/Khs74e/2Zb3jaNm+ImPFtFVuGsrqmFrkrxvf1J04vnzA/N9\ne1OeBS08nipP9ZWeJ9aAcoKHOpWhOWLde1RyzbTNLSJSIxotd5rvOtEwiD96qkxd\nsrICRX55QO7L9zpTQrfH/ZBwJuJ96CyqE0ls9NHSXNNlq7pE2DYqvkcT5anMqL5x\nTBGOlN059L5iMiaIiZE2+UOUIhV9FpGSo7vXydvUdZ3xQuWxu8bo0LwGC6vDH+tX\nXr2xVbAj7AH5BMSg3a/o\n=Udvd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree bd84faa9ee65e14d4ddbe07ac9f11a2207c93de2\nparent dc029ef5072e9114125e4d332d3631dc1c3d4883\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1787020916 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787020916 -0400\n\nfix(code): avoid transcript hydration lag (#5479)\n\nResumed transcripts now load quickly and scroll smoothly without\nblocking on message hydration.\n\n---\n\nTextual reapplies styles across the mounted DOM whenever history widgets\nare inserted. This made on-demand hydration stutter even in small\nbatches, especially because collapsed tool rows still retained their\nfull widget trees.\n\nThis mounts a small initial history window, warms it in bounded batches,\nprefetches relative to virtual spacer boundaries, coalesces hydration\nwork, and delays pruning until scrolling settles. Restored successful\ntool runs are represented by lazy data-backed summaries whose detail\nwidgets mount only when expanded.\n\nOn a 681-message local thread, restored history compacted to 265 display\nrows, initial loading took about 0.9 seconds, and background warmup\ncompleted the transcript before backward scrolling required hydration.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- 623 focused tests passed\n- Ruff passed on changed files\n- `ty` passed on changed production files\n\n</details>\n\n## Video\n### New (left) - Old (right)\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3f0d472d-5874-47f4-b247-92833f20c47d\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T02:41:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3c8cae6fa44d4e12062fdb10421b48587925eade","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3c8cae6fa44d4e12062fdb10421b48587925eade","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3c8cae6fa44d4e12062fdb10421b48587925eade/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"dc029ef5072e9114125e4d332d3631dc1c3d4883","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/dc029ef5072e9114125e4d332d3631dc1c3d4883","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/dc029ef5072e9114125e4d332d3631dc1c3d4883"}]},{"sha":"dc029ef5072e9114125e4d332d3631dc1c3d4883","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGRjMDI5ZWY1MDcyZTkxMTQxMjVlNGQzMzJkMzYzMWRjMWMzZDQ4ODM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T02:38:10Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T02:38:10Z"},"message":"fix(code): defer plugin reload hint during startup (#5502)\n\nInstalled plugins no longer suggest `/reload` while the initial server\nconnection status is still loading.\n\n---\n\nThe plugin manager now receives the current connection state and leaves\nMCP status indeterminate until startup settles. Verified with focused\nmanager-state and command-routing tests plus package lint and type\nchecks.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4e557032-9927-6074-9d26-2d29863a0925)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"b34d0038029df462dba02ae6577e2c79e98481d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b34d0038029df462dba02ae6577e2c79e98481d6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/dc029ef5072e9114125e4d332d3631dc1c3d4883","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg8WSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6IoQAKd3cQt3hfRf6k8mjZTGD5Sb\nu2Sw0vtx4tTI6kkLb4lgTZwHUNvq3h9ewvK5FD4NlOmEv8P7Vh1Os9VGfwXpmAe8\nCFV/V31sDdzhtAMLmuXPGXalrqBD4Z8EjbUn69Sxhm4HasZ1t0LFl4U9+2ew18vt\n1d4XLPWfePlkOfHjs8YjTcuGDtm0shZIKH0An5dYp7neNFQT+RyoTgS+eho5dcnj\nbnvMWRWClcxTJnrPmTqLW91gXd2uM1lckfQtV0yI8j1a5FhuXjzZzmouLQmgylUV\nsAQpV2bJjUUayeNzpmwH9tvrx+8aGe6rSTNOSMxqfPRayUx3CXkpeSyw3SEMQ7kC\nD6KhGc2Q3EUcAytSQfMmZRIt3lL9ARXhzYsacf/cV60mfVRpJ0rH1L0+T5v+Z+At\nvs1uCFWRq6wdB/oA+X9/fzEvjwjdhECHDFWliJSxroyAq9i42bhRQYex2b3/Fext\nf3nOWnOcm8pLhbtRqyvFkJXJ0wHdEZcpwMKtbQzlgQcLeckaBWtu0JvynuvLrXl+\nqM1cr6zSMGcYVRDcKjU1Zx4f0fijCL5tnmpxB0Z3UkrTa1fPYKM4E9mLlbLSFXRw\nKuoAToaC8G7rvZfHmh9W0CPxj3VOqqS4YtWNiAmkLPmuswan9UVvUIEFcMy/lQCN\nyO0z1PQm3Q5E/IlypJ/e\n=QnYH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b34d0038029df462dba02ae6577e2c79e98481d6\nparent 064a75b3118b78aec32faeb6efd5ad6625be855e\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787020690 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787020690 -0400\n\nfix(code): defer plugin reload hint during startup (#5502)\n\nInstalled plugins no longer suggest `/reload` while the initial server\nconnection status is still loading.\n\n---\n\nThe plugin manager now receives the current connection state and leaves\nMCP status indeterminate until startup settles. Verified with focused\nmanager-state and command-routing tests plus package lint and type\nchecks.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/4e557032-9927-6074-9d26-2d29863a0925)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T02:38:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/dc029ef5072e9114125e4d332d3631dc1c3d4883","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/dc029ef5072e9114125e4d332d3631dc1c3d4883","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/dc029ef5072e9114125e4d332d3631dc1c3d4883/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"064a75b3118b78aec32faeb6efd5ad6625be855e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/064a75b3118b78aec32faeb6efd5ad6625be855e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/064a75b3118b78aec32faeb6efd5ad6625be855e"}]},{"sha":"064a75b3118b78aec32faeb6efd5ad6625be855e","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDA2NGE3NWIzMTE4Yjc4YWVjMzJmYWViNmVmZDVhZDY2MjViZTg1NWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T01:58:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T01:58:57Z"},"message":"feat(infra): credit issue reporters in release notes (#5565)\n\nGitHub release notes now include a **Special thanks** section. It\ncredits the users who reported the issues that this release's pull\nrequests closed, with links to those issues. The existing\ncommunity-contributor shoutouts credit pull request authors; this\nsection credits issue reporters. Users who are internal maintainers on\nthis release are not included.\n\n```md\n**Special thanks** to everyone who reported the issues addressed in this release: @carol ([#5310](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5310)), @dave ([#5201](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5201), [#5202](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5202))\n```\n\n---\n\nThe existing `collect_contributors` walk does the lookup. Its per-PR `gh\npr view` call now also requests `closingIssuesReferences`, so both\nattribution lists use the same range, retry, and failure handling.\n\nFor each merged PR, the issue author is credited — not the PR author.\nEntries are grouped by login with deduplicated, ascending issue numbers,\nand rendered as a comma-separated list like the other attribution lines.\nBot accounts (`[bot]` suffix), empty logins, and unusable issue numbers\nare skipped with a warning. A missing `closingIssuesReferences` field\nalso warns instead of silently producing an empty section. If no closed\nissues are found, the section is omitted. Lookup failures never block a\nrelease.","tree":{"sha":"30b4e6ddfa2af2132839e152ee4d57020a8120a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/30b4e6ddfa2af2132839e152ee4d57020a8120a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/064a75b3118b78aec32faeb6efd5ad6625be855e","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg7xhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANAwQAFrG7fjqSh/M9FRQtmZvSoQL\n2rug9qqCajEgC+pb5NATBksE38ItwCji3e2k76xFngb023CXxJw5CxV91Jd2Ax1V\nAmtvFa0qsHAV+oufHDX+p0aX8LxNqpkBQZDVoM+UfJJYtrRvZVeYLjNWl4V/1/Vn\n69+kMONpA3Ukg/TIj7p8DF8x5cSswxTGcHdCt/X0rlWO8LAn1Z3FO42nGROGe6AY\ng+BZyY5MneJR/Yuv0K2HA0VUMOWEEtj8nUtGE1vtiJ6LNMdcaqRPj2NQwTwH3p3a\naHQAstbMcy5wz9NBmtn+zKrSrLty+mfyKVytu7cyBBZMKJoZpH2obIJbnWVkBchP\nATu6B9t8OnT8klHDPypLkQImzdDf9GA4CUwj0rufpCF49Std6L9ChLVCLVft7aj5\nS9FlmZeE4M1hoY8slvYODl9QJlWIsm837AJ2Vm4mTeZZk/IciXpgm0ty8cxBZWdi\nDBERYAyoC/sReZQIst7aRgtdoQVyjaq+52BDUfBSpQl3wvzvj3m5vml1IaaV1wcB\ntRv07rNJGqsokDa48d1a+oDFmpcB9DOllyQKwqETiXcOv/asQPHDiKfX3Gam0KR5\n2okVe0BrLq13vuVg03G19n4dPyq/w/mbm6rn5YrjZGHcJ16eAWRmKZBGxYInuGaR\nX60UKeGJEAXkjMHBT+AH\n=hJXO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 30b4e6ddfa2af2132839e152ee4d57020a8120a6\nparent 22045da8a7ff7611a166403b604ca84a5eaa818a\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787018337 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787018337 -0400\n\nfeat(infra): credit issue reporters in release notes (#5565)\n\nGitHub release notes now include a **Special thanks** section. It\ncredits the users who reported the issues that this release's pull\nrequests closed, with links to those issues. The existing\ncommunity-contributor shoutouts credit pull request authors; this\nsection credits issue reporters. Users who are internal maintainers on\nthis release are not included.\n\n```md\n**Special thanks** to everyone who reported the issues addressed in this release: @carol ([#5310](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5310)), @dave ([#5201](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5201), [#5202](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5202))\n```\n\n---\n\nThe existing `collect_contributors` walk does the lookup. Its per-PR `gh\npr view` call now also requests `closingIssuesReferences`, so both\nattribution lists use the same range, retry, and failure handling.\n\nFor each merged PR, the issue author is credited — not the PR author.\nEntries are grouped by login with deduplicated, ascending issue numbers,\nand rendered as a comma-separated list like the other attribution lines.\nBot accounts (`[bot]` suffix), empty logins, and unusable issue numbers\nare skipped with a warning. A missing `closingIssuesReferences` field\nalso warns instead of silently producing an empty section. If no closed\nissues are found, the section is omitted. Lookup failures never block a\nrelease.","verified_at":"2026-08-18T01:58:57Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/064a75b3118b78aec32faeb6efd5ad6625be855e","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/064a75b3118b78aec32faeb6efd5ad6625be855e","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/064a75b3118b78aec32faeb6efd5ad6625be855e/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"22045da8a7ff7611a166403b604ca84a5eaa818a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/22045da8a7ff7611a166403b604ca84a5eaa818a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/22045da8a7ff7611a166403b604ca84a5eaa818a"}]},{"sha":"22045da8a7ff7611a166403b604ca84a5eaa818a","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDIyMDQ1ZGE4YTdmZjc2MTFhMTY2NDAzYjYwNGNhODRhNWVhYTgxOGE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T01:50:38Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T01:50:38Z"},"message":"chore(infra): consolidate author-response automation on `waiting-on-author` (#5570)\n\n`waiting-on-author` is now the single label for author-response\nautomation: it is removed automatically when the author replies, and the\nitem auto-closes after 10 days without a reply (with a comment\nexplaining how to reopen).\n\n---\n\nThe repo had two labels with the same intent: `needs-response` (which\nhad the reply-detection and auto-close automation) and\n`waiting-on-author` (manual only, though its description claimed it was\nremoved automatically — it wasn't). Maintainers had to remember which of\nthe two actually did something.\n\nThis consolidates on `waiting-on-author`, the more memorable name, by\nrenaming the two workflows (`needs_response.yml` →\n`waiting_on_author.yml`, `needs_response_author_reply.yml` →\n`waiting_on_author_reply.yml`) and pointing them at the\n`waiting-on-author` label. Behavior is unchanged otherwise: replies via\nconversation comments, review-thread replies, and submitted reviews all\nclear the label; pushing commits does not; the 10-day timeout is\nmeasured from the latest label event; `do-not-close` and draft PRs are\nskipped.\n\nAlready done outside this PR (label state isn't version-controlled):\n- Migrated the one open item carrying `needs-response` (#2982) to\n`waiting-on-author`\n- Deleted the `needs-response` label\n- Updated the `waiting-on-author` description to \"Maintainer awaits\nauthor reply. Removed on reply. Auto-closes after 10 days.\"","tree":{"sha":"a80fdad073884421d4e1c7ff21531136280e1f64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a80fdad073884421d4e1c7ff21531136280e1f64"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/22045da8a7ff7611a166403b604ca84a5eaa818a","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg7puCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAylEQABVdOyYj7znNE9fFvhh/9JFH\ni4vdVCyhJjlwKeg5yF9/MYP5ao0Tbnf8NIo+E1UO9qC6LDdskCHvZo9ZKen7LOj6\nTKEd2mgaf2/DNdbwdDVRUXg4pGkb3/KcSzGr4JFctYTzyZ//PfjpwBf/m16DdLEp\n8RkiLEbw344slsXZfxlpn3/MHnwxP+QPGPy+pn9qDE5b+tmN69J+3zaQWKitU+ga\nHrYxYUlHvfAXO+nn5TCtsM1WNxXYjOkl4ZAlw5Cv3YYeG2pLScvgxR+O9w6Nk9fB\ngX5ocMpypQMqf4QW2lTOKgj+gejUKEoKQNg3m7Snh6W1H/gYw7Q81ncZVpmz9q8Y\nB1Bfxys2mIMciGrhaMs5o7Vm8mMBkU6pGw1G5G9z8y2pPCm0aNwdqUwBFWgJYuwV\n8RAPAKZZPDju/SszgQBPfrHWt0LL4XMfFGNAbBZX3Vdb2lx7cpmvI1+ONT/luXI3\nPJ5RDlye/Pv70lxz6zEqN+ol0aawK7kG43iqjgenUC+scfA3cQlisMTA2fnzbO8e\ni8YFJ8beqMru4ajwgSsi2saijVPdrpSblj+dVw3u3VgY9OE7YWJYzey49q4VZ07F\njSYsi6Ee8gCfS3m2iKvw1mMCbjyo07sr+zhfFYHzCfK9WWPICpf/zdQM9ncaqd+d\nORQDnCYoRJb5n48CuZzg\n=7AXd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a80fdad073884421d4e1c7ff21531136280e1f64\nparent e03f03026984bf4bdeb8bd661707f29a4d682738\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787017838 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787017838 -0400\n\nchore(infra): consolidate author-response automation on `waiting-on-author` (#5570)\n\n`waiting-on-author` is now the single label for author-response\nautomation: it is removed automatically when the author replies, and the\nitem auto-closes after 10 days without a reply (with a comment\nexplaining how to reopen).\n\n---\n\nThe repo had two labels with the same intent: `needs-response` (which\nhad the reply-detection and auto-close automation) and\n`waiting-on-author` (manual only, though its description claimed it was\nremoved automatically — it wasn't). Maintainers had to remember which of\nthe two actually did something.\n\nThis consolidates on `waiting-on-author`, the more memorable name, by\nrenaming the two workflows (`needs_response.yml` →\n`waiting_on_author.yml`, `needs_response_author_reply.yml` →\n`waiting_on_author_reply.yml`) and pointing them at the\n`waiting-on-author` label. Behavior is unchanged otherwise: replies via\nconversation comments, review-thread replies, and submitted reviews all\nclear the label; pushing commits does not; the 10-day timeout is\nmeasured from the latest label event; `do-not-close` and draft PRs are\nskipped.\n\nAlready done outside this PR (label state isn't version-controlled):\n- Migrated the one open item carrying `needs-response` (#2982) to\n`waiting-on-author`\n- Deleted the `needs-response` label\n- Updated the `waiting-on-author` description to \"Maintainer awaits\nauthor reply. Removed on reply. Auto-closes after 10 days.\"","verified_at":"2026-08-18T01:50:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/22045da8a7ff7611a166403b604ca84a5eaa818a","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/22045da8a7ff7611a166403b604ca84a5eaa818a","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/22045da8a7ff7611a166403b604ca84a5eaa818a/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e03f03026984bf4bdeb8bd661707f29a4d682738","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e03f03026984bf4bdeb8bd661707f29a4d682738","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e03f03026984bf4bdeb8bd661707f29a4d682738"}]},{"sha":"e03f03026984bf4bdeb8bd661707f29a4d682738","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGUwM2YwMzAyNjk4NGJmNGJkZWI4YmQ2NjE3MDdmMjlhNGQ2ODI3Mzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T01:37:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T01:37:18Z"},"message":"fix(code): avoid plugin reload prompt flash (#5500)\n\nPlugin reload confirmation now appears without flashing the chat screen\nbetween modals.\n\n---\n\n`PluginManagerScreen` keeps its backdrop mounted while plugin state is\nchecked and transforms in place into the reload confirmation. This\nremoves the standalone follow-up modal while preserving reload,\ndeferral, and failure behavior; Textual keypress tests cover modal\ncontinuity.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/37b3ae42-2400-0998-058a-09917b0bc219)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"7ebc4c74351d129d594b69e530146a1869a8f356","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7ebc4c74351d129d594b69e530146a1869a8f356"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/e03f03026984bf4bdeb8bd661707f29a4d682738","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg7dOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJY4QAI7e9L/oItb2KN9/erV5MKLz\nfg6mHKNiyq1ro/PBFl8qUKn7IDvCMnJgd5yb+6v/nla2yRi3vUpZK9Vob8QLMLUX\nFKFkHMWsfAedqYTBC6P5JCFWqtI3RjRkZFmsk0mmCmFFB9zPp6CcQrR0RNyAPWfq\nQ/l+vx+PJCbie1dAFImIFJ7byCut5mLsLQYCZtsOa1VTZRj9MKs9YFxW7YA32nxb\nDehr9hDFl3NbhgsXU2yLgSWY5gNhzIkUpmdOHZTVirsRjk5CF12PCq8MRVcOHoYc\nvIsUIlvoDYYJxr1LKTuaW6bCrxIWmW8PFkm3Slz3POVNFOd5+3v55GHujOn5dCIz\nuCEoEbWE7kEnImzef40g4l8wsphjeENqk7guVPT820doYlVtAVYmdSl229Hh4Oej\nMmQsfiCsxb8oDTxVAGr4WxiYxG8PGqe760Z+AV20uce7uNjQno+rPo8AQufkbPDk\nffhNKNXkrnz3jDGj3tlv7FzBRvBt8NIR+xYWfsmIAvJl3HUoJR7SA6rED7NjFMqO\n5+PJamplDzKDC28FKlTDrOZeD/muq1n1yj9qnPpv7UunVOdqO4Hg1W8QTQ8PYkfL\nqy7z7bHHfLF58UlyJu8SkmzUjARBRlb1kKk6IuSNFMuJDl4TjkdMUKpMLBEsjC5d\naJf050b+KL+LN3GtM0iW\n=C5+p\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7ebc4c74351d129d594b69e530146a1869a8f356\nparent c325e7c10929b701c8b368331de36d16b322564f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787017038 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787017038 -0400\n\nfix(code): avoid plugin reload prompt flash (#5500)\n\nPlugin reload confirmation now appears without flashing the chat screen\nbetween modals.\n\n---\n\n`PluginManagerScreen` keeps its backdrop mounted while plugin state is\nchecked and transforms in place into the reload confirmation. This\nremoves the standalone follow-up modal while preserving reload,\ndeferral, and failure behavior; Textual keypress tests cover modal\ncontinuity.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/37b3ae42-2400-0998-058a-09917b0bc219)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T01:37:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e03f03026984bf4bdeb8bd661707f29a4d682738","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e03f03026984bf4bdeb8bd661707f29a4d682738","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e03f03026984bf4bdeb8bd661707f29a4d682738/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c325e7c10929b701c8b368331de36d16b322564f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c325e7c10929b701c8b368331de36d16b322564f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c325e7c10929b701c8b368331de36d16b322564f"}]},{"sha":"c325e7c10929b701c8b368331de36d16b322564f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGMzMjVlN2MxMDkyOWI3MDFjOGIzNjgzMzFkZTM2ZDE2YjMyMjU2NGY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T01:37:09Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T01:37:09Z"},"message":"style(code): preserve subagent hint at narrow widths (#5410)\n\nThe dynamic subagent panel now keeps its expand/collapse hint visible\nwhen the terminal is narrow.\n\n---\n\nThe header previously rendered its summary and right-aligned hint as one\noversized line, allowing Textual to clip the action. The summary and\nhint now use separate flexible and fixed-width regions, so excess\nmetadata truncates with an ellipsis while the action remains intact.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/a7023827-4211-c99d-0478-fd027e53963d)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"68af49fadd5111e912847d420cb53bafef5ebffe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/68af49fadd5111e912847d420cb53bafef5ebffe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c325e7c10929b701c8b368331de36d16b322564f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg7dFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+n0QABVxpMdoKqMclsBayBeDV4wc\naIts5qqUflCZCrigd1B1WPK3R7GNL5XyJSbhk0GMqYNe/AtatDU9vQNYzN0Nqf8U\nek84rlWr1k7dbr/zbfehCUrUBceWTwpAmLVULlntRFcSxW7ykobRpi2ts338Lst9\nwf4dZLF9MUUd6NkT6ZRlHtLcA/P0Q27BOiMmcVKVx1xtYS5w0VxLVpRRplWGHw9w\nF5AmBwjS60E0eF4w6G8YRRRBOO4RMRLrCT1TwKc4p6za6xb+ta+G7l2OK3+eDuNg\nzlgvrnv7Mt6t7Q8+IsC69XnwUxvNvg13k3nuCApahCqugVY6Zryf5GurfdH0WtNm\nJaim4Wq0+5Cs4xwSXeyejarl0d4VzoF8rQLA+wGU6tnSc9ZRVvBxkPrE8XVnryeS\n496OaqnMdo9DxVjaaUTPafzP3sunchzpZihWNcC8AAH78BT95guMUp5G3uXepu77\nFmmvwmbKXMB8uGAxlAdvqqyjFLEs+8C6Ib0SniCH15pEZvGCkudp/xVZBBig3r7R\nv59XLaHWilVGm66nHw+KWsrzpWsqtLMkVXugDQuhjCEue4yu0x//TXfT0Qg3B1GJ\nObH2J4ljeBHxL6DIEPP95JfAUacVltELMsJ8R7tFAmVXn8HqI39VO8PyIvReUYn4\nHaVhxHGavMC3ajhs0fzy\n=+OUD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 68af49fadd5111e912847d420cb53bafef5ebffe\nparent c66d9b8500f120d6552af258750da8bb0dede7b8\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787017029 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787017029 -0400\n\nstyle(code): preserve subagent hint at narrow widths (#5410)\n\nThe dynamic subagent panel now keeps its expand/collapse hint visible\nwhen the terminal is narrow.\n\n---\n\nThe header previously rendered its summary and right-aligned hint as one\noversized line, allowing Textual to clip the action. The summary and\nhint now use separate flexible and fixed-width regions, so excess\nmetadata truncates with an ellipsis while the action remains intact.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/a7023827-4211-c99d-0478-fd027e53963d)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T01:37:10Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c325e7c10929b701c8b368331de36d16b322564f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c325e7c10929b701c8b368331de36d16b322564f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c325e7c10929b701c8b368331de36d16b322564f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"c66d9b8500f120d6552af258750da8bb0dede7b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c66d9b8500f120d6552af258750da8bb0dede7b8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c66d9b8500f120d6552af258750da8bb0dede7b8"}]},{"sha":"c66d9b8500f120d6552af258750da8bb0dede7b8","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGM2NmQ5Yjg1MDBmMTIwZDY1NTJhZjI1ODc1MGRhOGJiMGRlZGU3Yjg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T01:36:55Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T01:36:55Z"},"message":"fix(code): hide chat input cursor while unfocused (#5258)\n\nFixed a phantom blinking cursor in the chat input when clicking it while\nan approval widget holds keyboard focus.\n\n---\n\nClicking the chat input while an `edit_file` approval menu is open\npainted a blinking cursor there even though the menu immediately\nre-grabs focus, so the field looked editable but swallowed nothing.\nTextual's `TextArea._draw_cursor` is `(has_focus and not cursor_blink)\nor (cursor_blink and _cursor_visible)` — with blinking on it never\nconsults focus — and `_end_mouse_selection` (mouse-up) restarts the\nblink unconditionally, after the approval menu's `on_blur` handler has\nalready taken focus back. `PasteBurstTextArea` (shared base for the chat\ninput and inline prompts) now pauses the blink instead of restarting it\nwhen the text area is unfocused, which also covers programmatic\nmulti-character `insert()` into an unfocused input.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/857f729e-198f-4ba3-4bd4-251a76d07ad2)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"813ff2da0b0261c373ad419dac5cb2305ed54b90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/813ff2da0b0261c373ad419dac5cb2305ed54b90"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/c66d9b8500f120d6552af258750da8bb0dede7b8","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg7c3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7jQQAKy1Mi9y0QUDTw9Ab7AGUrez\nT3407rIPup7BM8iuqw2seOsoAXTc0NaOwpin5KuYmBw8yIRhwehwCPXewArGP4hj\nOdJBEAnkwEZg9VX5aS3IBDhFTHYY16slUEcD/rUfjXrG07HU1Pw43c7O/WWyfnnJ\nrbBxKSQI0wDJNazIk9aIA6vIHGdttMQa2WYpDj/5Ivwgjg7JX7Pocvc36jSSSD69\nx208DO6IBvp/GrOdDuhBoNGN82zDGUj3GujbNkUQGBkSc0JthcfEWgdQFPfSwj9q\nSiIl8oU05eUciGe8/c/gbvPw7BUQXSs/sdpHfPvYWTSjTkfaQdBL+4gvQKZ7gJ6j\njLvAtsJYJL3VX/ftXS2rZf5phRTkVA8+SwOisGix9QXFzh/6c8dvkkbvHK5/RNGB\n19OtfBTrfM/df+w9DP580W1MB33OHhoqz/pbnTY3zW7FrxVEONQFa7xU0C84qRbP\nwsJgIga4sLVlx2GN24rG4efUp9Rf3tGA3QwKCNHrkP+Y13fgv3GHzxriwYrupnra\nkyAm1HqNzVXmwrHIod7qWLcbJMwL6s1WcmBqAFlvT7y1qovIwnqd8qqwua9Z2DLz\n2LRZBVTXVNTsy85h9rme6oXD4cpBTaHLTL9qbUMZu1U/jUvgIJ5OagI84h4WfpmD\nNbX+mYuWgqsMAOyjx29a\n=5x/F\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 813ff2da0b0261c373ad419dac5cb2305ed54b90\nparent 96d72a188bf951c9d3ca103e6611dcb50961af93\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787017015 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787017015 -0400\n\nfix(code): hide chat input cursor while unfocused (#5258)\n\nFixed a phantom blinking cursor in the chat input when clicking it while\nan approval widget holds keyboard focus.\n\n---\n\nClicking the chat input while an `edit_file` approval menu is open\npainted a blinking cursor there even though the menu immediately\nre-grabs focus, so the field looked editable but swallowed nothing.\nTextual's `TextArea._draw_cursor` is `(has_focus and not cursor_blink)\nor (cursor_blink and _cursor_visible)` — with blinking on it never\nconsults focus — and `_end_mouse_selection` (mouse-up) restarts the\nblink unconditionally, after the approval menu's `on_blur` handler has\nalready taken focus back. `PasteBurstTextArea` (shared base for the chat\ninput and inline prompts) now pauses the blink instead of restarting it\nwhen the text area is unfocused, which also covers programmatic\nmulti-character `insert()` into an unfocused input.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/857f729e-198f-4ba3-4bd4-251a76d07ad2)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T01:36:56Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c66d9b8500f120d6552af258750da8bb0dede7b8","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/c66d9b8500f120d6552af258750da8bb0dede7b8","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/c66d9b8500f120d6552af258750da8bb0dede7b8/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://