commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-18T01:10:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-18T01:10:32Z"},"message":"fix(code): condition relative timestamp toggle (#5503)\n\nRelative timestamp controls now appear after Created At and Updated At,\nand only when at least one timestamp column is visible.\n\n---\n\nKeeps the formatting option adjacent to the columns it affects and\nremoves a no-op control when neither timestamp is shown.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/9260c3bf-bdc7-de2d-b68b-bd6e1a8c367d)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"30ab2aeb426d3959a4c0df5f95ab0793e0d537f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/30ab2aeb426d3959a4c0df5f95ab0793e0d537f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/96d72a188bf951c9d3ca103e6611dcb50961af93","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg7EICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAM44QAJWj+OyAQ1A6LK69mqKAFLqJ\nxwvor/q6odjeBRENMkLCiVfd9hfpDKpGLnh+HgV28REqO47Ps4QGtQzELVm3yVg/\nrxcdDmRyVLPKxnYrG4jkbvttUnoNmMHrPPKwOw4Hc48LubGhlqx2gSRQiHwZ1mVm\n479KYTMIRQYeSmYMNxyyrt+l5gtvMs1oElk183CF4nXiOg7KWcyGmmXKIrn3udOH\n3Q0vtbCNkTTBCRlN8ZRdSjyYhJodiIVx9VBfpVBiLhlEX5hieu2MiQlIHCj0ryRt\npe/23S3YJwzrGfezafeXVIftmBUPMP6FrViWA/Nax6xCdXX2QNTiMuw+rP1tZu5Y\nsoVOD5oAgbxg55WQmTXzjzWGPSUWHsb3uRiWOBVOg+sONEpiPMu2Eo4ui5nTwX8Z\n4EU5w4zGqRCGAlladAXYULJGNZDA06cqvcYxbN7k2lC9u2JJHJ8CSmFpwTTb686w\nNh+Ay5gNlIO7ZrIc3fZ9ja7GOp/dgYBzKpqudAv2gZbBoAOn/wID0c2zgXxbc8Bo\nc+qKv/4zzHpIYfkPahIKcHFwq+hLYklrCF593SihTwTTeHCNThMIX/U6o5DTZVGs\niQ2HhGSFnFTw5D8ud31Nuvo+oTixx0XzXDsqRYHAZiC9ELyRlxBi8AqxaZEqpRRA\nyQlXwZ9mNQ79qQVDFmg1\n=FFUb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 30ab2aeb426d3959a4c0df5f95ab0793e0d537f1\nparent 32f35d5e01f460549c10365eb569978909f5c969\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787015432 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787015432 -0400\n\nfix(code): condition relative timestamp toggle (#5503)\n\nRelative timestamp controls now appear after Created At and Updated At,\nand only when at least one timestamp column is visible.\n\n---\n\nKeeps the formatting option adjacent to the columns it affects and\nremoves a no-op control when neither timestamp is shown.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/9260c3bf-bdc7-de2d-b68b-bd6e1a8c367d)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-18T01:10:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/96d72a188bf951c9d3ca103e6611dcb50961af93","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/96d72a188bf951c9d3ca103e6611dcb50961af93","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/96d72a188bf951c9d3ca103e6611dcb50961af93/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"32f35d5e01f460549c10365eb569978909f5c969","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/32f35d5e01f460549c10365eb569978909f5c969","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/32f35d5e01f460549c10365eb569978909f5c969"}]},{"sha":"32f35d5e01f460549c10365eb569978909f5c969","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDMyZjM1ZDVlMDFmNDYwNTQ5YzEwMzY1ZWI1Njk5Nzg5MDlmNWM5Njk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-17T23:23:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-17T23:23:14Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): make `BackendProtocol.glob` recursive for bare patterns (#5026)\n\nFixes #4978\n\n`glob(\"*.py\")` now finds files in subdirectories on every backend. This\nalso aligns `glob()` with the `grep` include-glob rules from #3936.\n\nRelated: #3936, #4063.\n\n---\n\nBackends did not agree on what a bare pattern such as `*.py` means:\n\n- `FilesystemBackend` matched the file name at any depth.\n- `StoreBackend` and `StateBackend` matched top-level files only.\n- `SandboxBackend` matched top-level files only and skipped files under\nhidden directories.\n\nA caller that switched backends got different results for the same\npattern, and an agent that expected the recursive `FilesystemBackend`\nbehavior silently found fewer files on the others. The `grep`\ninclude-glob already had one shared contract (#3936); `glob()` did not.\n\n## The rules\n\nThis PR gives `glob()` the same contract as the `grep` include-glob on\nevery backend:\n\n- A pattern with no `/` matches the file name at any depth. `*.py`\nmatches `src/app/main.py` and `.hidden/x.py`.\n- A pattern with a `/` matches the path relative to the search root and\nsupports `**`.\n- A leading `/` anchors the pattern to the search root. `/*.py` matches\ntop-level files only.\n- A name that starts with a dot matches only if that pattern segment\nalso starts with a dot, and `**` does not go into dot-directories. So\n`*.yml` matches *more* files than `**/*.yml`.\n\nThe in-process backends use the shared matcher,\n`compile_grep_include_glob`; the Sandbox backend mirrors its contract\nremotely. If the matcher refuses a pattern (for example, brace expansion\npast its limit), it raises `ValueError` and the backend returns it as\n`GlobResult.error`.\n\n## Sandbox backend\n\nThe sandbox cannot call the shared matcher directly. Its remote script\napplies the same rules over `os.walk`, including hidden directories. A\n20-case differential test compares the remote matcher with\n`FilesystemBackend.glob`, which uses `compile_grep_include_glob`, across\nthe cases where the two underlying libraries disagree: negated character\nclasses, nested braces, empty path segments, trailing slashes, and case\nsensitivity.\n\nA bare pattern now walks the whole tree instead of listing one\ndirectory, so the script must not run unbounded. These limits keep it\ncontained and make partial results visible:\n\n- A 5-second time budget, checked per directory and within large\ndirectories, and a cap on the number of matches. If the script stops\nearly, the result is marked `truncated` so it is never shown as\ncomplete. A list clipped in transport is now also marked `truncated`.\n- `**` matching is memoized, so a pattern such as `**/*/**/*` cannot run\nexponentially.\n- A directory the script cannot read is reported instead of quietly\nmissing from the results.\n- Every failure returns a structured error code. Output the host cannot\nparse is an error, not an empty result.\n- Brace expansion is capped and returns `pattern_too_broad`, which is\ndistinct from `invalid_pattern` (used for `..` traversal).\n\n## What changes for callers\n\nThis is a bug fix, but some changes are visible to callers:\n\n1. `Store`, `State`, and `Sandbox` bare patterns now match files in\nsubdirectories. This is the intended fix. Code that assumed `*.py` meant\ntop-level only will now see nested paths.\n2. On `Filesystem`, a pattern that contains a `/` no longer gets an\nimplicit `**/` prefix, and `/*.py` is top-level only.\n3. A bare `*` does not match a name that starts with a dot. Use `.*` or\n`.github/**` for those. A non-dot file under a hidden directory still\nmatches `*.py` on every backend.\n4. `SandboxBackend.glob` returns absolute paths and regular files only,\nmatching `FilesystemBackend.glob`. It used to return\nsearch-root-relative paths and include directories. Relative paths also\nbypassed `deny` permission rules, because those rules match absolute\npatterns.\n5. `CompositeBackend` keeps an anchored pattern anchored when it strips\nthe route prefix. `/memories/*.md` stays top-level within the route\ninstead of matching at any depth.\n6. A pattern the matcher refuses (for example, brace expansion past its\nlimit) raises `ValueError` and is returned as `GlobResult.error` from\nevery backend. Before, a private `wcmatch` exception reached the caller.\n\n<details>\n<summary>1 — Bare patterns: before and after</summary>\n\n`glob(\"*.py\")` with `a.py` at the root and `sub/b.py` nested:\n\n- **Before:** `StoreBackend` and `StateBackend` returned `a.py` only.\n`FilesystemBackend` returned both.\n- **After:** every backend returns `a.py` and `sub/b.py`.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>2 — Leading <code>/</code> anchors: before and after</summary>\n\n`glob(\"/*.py\")` with `a.py` at the root and `sub/b.py` nested:\n\n- **Before:** `ContextHubBackend` returned both, because its matcher let\n`*` cross `/`.\n- **After:** every backend returns `a.py` only.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>3 — Dot names: before and after</summary>\n\n`glob(\"*.yml\")` with `.github/workflows/ci.yml`:\n\n- **Before:** matched on `Filesystem` and `ContextHub` (both crossed\ndot-directories); not on `Store`, `State`, or `Sandbox` (top-level\nonly).\n- **After:** still matches everywhere — a bare pattern matches the\nbasename at any depth. The dot rule applies once the pattern has a `/`:\n`**/*.yml` no longer matches, because `.github` starts with a dot and\nthe pattern segment does not. Use `.github/**` to match it.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>4 — Sandbox paths and permission rules: before and\nafter</summary>\n\n`glob(\"*.py\")` from search root `/workspace`, with a `deny` rule on\n`/workspace/secrets/**`:\n\n- **Before:** the sandbox returned `secrets/key.py` relative to the\nsearch root. The `deny` rule did not match it (the rule needs an\nabsolute path), so the file was not filtered out.\n- **After:** the sandbox returns `/workspace/secrets/key.py`, so the\n`deny` rule matches and the file is filtered out.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>5 — Routed patterns: before and after</summary>\n\n`glob(\"/memories/*.md\")` against a route mounted at `/memories/`, with\n`note.md` at the route root and `sub/nested.md` deeper:\n\n- **Before:** stripping the route prefix turned the pattern into the\nbasename pattern `*.md`, which matched `note.md` and `sub/nested.md`.\n- **After:** stripping keeps the anchor, so the pattern becomes `/*.md`\nand matches `note.md` only.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>6 — Invalid patterns: before and after</summary>\n\nA pattern whose brace expansion is too large (for example, many `{a,b}`\ngroups):\n\n- **Before:** the backend raised a private `wcmatch` exception to the\ncaller.\n- **After:** the matcher raises `ValueError`, and every backend returns\nit as `GlobResult.error`.\n\n</details>","tree":{"sha":"f38c36f054fc7d96c5490048725c9c704e34c47c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/f38c36f054fc7d96c5490048725c9c704e34c47c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/32f35d5e01f460549c10365eb569978909f5c969","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg5fiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtAoQALAqW1JEUnV3Qsh2Ft3y+axh\nw8t1y8yO/IL+7KOhayq7ocpz67M8GMljJGjo/+5cm4aY3W4nkw8YfPKtCMFGDrYP\nUdwE1JPua4N8Zk8ZVaLqacz4GcVEm7SQTwR0VJKOSgYMQu2+rQbwIzAkqgUsZbha\nNvTPGSrBmc/3wF3lqdJAksTK/tKd/3m06apidm7JraRWzqNFDiAKsXdUF6t+6WtL\nYutWQesMnm7hEZjymMCFmAFOLfcoEFZi2+rsD6gUJggwwQd33kffQNfeScrxvCdf\nSwCTS+JWN/KDsvpGUtGWbR3n5NsSmRJHv2jSquKG7HSzxOnSGFl4kDxt3ppSTxKP\nzzn/bU6fd6Wi6+Q0HD257v0SNwnMwLsq2qzw6czYf1ctXePMkTi8bGcv6CYyC3Gy\naDY2tZKrSZkME3buNYCyLr3ztG/XdvIvGb3dwJXgbD8o48Q6Fhvm6fbGilNwKIxQ\nc5f3lGVRn7M6vpWheeqtEXJOcrYs1QfdalPHcKvQpyJofdKjUZcCUaGecXlEjWUr\nodkkXBAuBK3knrZff+bZ/yQnrXANLLvtTUXSavf4dTbO68r9Q6rbWbVLG4cci+xA\nhOxgacqTPekmWRK/QqEXKn49jtPLqQXzAILiFN2vtUBKunt4Ec0EVRrXZ3dqWL1u\nos7b/ZI82qZ8/2xuVI3q\n=qOkZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree f38c36f054fc7d96c5490048725c9c704e34c47c\nparent 3cdc82181bc94a904290cce23db04d8a1341b123\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787008994 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787008994 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): make `BackendProtocol.glob` recursive for bare patterns (#5026)\n\nFixes #4978\n\n`glob(\"*.py\")` now finds files in subdirectories on every backend. This\nalso aligns `glob()` with the `grep` include-glob rules from #3936.\n\nRelated: #3936, #4063.\n\n---\n\nBackends did not agree on what a bare pattern such as `*.py` means:\n\n- `FilesystemBackend` matched the file name at any depth.\n- `StoreBackend` and `StateBackend` matched top-level files only.\n- `SandboxBackend` matched top-level files only and skipped files under\nhidden directories.\n\nA caller that switched backends got different results for the same\npattern, and an agent that expected the recursive `FilesystemBackend`\nbehavior silently found fewer files on the others. The `grep`\ninclude-glob already had one shared contract (#3936); `glob()` did not.\n\n## The rules\n\nThis PR gives `glob()` the same contract as the `grep` include-glob on\nevery backend:\n\n- A pattern with no `/` matches the file name at any depth. `*.py`\nmatches `src/app/main.py` and `.hidden/x.py`.\n- A pattern with a `/` matches the path relative to the search root and\nsupports `**`.\n- A leading `/` anchors the pattern to the search root. `/*.py` matches\ntop-level files only.\n- A name that starts with a dot matches only if that pattern segment\nalso starts with a dot, and `**` does not go into dot-directories. So\n`*.yml` matches *more* files than `**/*.yml`.\n\nThe in-process backends use the shared matcher,\n`compile_grep_include_glob`; the Sandbox backend mirrors its contract\nremotely. If the matcher refuses a pattern (for example, brace expansion\npast its limit), it raises `ValueError` and the backend returns it as\n`GlobResult.error`.\n\n## Sandbox backend\n\nThe sandbox cannot call the shared matcher directly. Its remote script\napplies the same rules over `os.walk`, including hidden directories. A\n20-case differential test compares the remote matcher with\n`FilesystemBackend.glob`, which uses `compile_grep_include_glob`, across\nthe cases where the two underlying libraries disagree: negated character\nclasses, nested braces, empty path segments, trailing slashes, and case\nsensitivity.\n\nA bare pattern now walks the whole tree instead of listing one\ndirectory, so the script must not run unbounded. These limits keep it\ncontained and make partial results visible:\n\n- A 5-second time budget, checked per directory and within large\ndirectories, and a cap on the number of matches. If the script stops\nearly, the result is marked `truncated` so it is never shown as\ncomplete. A list clipped in transport is now also marked `truncated`.\n- `**` matching is memoized, so a pattern such as `**/*/**/*` cannot run\nexponentially.\n- A directory the script cannot read is reported instead of quietly\nmissing from the results.\n- Every failure returns a structured error code. Output the host cannot\nparse is an error, not an empty result.\n- Brace expansion is capped and returns `pattern_too_broad`, which is\ndistinct from `invalid_pattern` (used for `..` traversal).\n\n## What changes for callers\n\nThis is a bug fix, but some changes are visible to callers:\n\n1. `Store`, `State`, and `Sandbox` bare patterns now match files in\nsubdirectories. This is the intended fix. Code that assumed `*.py` meant\ntop-level only will now see nested paths.\n2. On `Filesystem`, a pattern that contains a `/` no longer gets an\nimplicit `**/` prefix, and `/*.py` is top-level only.\n3. A bare `*` does not match a name that starts with a dot. Use `.*` or\n`.github/**` for those. A non-dot file under a hidden directory still\nmatches `*.py` on every backend.\n4. `SandboxBackend.glob` returns absolute paths and regular files only,\nmatching `FilesystemBackend.glob`. It used to return\nsearch-root-relative paths and include directories. Relative paths also\nbypassed `deny` permission rules, because those rules match absolute\npatterns.\n5. `CompositeBackend` keeps an anchored pattern anchored when it strips\nthe route prefix. `/memories/*.md` stays top-level within the route\ninstead of matching at any depth.\n6. A pattern the matcher refuses (for example, brace expansion past its\nlimit) raises `ValueError` and is returned as `GlobResult.error` from\nevery backend. Before, a private `wcmatch` exception reached the caller.\n\n<details>\n<summary>1 — Bare patterns: before and after</summary>\n\n`glob(\"*.py\")` with `a.py` at the root and `sub/b.py` nested:\n\n- **Before:** `StoreBackend` and `StateBackend` returned `a.py` only.\n`FilesystemBackend` returned both.\n- **After:** every backend returns `a.py` and `sub/b.py`.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>2 — Leading <code>/</code> anchors: before and after</summary>\n\n`glob(\"/*.py\")` with `a.py` at the root and `sub/b.py` nested:\n\n- **Before:** `ContextHubBackend` returned both, because its matcher let\n`*` cross `/`.\n- **After:** every backend returns `a.py` only.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>3 — Dot names: before and after</summary>\n\n`glob(\"*.yml\")` with `.github/workflows/ci.yml`:\n\n- **Before:** matched on `Filesystem` and `ContextHub` (both crossed\ndot-directories); not on `Store`, `State`, or `Sandbox` (top-level\nonly).\n- **After:** still matches everywhere — a bare pattern matches the\nbasename at any depth. The dot rule applies once the pattern has a `/`:\n`**/*.yml` no longer matches, because `.github` starts with a dot and\nthe pattern segment does not. Use `.github/**` to match it.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>4 — Sandbox paths and permission rules: before and\nafter</summary>\n\n`glob(\"*.py\")` from search root `/workspace`, with a `deny` rule on\n`/workspace/secrets/**`:\n\n- **Before:** the sandbox returned `secrets/key.py` relative to the\nsearch root. The `deny` rule did not match it (the rule needs an\nabsolute path), so the file was not filtered out.\n- **After:** the sandbox returns `/workspace/secrets/key.py`, so the\n`deny` rule matches and the file is filtered out.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>5 — Routed patterns: before and after</summary>\n\n`glob(\"/memories/*.md\")` against a route mounted at `/memories/`, with\n`note.md` at the route root and `sub/nested.md` deeper:\n\n- **Before:** stripping the route prefix turned the pattern into the\nbasename pattern `*.md`, which matched `note.md` and `sub/nested.md`.\n- **After:** stripping keeps the anchor, so the pattern becomes `/*.md`\nand matches `note.md` only.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>6 — Invalid patterns: before and after</summary>\n\nA pattern whose brace expansion is too large (for example, many `{a,b}`\ngroups):\n\n- **Before:** the backend raised a private `wcmatch` exception to the\ncaller.\n- **After:** the matcher raises `ValueError`, and every backend returns\nit as `GlobResult.error`.\n\n</details>","verified_at":"2026-08-17T23:23:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/32f35d5e01f460549c10365eb569978909f5c969","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/32f35d5e01f460549c10365eb569978909f5c969","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/32f35d5e01f460549c10365eb569978909f5c969/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3cdc82181bc94a904290cce23db04d8a1341b123","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3cdc82181bc94a904290cce23db04d8a1341b123","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3cdc82181bc94a904290cce23db04d8a1341b123"}]},{"sha":"3cdc82181bc94a904290cce23db04d8a1341b123","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDNjZGM4MjE4MWJjOTRhOTA0MjkwY2NlMjNkYjA0ZDhhMTM0MWIxMjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-17T22:55:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-17T22:55:30Z"},"message":"feat(code): carry `TERM_PROGRAM` into the resume hint (#5548)\n\nThe teardown resume hint prints a pasteable command for getting back\ninto a thread. A shell alias that exports `TERM_PROGRAM` cannot be\nrecovered from `argv[0]`, so the printed command drops it — along with\nanything keyed off it, such as conditional theme selection. Pasting the\nhint gets you the thread back, but not the environment it was launched\nin.\n\nThe variable now rides along as an env prefix when the launch\nenvironment supplied it (an inline `TERM_PROGRAM=x dcode`, a terminal's\nown export, or a shell alias):\n\n```\nResume this thread with:\nTERM_PROGRAM=WezTerm dcode -r a1b2c3\n```\n\nThe value is snapshotted at process entry, so a `TERM_PROGRAM` that\nappears only later — from a project or global `.env` file — is not\nechoed back. The value is shell-quoted, so a terminal name containing\nspaces or shell metacharacters cannot change what the pasted line does.\nA value containing control characters is omitted rather than stripped:\nstripping would both write raw escape sequences into teardown output and\nname a terminal the environment never actually contained.\n\nThe prefix uses POSIX syntax, so it is withheld on native Windows even\nwhen the variable is set — VS Code and WezTerm set `TERM_PROGRAM` on\nevery platform, and `cmd.exe`/PowerShell cannot parse a `VAR=value`\ncommand prefix. POSIX markers (`SHELL`, `MSYSTEM`, `WSL_DISTRO_NAME`)\nrestore the prefix under git-bash/MSYS/WSL.","tree":{"sha":"af265a9964e55907201961f5669b8d5b61c192e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/af265a9964e55907201961f5669b8d5b61c192e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/3cdc82181bc94a904290cce23db04d8a1341b123","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg5FiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+GoQAJadzGdjqN5DGZMpSP+jnNna\nmmmqyG/q3cKkewAP5eoGq6kCx7fbDhFY+08iCJ9DH7sHbK8VdwCGJlgSVCdidP8I\nazS8ON0Jmq8Jma5Tq03NDRx08PRar0uUSQrromn3kKDtAR7SunX29vMUyoEw6Bln\nc+H5Jur8Pn6uBWm3SMDm0/kwzYtNzrxoHFgyE+wiJ+vdevIDvYFN5IIx9pgLMcnS\nXR+ngEcp1ZjqIGa6+M4fU9sSB6B3ZF9jZ/JtGwQKfgbmC+gEJ8sTC49EpaWLaWGB\nc00Qig7tKEW/Yy30HoX05ycYzOGpDDRjeAb5hZ8X1Dol2DHzBl0Nv+OnT7PIQYGm\nWE986KpWcqZQEBYbRjfKb0Oh4lyXIqzab3aU1bNGDkOaqFFotgyFIwwwAZHnsf//\nhi9n6AmI2H61YCnnLFFMzd1pezyE28NOHI71i66z6WCZ5AalWs5op32uFxpMxmyn\nrWySCJZmoEIfLXHZ1tGYFD94VsjLRxqoXU0YRQnQ6XhciPhcfX9R5l96sPMYz3D6\no7BHM53U3ngHRAlD8RSyA1Z9pg1mUVkZxYssjIXdo9BvTb87TNeM7i/N0sSRywEF\nF8ZMfd+4dcm2nbsUJnG9wzAMQqHU8CbSZNI8ozNdf7x2BLUl0tzChp9KL8IayUmw\no//zUXZ1V/NDUY/SsmWA\n=jyYP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree af265a9964e55907201961f5669b8d5b61c192e6\nparent 0f5bd4f3356d0fcbdea436a27c8011629416a61c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787007330 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787007330 -0400\n\nfeat(code): carry `TERM_PROGRAM` into the resume hint (#5548)\n\nThe teardown resume hint prints a pasteable command for getting back\ninto a thread. A shell alias that exports `TERM_PROGRAM` cannot be\nrecovered from `argv[0]`, so the printed command drops it — along with\nanything keyed off it, such as conditional theme selection. Pasting the\nhint gets you the thread back, but not the environment it was launched\nin.\n\nThe variable now rides along as an env prefix when the launch\nenvironment supplied it (an inline `TERM_PROGRAM=x dcode`, a terminal's\nown export, or a shell alias):\n\n```\nResume this thread with:\nTERM_PROGRAM=WezTerm dcode -r a1b2c3\n```\n\nThe value is snapshotted at process entry, so a `TERM_PROGRAM` that\nappears only later — from a project or global `.env` file — is not\nechoed back. The value is shell-quoted, so a terminal name containing\nspaces or shell metacharacters cannot change what the pasted line does.\nA value containing control characters is omitted rather than stripped:\nstripping would both write raw escape sequences into teardown output and\nname a terminal the environment never actually contained.\n\nThe prefix uses POSIX syntax, so it is withheld on native Windows even\nwhen the variable is set — VS Code and WezTerm set `TERM_PROGRAM` on\nevery platform, and `cmd.exe`/PowerShell cannot parse a `VAR=value`\ncommand prefix. POSIX markers (`SHELL`, `MSYSTEM`, `WSL_DISTRO_NAME`)\nrestore the prefix under git-bash/MSYS/WSL.","verified_at":"2026-08-17T22:55:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3cdc82181bc94a904290cce23db04d8a1341b123","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3cdc82181bc94a904290cce23db04d8a1341b123","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3cdc82181bc94a904290cce23db04d8a1341b123/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0f5bd4f3356d0fcbdea436a27c8011629416a61c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0f5bd4f3356d0fcbdea436a27c8011629416a61c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0f5bd4f3356d0fcbdea436a27c8011629416a61c"}]},{"sha":"0f5bd4f3356d0fcbdea436a27c8011629416a61c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDBmNWJkNGYzMzU2ZDBmY2JkZWE0MzZhMjdjODAxMTYyOTQxNmE2MWM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-17T21:32:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-17T21:32:30Z"},"message":"fix(code): hide empty previous-thread hints (#5552)\n\nOffering a way back to an empty thread is noise — it lands you somewhere\nno different from the new thread you already have.\n\n---\n\n`/clear` and a thread switch both offer a `Previous thread: <id> (Resume\nwith /threads -r)` hint. That hint was gated only on `thread_exists`,\nand registering a thread with the server writes a checkpoint row, so a\nthread you never typed into still looked resumable. Leaving a fresh\nthread — with `/threads -r`, another `/clear`, or an agent swap —\ntherefore pointed you back at nothing.\n\nResuming such a thread works; it just isn't worth suggesting. So the\nhint now also asks whether the thread recorded any server output — an\n`ASSISTANT`, `TOOL`, or `SKILL` message — and stays quiet when it\ndidn't. Every path that leaves a thread samples the message store\nthrough the new `_store_has_server_output` before clearing it, so the\nanswer describes the thread being left rather than the one arriving.\n\nThe question is \"did you do anything here\", not \"can this be resumed\". A\nthread holding only `/goal` or `/rubric set` state is resumable but\nstill unused, so it gets no hint either. Suppression logs at `info`, so\na missing hint is still visible in the Debug Console.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e649f343-b71e-bb41-c988-9d422829699c)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e8ba6794c014fad06e8466ef5fec4c9888a12f33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e8ba6794c014fad06e8466ef5fec4c9888a12f33"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0f5bd4f3356d0fcbdea436a27c8011629416a61c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg33uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABPcQAKDdSgk0qHxXPGM91uNHmVl1\ni4MqCi4HgWe7lCMLO8tc+hf75wVdW3bS4spTBWWoquLm+Jbs85JKoSfCXJKzTenn\nBHTkAe64AWC8LBVAumbKYPFPMc6QAg5UnSgFuhSQpSoTzE8jp0aVIm9rKOA0Yi9H\nNiUtk3Tj5l2sdQ/HpTCtjuHl+0E8T/tcSON1Z6WvoP26o14iU26b+JT6xlhSlUTN\nIaTmkiyu9SVygYRhkfFFsMfNHrLQuohfHPKF+OL1HWHQIxgZZ3jORVie//YKaRyf\npGkojUu2Jk9+QpaHz8Hjdd/s0ZuNNfXHKEe37fkBl7Cj5jKUEoBbD2LQw2nIa8fm\nUxetxtfz/Rf1Lnls3X/mZorfMDnHQyJgLCdE2sONPFRo+x0z5BXu6yWyFht3n3mE\nLcnL9Ax2JyrSAlqmEf1HODCgviVpxwQ0oHlQpt7XUVH51manU5Pnz2p538jGIeFb\ny2j4XTwIVuN9m7ibH3X5Xhcq7Ym+10EzJRdh6/Cx7KgVG2ljKrR52Be2Bq1G5QoU\nPz4ez3ZG7tySRGAfERxInb5WytkKM0BN6M52J1adz6+sKpcr1ozZfgHQX4YzwYiL\nhbTNWRGrN9TMJ5ypl/TUy+9NqFtdNsLjWLAda32BxZnylTpEsekE8JX+y3wf6Nt0\noQsEs2wQwQ9CJjjgfVhD\n=as8n\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e8ba6794c014fad06e8466ef5fec4c9888a12f33\nparent 1c6d358c60306aad2af0067dcca76f85f4deeba1\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1787002350 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787002350 -0400\n\nfix(code): hide empty previous-thread hints (#5552)\n\nOffering a way back to an empty thread is noise — it lands you somewhere\nno different from the new thread you already have.\n\n---\n\n`/clear` and a thread switch both offer a `Previous thread: <id> (Resume\nwith /threads -r)` hint. That hint was gated only on `thread_exists`,\nand registering a thread with the server writes a checkpoint row, so a\nthread you never typed into still looked resumable. Leaving a fresh\nthread — with `/threads -r`, another `/clear`, or an agent swap —\ntherefore pointed you back at nothing.\n\nResuming such a thread works; it just isn't worth suggesting. So the\nhint now also asks whether the thread recorded any server output — an\n`ASSISTANT`, `TOOL`, or `SKILL` message — and stays quiet when it\ndidn't. Every path that leaves a thread samples the message store\nthrough the new `_store_has_server_output` before clearing it, so the\nanswer describes the thread being left rather than the one arriving.\n\nThe question is \"did you do anything here\", not \"can this be resumed\". A\nthread holding only `/goal` or `/rubric set` state is resumable but\nstill unused, so it gets no hint either. Suppression logs at `info`, so\na missing hint is still visible in the Debug Console.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/e649f343-b71e-bb41-c988-9d422829699c)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-17T21:32:31Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0f5bd4f3356d0fcbdea436a27c8011629416a61c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0f5bd4f3356d0fcbdea436a27c8011629416a61c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0f5bd4f3356d0fcbdea436a27c8011629416a61c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"1c6d358c60306aad2af0067dcca76f85f4deeba1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1c6d358c60306aad2af0067dcca76f85f4deeba1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1c6d358c60306aad2af0067dcca76f85f4deeba1"}]},{"sha":"1c6d358c60306aad2af0067dcca76f85f4deeba1","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDFjNmQzNThjNjAzMDZhYWQyYWYwMDY3ZGNjYTc2Zjg1ZjRkZWViYTE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-17T20:37:13Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-17T20:37:13Z"},"message":"fix(code): scroll resumed threads to the bottom (#5543)\n\nResumed `dcode -r` threads now open at the newest message.\n\n---\n\nThe fixed-delay timer could fire independently of layout readiness. This\ndelegates to Textual's refresh-aware deferred `scroll_end` so it uses\nthe final scroll bounds while preserving one-shot behavior.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/90d415c8-1ef7-2d69-d735-88f3844c142d)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"9cde73f46d6745cce44cf18d99d51bf683de52c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9cde73f46d6745cce44cf18d99d51bf683de52c0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/1c6d358c60306aad2af0067dcca76f85f4deeba1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg3D5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9dAQAGP5lOSWlEomOta928VWsYgw\njRaAtsecqsk6M3KsbJzDVoFPICsiud5f/9FUb3HpMLv6XwcqB8Hh3Na6c/g3xR0r\n75UeFiWCM5oS7tMCkFf2q5ZO9W6sWYMv8xVZULZnMUIQ5hLgd9MgedqXSmRMjV77\ntPk+BY2NNTVRqasXQfhTfjR4wffaYxRI3vyALRurHC1MXMpIEJ7cTUvtrk0RIU1q\nZR48J9FwMlF6RMrI2fkxyreM6As8kkPzFzTdMyfsG5y7OA6vYW//5TDotLp3D2+G\n34kU5jS7+ghv+li9AHChKlIll2sQ3AaK4xfFYcP7c2buRDkJMaj5rnWeUXjqEK/0\nlBpT5PDEoqGtFPc6oROZUMStehTMGUNnKh/V4+xco30OgJOHOocr6UHxoa23Idi5\nSFr0UuAsoVyrNzPO3KmklLS5b8wxzphoM4oNe51kwu/xc6vnTzqyDynThF21E+YG\nJNf7ABZM+ROAWl35y1ACodzlFmozyz+WDeC6fcHh7ZsFTzznkFuQCHsOLrPH4UdQ\n1s986euIeDyjDv81s00j79KVT2000Woj8dPYlbpt6eqV3tHCeGw5+3gIAfRIjPmA\nnR2V3GFmei58j2FvLwQCuuyM32hmOTgTZeaswTpKW5zx+V1PbLb3+Z4G5fIAcBz9\nFwiLAnCWOjlo1MSmAMFj\n=d7xN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9cde73f46d6745cce44cf18d99d51bf683de52c0\nparent ed3b15f32a26033ca0b8395aebc26ca8cabb7e50\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786999033 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786999033 -0400\n\nfix(code): scroll resumed threads to the bottom (#5543)\n\nResumed `dcode -r` threads now open at the newest message.\n\n---\n\nThe fixed-delay timer could fire independently of layout readiness. This\ndelegates to Textual's refresh-aware deferred `scroll_end` so it uses\nthe final scroll bounds while preserving one-shot behavior.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/90d415c8-1ef7-2d69-d735-88f3844c142d)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-17T20:37:14Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1c6d358c60306aad2af0067dcca76f85f4deeba1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/1c6d358c60306aad2af0067dcca76f85f4deeba1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/1c6d358c60306aad2af0067dcca76f85f4deeba1/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ed3b15f32a26033ca0b8395aebc26ca8cabb7e50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ed3b15f32a26033ca0b8395aebc26ca8cabb7e50","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ed3b15f32a26033ca0b8395aebc26ca8cabb7e50"}]},{"sha":"ed3b15f32a26033ca0b8395aebc26ca8cabb7e50","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGVkM2IxNWYzMmEyNjAzM2NhMGI4Mzk1YWViYzI2Y2E4Y2FiYjdlNTA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-17T20:35:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-17T20:35:17Z"},"message":"style(code): keep highlighted `/model` rows readable (#5245)\n\nThe highlighted row in the model picker no longer shows amber or red\ntext on the colored highlight. The text now stays readable.\n\n| Before | After |\n| ------ | ----- |\n| <img width=\"245\" height=\"79\" alt=\"Screenshot\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f5d108f7-6e0d-46b7-8d41-cefb8355e4b3\"\n/> | <img width=\"241\" height=\"82\" alt=\"Screenshot\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b277a0cf-eac2-4a09-ada0-48da8ee7f292\"\n/> |\n\n---\n\nThe picker paints the highlighted row with the accent color as the\nbackground. But the row text kept its own color. Rows with missing\ncredentials were amber. Status tags like `(deprecated)` were red. Amber\ntext on the blue highlight is hard to read. This made the highlighted\nrow almost unreadable.\n\nNow, `_format_option_label` sets only the text weight for a highlighted\nrow. The stylesheet sets the color. Rows that are not highlighted keep\ntheir old colors. No information is lost: the provider header still\nshows `not installed` or the missing-credential state in words, and the\nstatus tag still shows its text.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/94fa2f44-dbb2-7d25-ac86-12cb429676eb)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"0f067df3c56047fc52678b3a15272aaae9be40e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/0f067df3c56047fc52678b3a15272aaae9be40e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ed3b15f32a26033ca0b8395aebc26ca8cabb7e50","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg3CFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+40QACJOcsHuSvmPVYksLhMafdPt\na3r7ZYR4L5pBpMmDsfQEwHjmHYCVQl3iqkFpOdNqsdd11SZFWcSlu98G72YLRtM6\nBDr/FQME5ohJeqQIz6KXZ9zMQR0neOaOI1dUYusy7klwyjse6INj6W0wHamJ67SC\naeVaovx/Rc4+aoNVMOxlhjziJjmhgDzrfOZf4TaPtiDKwYEHHw9xd/00W+cLVjNh\ncoRr3OsAdhmM0+ikUCGnfUXksnALrCQ9BfozETZbfLDnCAcWpV8+w7LvEzBhqIOZ\n0cr7W80IQcHLgP2MJ4QK2HAmUf0Nq79+JQav7lUDQYkm0IsIQHhi4AXVNi/JLCna\njurwSo3DaGexSuDA5C5UT+jJopWEdopXzLI2HOERJGEqR4bCHWB1YTbyx9uJ4iFI\n8HpSSLg2DFz3XPeX69NpOBHYnGHZNF/IeVOWPq8XlRDoYXDZwZey+wLdrYLFPjIE\nmHuYcZCKZyBMA6OJ2nA16ah7QaaSsq9RiFGIyTu0GLMcMEypW04hrcRHJ7omqisp\n12wWSSU04Lnu4gGJ8HuAGetY34wbTV0AUH4uoSN9z8I8XF2vunYOapAx7ZWX30ry\nHC1YTbDYaSl6ubAuzIUguWcGF9Tu3/mkDgJ+Q2BBoFGxRuzw/PGIWhDjUCxKjZiL\n6U+6Ggg6tIy8hCSsXqJD\n=cQJO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 0f067df3c56047fc52678b3a15272aaae9be40e8\nparent b16a74085af0057a24ce00f23a6a165bf5f21ed2\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786998917 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786998917 -0400\n\nstyle(code): keep highlighted `/model` rows readable (#5245)\n\nThe highlighted row in the model picker no longer shows amber or red\ntext on the colored highlight. The text now stays readable.\n\n| Before | After |\n| ------ | ----- |\n| <img width=\"245\" height=\"79\" alt=\"Screenshot\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f5d108f7-6e0d-46b7-8d41-cefb8355e4b3\"\n/> | <img width=\"241\" height=\"82\" alt=\"Screenshot\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b277a0cf-eac2-4a09-ada0-48da8ee7f292\"\n/> |\n\n---\n\nThe picker paints the highlighted row with the accent color as the\nbackground. But the row text kept its own color. Rows with missing\ncredentials were amber. Status tags like `(deprecated)` were red. Amber\ntext on the blue highlight is hard to read. This made the highlighted\nrow almost unreadable.\n\nNow, `_format_option_label` sets only the text weight for a highlighted\nrow. The stylesheet sets the color. Rows that are not highlighted keep\ntheir old colors. No information is lost: the provider header still\nshows `not installed` or the missing-credential state in words, and the\nstatus tag still shows its text.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/94fa2f44-dbb2-7d25-ac86-12cb429676eb)\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-17T20:35:17Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ed3b15f32a26033ca0b8395aebc26ca8cabb7e50","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ed3b15f32a26033ca0b8395aebc26ca8cabb7e50","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ed3b15f32a26033ca0b8395aebc26ca8cabb7e50/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b16a74085af0057a24ce00f23a6a165bf5f21ed2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b16a74085af0057a24ce00f23a6a165bf5f21ed2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b16a74085af0057a24ce00f23a6a165bf5f21ed2"}]},{"sha":"b16a74085af0057a24ce00f23a6a165bf5f21ed2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGIxNmE3NDA4NWFmMDA1N2EyNGNlMDBmMjNhNmExNjViZjVmMjFlZDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-17T20:20:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-17T20:20:35Z"},"message":"fix(code): report MCP server changes on reload (#5504)\n\n`/reload` now shows MCP server changes. It reports servers that loaded,\nservers that were removed, servers that failed to load, and servers that\nrecovered.\n\n---\n\nBefore, `/reload` did not report MCP server state. The command now\ncompares the MCP server list before and after the reload and shows the\ndifference to the user.\n\nThe report can include these lines:\n\n- `Loaded: <names>` — servers that were added and are ready to use.\n- `Removed: <names>` — servers that are no longer configured.\n- `Failed to load: <names>` — servers that are new or that moved to an\nerror state.\n- `Recovered: <names>` — servers that had an error before and are\nhealthy now.\n- `Status changed: <names>` — servers whose status changed in another\nway.\n- `Config errors: <names>` — configuration files that failed to parse.\n- `Resolved config errors: <names>` — configuration files that parse\nagain.\n\nWhen MCP is disabled with `--no-mcp`, the reload skips the MCP metadata\nrefresh and reports `MCP server changes: no changes detected.`\n\nWhen the reload cannot refresh the MCP metadata, the report says so and\ntells the user to run `/mcp` to check the state. When nothing changed\nbut some servers are still in an error state, the report says how many\nservers still need attention.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b184325b-d47e-8738-c911-35b71364fa80)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"e221ae976b07a92a75a09d574ed56920e98e2fbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/e221ae976b07a92a75a09d574ed56920e98e2fbc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b16a74085af0057a24ce00f23a6a165bf5f21ed2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqg20TCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZusQAHZKMNU60flnl+rsCwzoZrxb\nXHUUtQ5FAf/wCT5o/IavDRsGB6lThwsGcf4F7MDEP65l+E2Bhuf45QCL1gAx5NXZ\nDNJQzZmS/uasLag93dwNkHBZ9pLmz6Ypu5029Fq6X8KpCpunen4fB7l1RHJdMgDR\nEsVkxIrsR0NMzPXYsiKySSe8CD/wQEslRX2S1vxPl8GGt13BZgdoYkKWu8ebfYG+\n3dj4y9sQxIFPAvXT58/GNeviB4jjCrHAec3slwnvEAS2khxjCMpnQ+rO8mvSSUX0\n9uT8cSSU9foOLBCrdEaUOe+XSV5TPNAhd1dbk3JtBlM4wiTcVWmgpInme6BMdjnH\nCGH1DowOKVik5+5msiAL9dMC1bbf/XE77FVngD5argG0kIko0TcfP0p5CzxNmoYQ\nqQ+o8AKcCUyGl1XxxfiZ3Av81WhXvp2o9n47KlwJIJ36jm9AD1A2FSnx6fNaiYdx\nxf6vQWbkNDw8qRJWO4cwEiVvbiGje1ypJz6s8e4Glue0zc0tiiSzsTpV67aDIHQj\n9W9InMo08gt1JYMHG8pMV8VTrFfynYO0lTcdw1vwnsMubp8XLejMrcdzF7xdvEUi\nuWQSeccNGlDmzd2d5pPJsDm9MNhH8dZrlpLnJjyaFNp3s7pJJlDNuC87JMjnoPrJ\n550OJ23s7QMZQaNf97i+\n=dG6J\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree e221ae976b07a92a75a09d574ed56920e98e2fbc\nparent fcc019beb731d1f81aab66ba345ce432fbb1e3d9\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786998035 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786998035 -0400\n\nfix(code): report MCP server changes on reload (#5504)\n\n`/reload` now shows MCP server changes. It reports servers that loaded,\nservers that were removed, servers that failed to load, and servers that\nrecovered.\n\n---\n\nBefore, `/reload` did not report MCP server state. The command now\ncompares the MCP server list before and after the reload and shows the\ndifference to the user.\n\nThe report can include these lines:\n\n- `Loaded: <names>` — servers that were added and are ready to use.\n- `Removed: <names>` — servers that are no longer configured.\n- `Failed to load: <names>` — servers that are new or that moved to an\nerror state.\n- `Recovered: <names>` — servers that had an error before and are\nhealthy now.\n- `Status changed: <names>` — servers whose status changed in another\nway.\n- `Config errors: <names>` — configuration files that failed to parse.\n- `Resolved config errors: <names>` — configuration files that parse\nagain.\n\nWhen MCP is disabled with `--no-mcp`, the reload skips the MCP metadata\nrefresh and reports `MCP server changes: no changes detected.`\n\nWhen the reload cannot refresh the MCP metadata, the report says so and\ntells the user to run `/mcp` to check the state. When nothing changed\nbut some servers are still in an error state, the report says how many\nservers still need attention.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/b184325b-d47e-8738-c911-35b71364fa80)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-17T20:20:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b16a74085af0057a24ce00f23a6a165bf5f21ed2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b16a74085af0057a24ce00f23a6a165bf5f21ed2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b16a74085af0057a24ce00f23a6a165bf5f21ed2/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"