%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"e34b85de2fe55e30c3db2353736344d534ac434b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e34b85de2fe55e30c3db2353736344d534ac434b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e34b85de2fe55e30c3db2353736344d534ac434b"}]},{"sha":"e34b85de2fe55e30c3db2353736344d534ac434b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGUzNGI4NWRlMmZlNTVlMzBjM2RiMjM1MzczNjM0NGQ1MzRhYzQzNGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-17T05:58:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-17T05:58:03Z"},"message":"test(code): run CLI end-to-end tests asynchronously and de-flake exit teardown (#5518)\n\n## End-to-end tests follow the CLI's async path\n\nThe CLI never invokes its agent graph synchronously. Every production\nentrypoint streams — `app.py`, `tui/textual_adapter.py`,\n`client/non_interactive.py`, and `client/remote_client.py` all call\n`astream` — so the end-to-end tests in `test_end_to_end.py` were\nexercising a graph traversal no user reaches. They now `await\nagent.ainvoke(...)`, preserving the checkpointer, middleware stack,\nfake-model responses, and every existing assertion.\n\nA secondary benefit: the synchronous Pregel path runs on a bounded\n`ContextThreadPoolExecutor` sized from `max_concurrency`, which\noversubscribes under `pytest-xdist` and can present as a hang against\nthe suite's 30s global timeout. This is load-dependent and did not\nreproduce in isolation locally (8 runs at `-n 16`), so it is offered as\nmotivation rather than a diagnosis.\n\n`CLICompactionMiddleware.wrap_model_call` and `awrap_model_call` are\nseparately written parallel implementations, and the summarization\nend-to-end test was the only thing driving the synchronous one. To keep\nthat branch from drifting, `test_auto_compaction_runs_precompact_hook`\nnow parametrizes over sync and async in addition to the existing\noverflow axis, covering both twins directly at the unit level.\n\nFull-graph synchronous coverage is retained elsewhere on purpose:\n`test_reliable_rubric.py`, `test_goal_rubric.py`,\n`hooks/test_server_lifecycle.py`, and\n`smoke_tests/test_system_prompt.py` still use `invoke`, and\n`goal_rubric.py` and `reliable_rubric.py` each have genuine synchronous\ninvocation arms in production.\n\n## Unit tests no longer read the developer's hook config\n\nNine tests in `TestExitGracefulWorkerHandoff` fail on any machine whose\n`~/.deepagents/hooks.json` declares a `SessionEnd` handler, and pass\neverywhere else — including CI, where no such file exists.\n\n`hooks/loading.py` and `hooks/runtime.py` bind `DEFAULT_CONFIG_DIR` with\na `from` import at module import. Whether they observe the redirect\ninstalled by the existing `_isolate_price_overrides` fixture is\ntherefore an ordering accident: imported lazily inside a test they pick\nup `tmp_path`, but imported at collection — which a whole-suite run does\n— they keep the real user directory.\n\nOnce real hooks load, any app that finishes startup during a test has\nsession-end handlers, and `exit()` consults\n`self._hooks.has_handlers(SESSION_END)` and takes the deferred-teardown\nbranch. `super().exit()` is then never called synchronously, so the\nclass's synchronous-exit assertions fail. Because the tests race app\nstartup, this reads as load-dependent flakiness rather than a\nmachine-configuration dependency.\n\nA new autouse fixture rebinds both names to the same `tmp_path` the\nprice-override fixture uses, so all three agree on one user config\ndirectory, and drops the legacy loader's parse cache. `hooks/runtime.py`\ncarried the same latent bug without yet causing a visible failure.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Full `tests/unit_tests` suite: **12597 passed, 0 failed**, three\nconsecutive runs (two ordered, one randomized). Before: 9-12 failures\nper run, all in `test_app.py`, with a set that varied between runs.\n- Mechanism verified directly rather than inferred — same probe module,\nonly the fixture differing: `user_hooks_path()` resolves to\n`/Users/<dev>/.deepagents/hooks.json` without the fixture and to an\nempty `tmp_path` with it.\n- `offload_middleware.py` coverage across `test_compact_tool.py` +\n`test_end_to_end.py`: 82% → 89% (the whole synchronous `wrap_model_call`\nbody was uncovered before).\n- Mutation check: disabling the overflow gate in the synchronous branch\nfails exactly the new `[True-False]` case, confirming the\nparametrization is not vacuous.\n- `make format`, `make lint`, `make type`: clean.\n\n</details>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a763cf310c911a23eef14e20a83da20391ed2257","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a763cf310c911a23eef14e20a83da20391ed2257"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/e34b85de2fe55e30c3db2353736344d534ac434b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgqLrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/74QAIKRCJbtGe0DyQJsdMIWXMYc\nsrsni6P0Dk32U0eYvnPbc7MHiCdCh5EY7HPfndeuGNoQzFTKBybyZPbTc0/ogJ/Z\nhDPukeazi6ucTEDSJ0jsKDnO1ak1DJymaevkQM+3sHnVyG7JhWe+UQGXb5cqaP4r\nO7AtdCwitt8iI2Xzz0F/OPyoH+jSwhlEgM+SQc2ngYn52egh+kpNGhCVeyaDe34W\nO4zmpCWBRfpLohz/RbkWYHqygp3RDdPeNcnlcDr8Y3u6GEV0Xdkj51ei03GhpUGV\nmmgxTzfNcgdbhUC0Hr4v0ViIkNq4/YqstwasDaJP3WutjaLJT/EcbKSSlqW5lnPC\nxMscKM53l8zhIjIxMZrlNiG64+E3taaKLICxR0sjN9xaiHbaaaqQGb5glVrgm4v9\nJVXNSL4BuoIV7RDDR5GftT0PAZqQ0sd+VuJazKoLP7b5MUwaOcCteW8FAuQ0E+dF\nCTWODrT4jh+/zW497529jh7AwEOTh0KJ08HPzbJOZ0lNPxhJ0XK/+JASwtScOVp6\nDeinR12OsYP2x9uA7WuUHBqibtlATHizr4PoOFRDVUDgodcw/ssq5EleFoEpAUGy\nD5nz+7ZP3GQMWuPogG8YtWSxSeI66T5A3n3Wg6Sh8HrknxYxaWhBPDrA+fPZCRcL\n4qwRiy0/uGQo5cTTMawa\n=No8t\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a763cf310c911a23eef14e20a83da20391ed2257\nparent a84c557e2b6e54dd6c2669956bbc5c67fb7b20fd\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786946283 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786946283 -0400\n\ntest(code): run CLI end-to-end tests asynchronously and de-flake exit teardown (#5518)\n\n## End-to-end tests follow the CLI's async path\n\nThe CLI never invokes its agent graph synchronously. Every production\nentrypoint streams — `app.py`, `tui/textual_adapter.py`,\n`client/non_interactive.py`, and `client/remote_client.py` all call\n`astream` — so the end-to-end tests in `test_end_to_end.py` were\nexercising a graph traversal no user reaches. They now `await\nagent.ainvoke(...)`, preserving the checkpointer, middleware stack,\nfake-model responses, and every existing assertion.\n\nA secondary benefit: the synchronous Pregel path runs on a bounded\n`ContextThreadPoolExecutor` sized from `max_concurrency`, which\noversubscribes under `pytest-xdist` and can present as a hang against\nthe suite's 30s global timeout. This is load-dependent and did not\nreproduce in isolation locally (8 runs at `-n 16`), so it is offered as\nmotivation rather than a diagnosis.\n\n`CLICompactionMiddleware.wrap_model_call` and `awrap_model_call` are\nseparately written parallel implementations, and the summarization\nend-to-end test was the only thing driving the synchronous one. To keep\nthat branch from drifting, `test_auto_compaction_runs_precompact_hook`\nnow parametrizes over sync and async in addition to the existing\noverflow axis, covering both twins directly at the unit level.\n\nFull-graph synchronous coverage is retained elsewhere on purpose:\n`test_reliable_rubric.py`, `test_goal_rubric.py`,\n`hooks/test_server_lifecycle.py`, and\n`smoke_tests/test_system_prompt.py` still use `invoke`, and\n`goal_rubric.py` and `reliable_rubric.py` each have genuine synchronous\ninvocation arms in production.\n\n## Unit tests no longer read the developer's hook config\n\nNine tests in `TestExitGracefulWorkerHandoff` fail on any machine whose\n`~/.deepagents/hooks.json` declares a `SessionEnd` handler, and pass\neverywhere else — including CI, where no such file exists.\n\n`hooks/loading.py` and `hooks/runtime.py` bind `DEFAULT_CONFIG_DIR` with\na `from` import at module import. Whether they observe the redirect\ninstalled by the existing `_isolate_price_overrides` fixture is\ntherefore an ordering accident: imported lazily inside a test they pick\nup `tmp_path`, but imported at collection — which a whole-suite run does\n— they keep the real user directory.\n\nOnce real hooks load, any app that finishes startup during a test has\nsession-end handlers, and `exit()` consults\n`self._hooks.has_handlers(SESSION_END)` and takes the deferred-teardown\nbranch. `super().exit()` is then never called synchronously, so the\nclass's synchronous-exit assertions fail. Because the tests race app\nstartup, this reads as load-dependent flakiness rather than a\nmachine-configuration dependency.\n\nA new autouse fixture rebinds both names to the same `tmp_path` the\nprice-override fixture uses, so all three agree on one user config\ndirectory, and drops the legacy loader's parse cache. `hooks/runtime.py`\ncarried the same latent bug without yet causing a visible failure.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Test plan</summary>\n\n- Full `tests/unit_tests` suite: **12597 passed, 0 failed**, three\nconsecutive runs (two ordered, one randomized). Before: 9-12 failures\nper run, all in `test_app.py`, with a set that varied between runs.\n- Mechanism verified directly rather than inferred — same probe module,\nonly the fixture differing: `user_hooks_path()` resolves to\n`/Users/<dev>/.deepagents/hooks.json` without the fixture and to an\nempty `tmp_path` with it.\n- `offload_middleware.py` coverage across `test_compact_tool.py` +\n`test_end_to_end.py`: 82% → 89% (the whole synchronous `wrap_model_call`\nbody was uncovered before).\n- Mutation check: disabling the overflow gate in the synchronous branch\nfails exactly the new `[True-False]` case, confirming the\nparametrization is not vacuous.\n- `make format`, `make lint`, `make type`: clean.\n\n</details>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-17T05:58:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e34b85de2fe55e30c3db2353736344d534ac434b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/e34b85de2fe55e30c3db2353736344d534ac434b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/e34b85de2fe55e30c3db2353736344d534ac434b/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a84c557e2b6e54dd6c2669956bbc5c67fb7b20fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a84c557e2b6e54dd6c2669956bbc5c67fb7b20fd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a84c557e2b6e54dd6c2669956bbc5c67fb7b20fd"}]},{"sha":"a84c557e2b6e54dd6c2669956bbc5c67fb7b20fd","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGE4NGM1NTdlMmI2ZTU0ZGQ2YzI2Njk5NTZiYmM1YzY3ZmI3YjIwZmQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-17T05:48:03Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-17T05:48:03Z"},"message":"ci(infra): render `!keep-open` as a fenced block in the stale-PR warning (#5538)\n\nThe stale-PR warning comment now renders the keep-open command as its\nown fenced code block, so GitHub shows a copy button next to it — a\nmaintainer can copy the exact phrase instead of selecting it out of a\nsentence.\n\n---\n\nThe warning posted by `close-old-prs.js` previously ended with \"...or\ncomments `!keep-open`.\" inline. It now ends with \"...or comments:\"\nfollowed by:\n\n```\n!keep-open\n```\n\nOnly the warning body changes; the post-close message keeps its inline\nmention (no copy affordance needed once the PR is already closed), and\nthe `keep_open_on_comment.yml` trigger still matches the phrase anywhere\nin a comment body, so comments posted via the copy button work the same\nas before.","tree":{"sha":"b9dd87d3072c5e3e94508387f5c601ab2cd694d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/b9dd87d3072c5e3e94508387f5c601ab2cd694d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a84c557e2b6e54dd6c2669956bbc5c67fb7b20fd","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgqCTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEAkQAK/494F/Q1jz9BAGkvd+EEYz\ngg8cNBgITLuRi3bbMGPbrprKTXsYWS1p0pjFrMZFIkXxwISbQLLP6hAN+jhjV7Xz\nSWkRtQ3aYhu67LkxpaiK9RiclCQbAatfhE6miZKIJeSrHQWYtTJVZDccVOe4g0Om\n12lIeCkcBvnaJGAPrmnNL16RP6O2zW6eVi2rbBIbLVGtg5NFoIOObwC4zLu0loYq\nyBn+CTScc/jHqCfWBKrMS5NcO/QlOT1fQ140UHXD8bZOLt6k+LJ3ixkqJ6ftOYJD\nWf+88zGHf0JgcIJPGcbuoa9lwcQ4KRyyCX423Q8AMgR8t77dK0Xue3cJ0l+yJBWd\nUp2XAwcqLWXCWfVxt/zqLSC8XpxIrWViqdVefQK2rJdiARVGeU3k0qrWaD1h0bib\nHK46UOnAEQ/l1x/4gQckQ0qBrGj3WsaDEiiqKCQHr674R/7o3IFn6FuTas77xwpR\nq0xgOrVeysH/GuSKXiO9mID/XMNT9WxpMxfKEfvUDfFyM5/EuMS1ryAnJurLDwT4\nAhcptJmMyepIjrgZRVytA/686IVrl4ipfXY3eGHiOAPoSV1QrJd0HozTu5cNL1g4\nPUXTmIBvM31/s0aisxBcJs6K76V/AAv1+S4MSowNlRhSpaqX9SGd+gH3T+RWggKb\nib52LeMs6ETa9fpkIfE5\n=v0IV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree b9dd87d3072c5e3e94508387f5c601ab2cd694d7\nparent d01e4ac5bf36752e5c89c1c6645d486282cb611f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786945683 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786945683 -0400\n\nci(infra): render `!keep-open` as a fenced block in the stale-PR warning (#5538)\n\nThe stale-PR warning comment now renders the keep-open command as its\nown fenced code block, so GitHub shows a copy button next to it — a\nmaintainer can copy the exact phrase instead of selecting it out of a\nsentence.\n\n---\n\nThe warning posted by `close-old-prs.js` previously ended with \"...or\ncomments `!keep-open`.\" inline. It now ends with \"...or comments:\"\nfollowed by:\n\n```\n!keep-open\n```\n\nOnly the warning body changes; the post-close message keeps its inline\nmention (no copy affordance needed once the PR is already closed), and\nthe `keep_open_on_comment.yml` trigger still matches the phrase anywhere\nin a comment body, so comments posted via the copy button work the same\nas before.","verified_at":"2026-08-17T05:48:04Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a84c557e2b6e54dd6c2669956bbc5c67fb7b20fd","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a84c557e2b6e54dd6c2669956bbc5c67fb7b20fd","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a84c557e2b6e54dd6c2669956bbc5c67fb7b20fd/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"d01e4ac5bf36752e5c89c1c6645d486282cb611f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d01e4ac5bf36752e5c89c1c6645d486282cb611f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d01e4ac5bf36752e5c89c1c6645d486282cb611f"}]},{"sha":"d01e4ac5bf36752e5c89c1c6645d486282cb611f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGQwMWU0YWM1YmYzNjc1MmU1Yzg5YzFjNjY0NWQ0ODYyODJjYjYxMWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-15T08:10:36Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-15T08:10:36Z"},"message":"feat(code): resize chat input by dragging its top border (#5524)\n\nThe chat input can now be resized by dragging its highlighted top\nborder; double-clicking toggles between maximum and automatic sizing.\n\n---\n\nAn explicit inset handle makes mouse targeting reliable while preserving\ncorner colors, and only the interior rule highlights with the active\nmode color. Manual resizing remembers the requested height while\ntemporarily expanding to keep up to eight visual draft rows visible, so\ndeleting/backspacing lines retracts the composer again; screen and\nautocomplete space remain authoritative. Focused Textual interaction,\ncontent growth/retraction, hover, mode-color, geometry, scrollbar,\naction-button, autocomplete, and startup-tip tests cover the behavior.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/16618e76-ab37-1337-98ab-692ff2967371)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"04b29c8ffe32c27ad887a573eb167c3a283a0244","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/04b29c8ffe32c27ad887a573eb167c3a283a0244"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/d01e4ac5bf36752e5c89c1c6645d486282cb611f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqgB78CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKPkQAGEXx4bW/+t7jls1CkCyhu7Q\nR9h2ffNGMaS1YEv/FACkMB0RQuc42iQ/X7b/oh4QRR7H3eBXHouD4YksnaUVzmpc\nvs2/uKcHntVskP4MSxhJU48E6JV8Td325SURfuvHwqPu3xg0lfJQX+GHXpwjUTYJ\ntxnOCCMkkc12EFe87WqALbi0pI6Zo+y7cgw7DYuHnOIlhs2YNoIxfFdrBxAw5kcy\nc8rXgr+Kzw5M2y6URHv7hv+H58oLkC2057KtkMNeFjLbjMXzTOwqKeb4aQPjL+ED\nou53kDYC/nROWRFELnESnKsBzid/tOUHEALX+x8pAEUaRTJtk4/3wff/Wadx3fDI\n5jIKM7uUVOeep3OQ8E8gT/DQnLTUgCI3V7lNstpp4Ns34bE1UhGaaFvyoN/PHpFT\nLmRpqBkxCZXOCOQkb0wLWboajcJlTIYjy1S1aly9OOwbwAbds9XU/TnH2K6IVVBQ\no0CGK/yHx4A6p7wwJOgTEpDjJt/a6cL81EF1/vr/lQCRq52GeVFWehMLjlczCeY6\nXXqNFzS6IwRDrnqKBh632rn22CUJFAvq5FDUeu4oYhB4Aofaa1PdXW0YlCv9CH8T\nfueQGOIVSWQvf0bmyZ38oKombhZjTp3oz8c5Qjxaht/hhDDh2o9LjD+gR28HKJiy\nwWpSub6oUN0DtyUc6ICz\n=QsBz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 04b29c8ffe32c27ad887a573eb167c3a283a0244\nparent 0f75e2ec40d5356e8d123e24246cac4d34673438\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786781436 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786781436 -0700\n\nfeat(code): resize chat input by dragging its top border (#5524)\n\nThe chat input can now be resized by dragging its highlighted top\nborder; double-clicking toggles between maximum and automatic sizing.\n\n---\n\nAn explicit inset handle makes mouse targeting reliable while preserving\ncorner colors, and only the interior rule highlights with the active\nmode color. Manual resizing remembers the requested height while\ntemporarily expanding to keep up to eight visual draft rows visible, so\ndeleting/backspacing lines retracts the composer again; screen and\nautocomplete space remain authoritative. Focused Textual interaction,\ncontent growth/retraction, hover, mode-color, geometry, scrollbar,\naction-button, autocomplete, and startup-tip tests cover the behavior.\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/16618e76-ab37-1337-98ab-692ff2967371)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-15T08:10:37Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d01e4ac5bf36752e5c89c1c6645d486282cb611f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/d01e4ac5bf36752e5c89c1c6645d486282cb611f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/d01e4ac5bf36752e5c89c1c6645d486282cb611f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"0f75e2ec40d5356e8d123e24246cac4d34673438","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0f75e2ec40d5356e8d123e24246cac4d34673438","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0f75e2ec40d5356e8d123e24246cac4d34673438"}]},{"sha":"0f75e2ec40d5356e8d123e24246cac4d34673438","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDBmNzVlMmVjNDBkNTM1NmU4ZDEyM2UyNDI0NmNhYzRkMzQ2NzM0Mzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-14T20:38:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-14T20:38:20Z"},"message":"ci(infra): exempt PRs from auto-close via `!keep-open` comment (#5517)\n\nCommenting `!keep-open` on a PR now exempts it from the auto-close\nsweep, same as adding the `do-not-close` label — easier to fire off a\nquick comment than to open the label picker.\n\n---\n\nThe new `keep_open_on_comment.yml` workflow listens for `issue_comment:\ncreated` on PRs. When a MEMBER/OWNER/COLLABORATOR comments anything\ncontaining `!keep-open`, it reacts 👀, applies `do-not-close` via a\nshared `applyBypassLabel` helper, then reacts 🚀. Applying the label\nfires the `labeled` event, so the existing `clear_pending_deletion.yml`\nworkflow removes `pending-deletion` and minimizes the stale warning\ncomment — the end state is identical to adding the label by hand.\n\n- The actor gate is `author_association` rather than a user list, so\nanyone with triage access can use it and no one gains a power they\ndidn't already have. Bots and CONTRIBUTORs are excluded.\n- The match is a substring, not exact equality, so `still relevant —\n!keep-open` works. The `!` prefix keeps ordinary prose from accidentally\nexempting a PR.\n- Only `created` is handled: editing or deleting the comment later does\nnot remove the label, matching the label's own manual semantics.\n- The warning and close notices posted by the sweep now mention\n`!keep-open` alongside the label.","tree":{"sha":"6ac92387d15538931b7a09077b49d4ff666767bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6ac92387d15538931b7a09077b49d4ff666767bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/0f75e2ec40d5356e8d123e24246cac4d34673438","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqf3y8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0s8QAF6vKxaRQcp+Cm/F7tVIsdTj\nzG6NdYVc/3iqyn+CNRN5ZXqQzZtaYqvUeiQTyY0QOtQjb7yIICYVl06XjF3mFim6\nofXFr/5HeBhBhSBHF0YAOb469Zzr4jJPYxDz/5aVNMt6eJfQwkg/8UVeU1l/z6nH\nrZ+NBGkAhgDVQ8JGG7bCR4abCGB3bLK81sQSJ/r9KAyu6OhfAZfWjV4mCd4yPTXd\nh04CYUbV03Z6ja2wc7NQ9z2js0W14zNYasjmnInjWynFHMBYzCzlbhR2ZRGzAxgq\nF6dArBQtjvsbUUZbJWi/MKR01/bYFC5gHX7I9iIfcrWHQn+8U47fajQdR9GTTiqd\nJQxqSmgvgGrmX931KvvO4/186jML9j+3yH/umtvttwDfK9QcmX5PsAi3kfPriPcq\nw9X22UGOKEeQAdky7cjWikeN4lPKQZ+499W+6W6wXOe+BkHIQJmxcjqssugSqYJ9\nfvrqSWKjWeMnI388bxgt6Nokjezdjr3ATkyfSPNrMjWE/IBJI4aBNCox8Q+BVgmz\nBdpPmMp3us507x2/gKdvJ/wBSJsOi28RDI2qrECX/fjQSns6F2yViY0r4b4UQL8K\nzvSPHDIB5gu1g3ddqYtTT/OAideStTn0SERCdBNkcbaBiSJGyLU7wb53txlBpt12\nrWsHBOFXfw4RUREzQok9\n=P8a2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6ac92387d15538931b7a09077b49d4ff666767bb\nparent a38dc4297b225e424207df5efd7dec0cf38ce832\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786739900 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786739900 -0700\n\nci(infra): exempt PRs from auto-close via `!keep-open` comment (#5517)\n\nCommenting `!keep-open` on a PR now exempts it from the auto-close\nsweep, same as adding the `do-not-close` label — easier to fire off a\nquick comment than to open the label picker.\n\n---\n\nThe new `keep_open_on_comment.yml` workflow listens for `issue_comment:\ncreated` on PRs. When a MEMBER/OWNER/COLLABORATOR comments anything\ncontaining `!keep-open`, it reacts 👀, applies `do-not-close` via a\nshared `applyBypassLabel` helper, then reacts 🚀. Applying the label\nfires the `labeled` event, so the existing `clear_pending_deletion.yml`\nworkflow removes `pending-deletion` and minimizes the stale warning\ncomment — the end state is identical to adding the label by hand.\n\n- The actor gate is `author_association` rather than a user list, so\nanyone with triage access can use it and no one gains a power they\ndidn't already have. Bots and CONTRIBUTORs are excluded.\n- The match is a substring, not exact equality, so `still relevant —\n!keep-open` works. The `!` prefix keeps ordinary prose from accidentally\nexempting a PR.\n- Only `created` is handled: editing or deleting the comment later does\nnot remove the label, matching the label's own manual semantics.\n- The warning and close notices posted by the sweep now mention\n`!keep-open` alongside the label.","verified_at":"2026-08-14T20:38:21Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0f75e2ec40d5356e8d123e24246cac4d34673438","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/0f75e2ec40d5356e8d123e24246cac4d34673438","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/0f75e2ec40d5356e8d123e24246cac4d34673438/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type"