rl":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b28cee439b9f41f954689168250b044e71b8e855"}]},{"sha":"b28cee439b9f41f954689168250b044e71b8e855","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGIyOGNlZTQzOWI5ZjQxZjk1NDY4OTE2ODI1MGIwNDRlNzFiOGU4NTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-13T18:54:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-13T18:54:56Z"},"message":"ci(infra): surface the minimums PR link in the job summary (#5487)\n\nThe \"Raise dependency minimums\" job summary now shows the link to the PR\nit opened (or the one already open) instead of only emitting it as a\n`::notice::` annotation in the step logs.\n\n---\n\nThe workflow previously surfaced the PR URL exclusively through\n`::notice::` annotations, which GitHub renders collapsed under the job's\nannotation list — from a run's summary page there was no way to see\nwhich PR a run opened without expanding step logs (e.g. run 31730870363\nopened #5481, invisible from the summary).\n\nThe `**PR:**` line is appended on all three outcomes: PR opened, PR\nalready open for the branch (no duplicate created), and nothing to raise\n(states that no PR was opened, so the summary always reflects the\noutcome).","tree":{"sha":"056b1f2a69b019263a97e3c5e07697a72516c62a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/056b1f2a69b019263a97e3c5e07697a72516c62a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b28cee439b9f41f954689168250b044e71b8e855","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfhMACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8rcQAGEaVGk+9RZXo9mbY1Ex0yzj\nv+azy0j/2N/v/Y0jmjsXm6gFsk3drrzCkd8B5eXb9rLyKwRHIbE38wPIncd1JwuX\nlPCdvhKkwiishA9TXKRUu569lflWLlL7TEsbE/7JlQE5FdlqzWL3pNN0hTAzBMHx\nlrCjHOiY8enf53a/j+FMkKdH+MrQARb0RELT3IAl7V3JXwxD/f3K4+N2EB+KPcP+\nCS86dT6GRHEczwXxuyO7hXeCXk3ymcui5FSjixoG5mc9dVFbego5eJIFs0KIbWHk\nAdvvfgwhzWeygmRHBZr0RU9IBV5XrthzG+oGQ0WpSEJ9LgLQzfym55bAkVEVnBKD\neI1Fn7W7/6iHB6qVJRRPC1kOLg/p5+GLDdsSgbIAMW5LFofKvs7dQWigaSTpc4TD\nbpjtLY+CAu9ZXOgQSYVEqp5PzMc1APSViPgt/lXSQcUotMBX2ZkIkwIDZ9FE/YUF\nzvCVlq7cW7P7UKRRvO9C2bkFA4uq8wxPbZGr8YJjKpqnbNBuihsZW3tLeWoiJs7D\nxOLkS1UsPkQgca+APV4fvTCZxPJaIZNIhADwfcPbcNiVLNd1ilpRqBAbCoCWlHdL\nKwE2CHElkEUdQJOI95eeGo+jQ8VEMPoPeNY2r4iGaHAfCLtI9abdAnJw8eVT1Nxq\n75P3N78EheOG158FrLew\n=zPP0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 056b1f2a69b019263a97e3c5e07697a72516c62a\nparent 8270dec30c849b12c880802abd6e67781b1953ce\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786647296 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786647296 -0700\n\nci(infra): surface the minimums PR link in the job summary (#5487)\n\nThe \"Raise dependency minimums\" job summary now shows the link to the PR\nit opened (or the one already open) instead of only emitting it as a\n`::notice::` annotation in the step logs.\n\n---\n\nThe workflow previously surfaced the PR URL exclusively through\n`::notice::` annotations, which GitHub renders collapsed under the job's\nannotation list — from a run's summary page there was no way to see\nwhich PR a run opened without expanding step logs (e.g. run 31730870363\nopened #5481, invisible from the summary).\n\nThe `**PR:**` line is appended on all three outcomes: PR opened, PR\nalready open for the branch (no duplicate created), and nothing to raise\n(states that no PR was opened, so the summary always reflects the\noutcome).","verified_at":"2026-08-13T18:55:00Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b28cee439b9f41f954689168250b044e71b8e855","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b28cee439b9f41f954689168250b044e71b8e855","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b28cee439b9f41f954689168250b044e71b8e855/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"8270dec30c849b12c880802abd6e67781b1953ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8270dec30c849b12c880802abd6e67781b1953ce","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8270dec30c849b12c880802abd6e67781b1953ce"}]},{"sha":"8270dec30c849b12c880802abd6e67781b1953ce","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDgyNzBkZWMzMGM4NDliMTJjODgwODAyYWJkNmU2Nzc4MWIxOTUzY2U","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-13T18:40:07Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-13T18:40:07Z"},"message":"ci(infra): annotate `bump_code_sdk_pin.yml` runs when the pin is already current (#5483)\n\nThe `bump_code_sdk_pin.yml` workflow now adds a run annotation when the\nCode pin is current. Example: \"Nothing to do: Code SDK pin 0.7.5 is not\nbehind the workspace SDK version 0.7.5.\" Before this change, the\nworkflow wrote only a line in the step log.\n\n---\n\nSee https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/31730874462\nfor an example of the problem. On that run, the run summary page did not\nshow the result. It was necessary to open the job log to see why the\nworkflow did not open a PR. The workflow already adds annotations for\nits other results (`::notice::` for \"PR already exists\" and \"Opened\nPR\"). This change makes the skip path do the same.","tree":{"sha":"09fa5a8858931396521d56f0a55f733c777c3166","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/09fa5a8858931396521d56f0a55f733c777c3166"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8270dec30c849b12c880802abd6e67781b1953ce","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfg+HCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANCEQAFEMqqMLa8FVWT74aQvcEjLO\nu1Z7odokvBqrJmyz+FGxW+bp1ir6IpYV1zds7xyjBE2CqY5Zp9GehxSM9mcdp7OG\nmk2n3w4KqR2U+oPAsCXArQ9eLeXQwnk7Nhm0OUSq8RljOmyCBvXg5iFeuJS4InSM\nEzFGpu/oNwnI5+8nghj3qQEo4BXYsGybvpYsbvdHHoyA/T+e9uqkBwc2TnbZi/2I\nuCAbVjk7bueeC+x2ZAT1PeTK+QdfKZxaUWaAYKohfa7HKVEipg9QpJgExax0b0Ae\naK0IB+r69s2zBl28WbDxLkJX9PQamLtf2D1VIPOx8QjY9l+r0katCaBDdTtrWEGb\nbKM8vTusKIKHWPDkrie7buAd69R5FeDW3gV++kiEzCTC2dcUJZfMhiDzOpWCYaxz\nli5213CPCGPo0S4kVLG7Nvdw86B0gVZjaoKDjB2XlrIJKZ7QeWjoYYqURYvEKe0t\nov8YYU2ur7K8vT1KdAl2d9xGrE5eWIwtqF3VpaEz4NAb4h1240cbFwAEw5OXSbOm\n26WRz1ZD8D83CRW1ed9tQLzkbOX62FNJeRwFFXOJUm+/VsozqKIgFoL3aPzeuXG5\nF41kxD3x6e5NyohAPaq/SKnWAENNi5KVnkB8DHpZid8CzoaS36h31GaYnQ5Pt1LU\n7Oeui6O0v/9+m8xWgHDx\n=LfEi\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 09fa5a8858931396521d56f0a55f733c777c3166\nparent f7cd46c92cae36bc219cd4a87a5e93b3fe68e187\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786646407 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786646407 -0700\n\nci(infra): annotate `bump_code_sdk_pin.yml` runs when the pin is already current (#5483)\n\nThe `bump_code_sdk_pin.yml` workflow now adds a run annotation when the\nCode pin is current. Example: \"Nothing to do: Code SDK pin 0.7.5 is not\nbehind the workspace SDK version 0.7.5.\" Before this change, the\nworkflow wrote only a line in the step log.\n\n---\n\nSee https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/31730874462\nfor an example of the problem. On that run, the run summary page did not\nshow the result. It was necessary to open the job log to see why the\nworkflow did not open a PR. The workflow already adds annotations for\nits other results (`::notice::` for \"PR already exists\" and \"Opened\nPR\"). This change makes the skip path do the same.","verified_at":"2026-08-13T18:40:11Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8270dec30c849b12c880802abd6e67781b1953ce","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8270dec30c849b12c880802abd6e67781b1953ce","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8270dec30c849b12c880802abd6e67781b1953ce/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f7cd46c92cae36bc219cd4a87a5e93b3fe68e187","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f7cd46c92cae36bc219cd4a87a5e93b3fe68e187","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f7cd46c92cae36bc219cd4a87a5e93b3fe68e187"}]},{"sha":"f7cd46c92cae36bc219cd4a87a5e93b3fe68e187","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGY3Y2Q0NmM5MmNhZTM2YmMyMTljZDRhODdhNWU5M2IzZmU2OGUxODc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-13T18:39:35Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-13T18:39:35Z"},"message":"ci(infra): backtick package name and tabulate minimums PR body (#5485)\n\nPRs opened by `raise_langchain_minimums.yml` get titles like\n``chore(deps): raise dependency minimums for `deepagents-code` ``\ninstead of the package name in plain text, and the list of raised bounds\nin the body becomes a Manifest / Dependency / Change table instead of\nbullets.\n\n---\n\nTwo readability fixes to the automated dependency-minimums PRs, e.g.\n#5481:\n\n- The package name in the title (and the workflow's commit message) was\nthe only identifier not wrapped in backticks — the PR body, workflow\ncomments, and our title conventions all put named entities in backticks.\nThe title now reads ``... for `deepagents-code` ``.\n- With several raised bounds in one run, the bullet format buried the\nactual old → new specifier change at the end of a long line led by the\nmanifest path. Rendered as a table:\n\n  | Manifest | Dependency | Change |\n  |---|---|---|\n| `libs/code/pyproject.toml` | `langchain` | `langchain>=1.3.14,<2.0.0`\n→ `langchain>=1.3.15,<2.0.0` |\n| `libs/code/pyproject.toml` | `langsmith` |\n`langsmith[sandbox]>=0.10.10` → `langsmith[sandbox]>=0.10.18` |\n\nThe title change is cosmetic only — `chore(deps):` parsing by\nrelease-please and the PR title lint are unaffected. #5481's title was\nalready edited in place; the table format applies to the next scheduled\nrun.","tree":{"sha":"3a0c5d128876d3e34cb55dbd306dff42391428f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/3a0c5d128876d3e34cb55dbd306dff42391428f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f7cd46c92cae36bc219cd4a87a5e93b3fe68e187","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfg9nCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAr5YQABxBtOBvFiTdlEhiJWrCL9zK\nMBfd0VuE35Vd2m/2rvOihohsVJvpOsGX9zAy72Jbzxyn1NZlBkpbZG5BLpJJTEwh\ndNFvR/x+PjA+V4rADIKHEzjGnU/UQKQE7MGUcnfd3ETmCXrPmdgEqP1x3oCLHDJa\nkDt14TXnmhL7BgGPEf3+aexw5pgXxxDx7jYit2EVLEfdnlayLgSEL/726syMz05d\n8aHFSqEaUp7RdQIc4lOoPr65i56f8t4uwk1gPbM9eYw4YZs0+ObIHfNY/Mg8gl4W\nW/9sWvRXla/V5YGhzisyG/wIUChL1wk96LrSrs0K9At9qYsi46CNXMObMuQUggVc\nwSyhD13pYFigaNSi9WYlBQukFLW0fLvNDgCVt/8qgROXDMSTpHU02YjqwJnlehOP\npUr0SA0elKRLcAkgc0Ct0BbkgHLSWML9zkZ/hrDxfZmgvhldXPHimBFOoi4zUI4j\nIJ1K7ktE9Uk6bKrqXA58ljlgNjm0RooaheOOtNakw1JVnaG7JYjAMqNe9nrGiScN\nhUs6QmWyqrsdUH4tijpPuUF03C4YjH7mz9mO0WDJGONstcSSGLPLzZ3u12qFWUck\n++hA7hn9E26Q64W8GuwbjvPQ2iGL25Q1O8g3SEqdVziTeNZVjUthL35qq+JfaPhI\nFVFGWzcyTLsKk7P8AWIb\n=/dRT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3a0c5d128876d3e34cb55dbd306dff42391428f6\nparent 2d3ec5410db5953a21863ae6bc9ab43bd2607489\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786646375 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786646375 -0700\n\nci(infra): backtick package name and tabulate minimums PR body (#5485)\n\nPRs opened by `raise_langchain_minimums.yml` get titles like\n``chore(deps): raise dependency minimums for `deepagents-code` ``\ninstead of the package name in plain text, and the list of raised bounds\nin the body becomes a Manifest / Dependency / Change table instead of\nbullets.\n\n---\n\nTwo readability fixes to the automated dependency-minimums PRs, e.g.\n#5481:\n\n- The package name in the title (and the workflow's commit message) was\nthe only identifier not wrapped in backticks — the PR body, workflow\ncomments, and our title conventions all put named entities in backticks.\nThe title now reads ``... for `deepagents-code` ``.\n- With several raised bounds in one run, the bullet format buried the\nactual old → new specifier change at the end of a long line led by the\nmanifest path. Rendered as a table:\n\n  | Manifest | Dependency | Change |\n  |---|---|---|\n| `libs/code/pyproject.toml` | `langchain` | `langchain>=1.3.14,<2.0.0`\n→ `langchain>=1.3.15,<2.0.0` |\n| `libs/code/pyproject.toml` | `langsmith` |\n`langsmith[sandbox]>=0.10.10` → `langsmith[sandbox]>=0.10.18` |\n\nThe title change is cosmetic only — `chore(deps):` parsing by\nrelease-please and the PR title lint are unaffected. #5481's title was\nalready edited in place; the table format applies to the next scheduled\nrun.","verified_at":"2026-08-13T18:39:41Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f7cd46c92cae36bc219cd4a87a5e93b3fe68e187","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f7cd46c92cae36bc219cd4a87a5e93b3fe68e187","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f7cd46c92cae36bc219cd4a87a5e93b3fe68e187/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2d3ec5410db5953a21863ae6bc9ab43bd2607489","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2d3ec5410db5953a21863ae6bc9ab43bd2607489","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2d3ec5410db5953a21863ae6bc9ab43bd2607489"}]},{"sha":"2d3ec5410db5953a21863ae6bc9ab43bd2607489","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDJkM2VjNTQxMGRiNTk1M2EyMTg2M2FlNmJjOWFiNDNiZDI2MDc0ODk","commit":{"author":{"name":"langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]","email":"248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-13T18:34:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-13T18:34:32Z"},"message":"chore(deps): raise dependency minimums for `deepagents-code` (#5481)\n\nRaises the LangChain-ecosystem dependency lower bounds (`langchain*`,\n`langgraph*`, `langsmith*`, `deepagents*`) for `deepagents-code` to the\nlatest compatible stable PyPI release, and regenerates every affected\n`uv.lock`. Upper bounds, extras, and markers are preserved; exact `==`\npins are left alone.\n\nRaised 8 minimum(s):\n\n- `libs/code/pyproject.toml`: `langchain` `langchain>=1.3.14,<2.0.0` →\n`langchain>=1.3.15,<2.0.0`\n- `libs/code/pyproject.toml`: `langgraph-runtime-inmem`\n`langgraph-runtime-inmem>=0.31.1,<1.0.0` →\n`langgraph-runtime-inmem>=0.32.4,<1.0.0`\n- `libs/code/pyproject.toml`: `langchain-anthropic`\n`langchain-anthropic>=1.5.4,<2.0.0` →\n`langchain-anthropic>=1.5.6,<2.0.0`\n- `libs/code/pyproject.toml`: `langchain-google-genai`\n`langchain-google-genai>=4.3.2,<5.0.0` →\n`langchain-google-genai>=4.3.3,<5.0.0`\n- `libs/code/pyproject.toml`: `langchain-openai`\n`langchain-openai>=1.4.1,<2.0.0` → `langchain-openai>=1.5.0,<2.0.0`\n- `libs/code/pyproject.toml`: `langsmith` `langsmith[sandbox]>=0.10.10`\n→ `langsmith[sandbox]>=0.10.18`\n- `libs/code/pyproject.toml`: `langchain-mcp-adapters`\n`langchain-mcp-adapters>=0.3.0,<1.0.0` →\n`langchain-mcp-adapters>=0.3.2,<1.0.0`\n- `libs/code/pyproject.toml`: `langchain-aws`\n`langchain-aws>=1.6.3,<2.0.0` → `langchain-aws>=1.7.0,<2.0.0`\n\nOpened automatically by `raise_langchain_minimums.yml`. Review the\nraised bounds against any compatibility notes in the manifest comments\nbefore merging.\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"501e196bd5cd4be10aa558bdd29e346b2ab14c9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/501e196bd5cd4be10aa558bdd29e346b2ab14c9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2d3ec5410db5953a21863ae6bc9ab43bd2607489","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfg44CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5G4QAF0ugsgstk3cKW4ExP7DgOkW\nIPYDQsQ2hOmTActJDPDH6VNQOfjY8fSvtQYxDxR6RbsBjAPYEaE6GiNEdP42S7yt\ncPzRaDPqdd/kgkQNEvr6g6FDF108OyDL5OuK+9JWHNsS197g5P6Byph9OcX54URC\nxooAUsgdla3NvnEIGe+D4riIUVnIEyuBMCMzDjOH+WuW6sYvV1o2jnSoQuZCY1aC\ncAkVhIv0f5D3UndGDNlXwcTWt7krFmqCBNJb2AqL3gcB4DoZcQb7OOqyBUv4hSI1\n6fMrVxk10KqGE7S3qQGHwDtSs5n12elolhZzTPHR0ic1yPcalcceWoujZQeAOxIB\niJY+dazxFE8hhy9rc5GbsfSVqCPolkyBcrAy8R6vOFpdS2SvL2hPA4UJze779tt1\nK+hRzfFBbcu3RoM+tbVjBFOOjOSh9Qbh/6kTecEfqDUmej9VxHZk7h82+YysATPA\niHqrTO1gK8bne2OcVpH3tz869Ol6cFLxZHsJG4HpvrmVgqKIK5optQi39P6RcnLW\ncfs0/Xtu44UdIl8nQJSaoqIFe/ccLtZXkvHkDqDw0NTDy1e0G9nQa4bmT6YLM98F\nH1HtvHMvRrhIfHgGce+Q+gzMcwol5E5z5wdSho7ITgC+p8DFTozdh6pR8JM4wUK5\n+CB74N1KtqrL+Tv298b+\n=fIDr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 501e196bd5cd4be10aa558bdd29e346b2ab14c9e\nparent a9852f5e5e11fcb1324258c23ce56f1e45cfb748\nauthor langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1786646072 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786646072 -0700\n\nchore(deps): raise dependency minimums for `deepagents-code` (#5481)\n\nRaises the LangChain-ecosystem dependency lower bounds (`langchain*`,\n`langgraph*`, `langsmith*`, `deepagents*`) for `deepagents-code` to the\nlatest compatible stable PyPI release, and regenerates every affected\n`uv.lock`. Upper bounds, extras, and markers are preserved; exact `==`\npins are left alone.\n\nRaised 8 minimum(s):\n\n- `libs/code/pyproject.toml`: `langchain` `langchain>=1.3.14,<2.0.0` →\n`langchain>=1.3.15,<2.0.0`\n- `libs/code/pyproject.toml`: `langgraph-runtime-inmem`\n`langgraph-runtime-inmem>=0.31.1,<1.0.0` →\n`langgraph-runtime-inmem>=0.32.4,<1.0.0`\n- `libs/code/pyproject.toml`: `langchain-anthropic`\n`langchain-anthropic>=1.5.4,<2.0.0` →\n`langchain-anthropic>=1.5.6,<2.0.0`\n- `libs/code/pyproject.toml`: `langchain-google-genai`\n`langchain-google-genai>=4.3.2,<5.0.0` →\n`langchain-google-genai>=4.3.3,<5.0.0`\n- `libs/code/pyproject.toml`: `langchain-openai`\n`langchain-openai>=1.4.1,<2.0.0` → `langchain-openai>=1.5.0,<2.0.0`\n- `libs/code/pyproject.toml`: `langsmith` `langsmith[sandbox]>=0.10.10`\n→ `langsmith[sandbox]>=0.10.18`\n- `libs/code/pyproject.toml`: `langchain-mcp-adapters`\n`langchain-mcp-adapters>=0.3.0,<1.0.0` →\n`langchain-mcp-adapters>=0.3.2,<1.0.0`\n- `libs/code/pyproject.toml`: `langchain-aws`\n`langchain-aws>=1.6.3,<2.0.0` → `langchain-aws>=1.7.0,<2.0.0`\n\nOpened automatically by `raise_langchain_minimums.yml`. Review the\nraised bounds against any compatibility notes in the manifest comments\nbefore merging.\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-13T18:34:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2d3ec5410db5953a21863ae6bc9ab43bd2607489","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2d3ec5410db5953a21863ae6bc9ab43bd2607489","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2d3ec5410db5953a21863ae6bc9ab43bd2607489/comments","author":{"login":"langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]","id":248757908,"node_id":"BOT_kgDODtO-lA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2441712?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/langchain-oss-automated-triage","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"a9852f5e5e11fcb1324258c23ce56f1e45cfb748","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a9852f5e5e11fcb1324258c23ce56f1e45cfb748","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a9852f5e5e11fcb1324258c23ce56f1e45cfb748"}]},{"sha":"a9852f5e5e11fcb1324258c23ce56f1e45cfb748","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGE5ODUyZjVlNWUxMWZjYjEzMjQyNThjMjNjZTU2ZjFlNDVjZmI3NDg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-13T18:32:25Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-13T18:32:25Z"},"message":"chore(infra): raise `genai-prices` manifest floor in daily bump and shorten PR body (#5478)\n\nThe daily `genai-prices` bump workflow now updates the `>=` minimum in\n`libs/code/pyproject.toml` to the resolved version. Before this change,\nthe workflow moved only the lockfile pin. The automatic PR body is now:\n\n    Bumps `genai-prices` from `X.Y.Z` to `A.B.C`.\n\n    Opened automatically by `bump_genai_prices.yml`.\n\n---\n\nThe minimum must stay current. If it does not, fresh installs can still\nselect old releases, and the pin cannot protect them from an old parser.\nAfter `uv lock` resolves, the workflow rewrites the minimum with `sed`.\nThe push step stages `pyproject.toml` and `uv.lock`. The skip check\ncompares both files.\n\nA pin that does not move is not sufficient for \"no work to do\". If the\nmanifest minimum is behind the pin, the run counts as stale. Without\nthis, the first run would discard the rewritten minimum and repeat the\nsame no-op each day.\n\nThe version-format check now runs before the `sed`. A bad `read_pin`\nvalue stops the job instead of corrupting the manifest.\n\nThe workflow now checks PyPI for the newest release that is not yanked.\nIf the pin is current but PyPI has a newer release, the declared ceiling\nprevents the bump. The workflow files one tracking issue for this\ncondition and adds comments to it on later runs.\n\nThe shorter body (langchain-ai/deepagents#5476 shows the old body)\nremoves the phrase \"newest version permitted by the range\". That phrase\nis not correct after the minimum moves.","tree":{"sha":"2b6ba2c7b48658e868b531a9a769723e4e170250","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/2b6ba2c7b48658e868b531a9a769723e4e170250"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/a9852f5e5e11fcb1324258c23ce56f1e45cfb748","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfg25CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6dgQAKy14aAwREZeAUOTBX7oT/lA\nSe8ixvqNA7SJRIPb3z1V0rTJ4IIH/zA1rBN6xU+h1HiK39j6d9WPgdO9zbQWL5+q\neTZYdMayn5hRmcZT0Uo9YX4JhiE26f5OX0+nrMwqU9axGDla6B8S016tceVi2yzO\nNbdGx8I+K3H3zcrkfStv1RNkr2rd8YlFUH8cj2i2YiVRadBtxAN48aHlK5B+Zsaq\nv8YRY0RwYdsENv+JmkCc+smC26b87dsPA0msjH7Eidd7hoJm5jKGYRQ6itUXCeb5\nE8kLWV9V9/ibvQ81qBYmOck3mxBBlUMp+b5d18BXfKqd5WCGRvNvQ2sMkCkmVu7I\nSUDGSBkSLxPu1sx4jEmh9tq6gknOtlE2TCuYalflEjd6MQO5j8rEYjrriaJZ28a+\nuGMsyFAALSpt9XxeS3XzFdGxPb97wLY9jqxCLVLOzoxm2OyaUNART1Ot0j7/Cvfq\nA/aH0sSo7vGanPss5EH9fcoYUJmJxQcJPsGVRfxEvawc+vjn2l7L7/12zqAsBZ2I\ns+BrdgvAgN4S3tMsAU7fbkISsm60n70du58j54Pcme4pY6aJ6zHqxJtUNv6TGi4p\nemRMyCWtmJgZ9AQGXQWrYvjGeFTwwc7pSizrWwfL9v0VGRLedtpjja/nmCAcBOjO\nUDThm69MjR12BGQhj086\n=qmhI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 2b6ba2c7b48658e868b531a9a769723e4e170250\nparent b0f0a465d7f847323340c5974973db30ade538a2\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786645945 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786645945 -0700\n\nchore(infra): raise `genai-prices` manifest floor in daily bump and shorten PR body (#5478)\n\nThe daily `genai-prices` bump workflow now updates the `>=` minimum in\n`libs/code/pyproject.toml` to the resolved version. Before this change,\nthe workflow moved only the lockfile pin. The automatic PR body is now:\n\n    Bumps `genai-prices` from `X.Y.Z` to `A.B.C`.\n\n    Opened automatically by `bump_genai_prices.yml`.\n\n---\n\nThe minimum must stay current. If it does not, fresh installs can still\nselect old releases, and the pin cannot protect them from an old parser.\nAfter `uv lock` resolves, the workflow rewrites the minimum with `sed`.\nThe push step stages `pyproject.toml` and `uv.lock`. The skip check\ncompares both files.\n\nA pin that does not move is not sufficient for \"no work to do\". If the\nmanifest minimum is behind the pin, the run counts as stale. Without\nthis, the first run would discard the rewritten minimum and repeat the\nsame no-op each day.\n\nThe version-format check now runs before the `sed`. A bad `read_pin`\nvalue stops the job instead of corrupting the manifest.\n\nThe workflow now checks PyPI for the newest release that is not yanked.\nIf the pin is current but PyPI has a newer release, the declared ceiling\nprevents the bump. The workflow files one tracking issue for this\ncondition and adds comments to it on later runs.\n\nThe shorter body (langchain-ai/deepagents#5476 shows the old body)\nremoves the phrase \"newest version permitted by the range\". That phrase\nis not correct after the minimum moves.","verified_at":"2026-08-13T18:32:29Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a9852f5e5e11fcb1324258c23ce56f1e45cfb748","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/a9852f5e5e11fcb1324258c23ce56f1e45cfb748","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/a9852f5e5e11fcb1324258c23ce56f1e45cfb748/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b0f0a465d7f847323340c5974973db30ade538a2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b0f0a465d7f847323340c5974973db30ade538a2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b0f0a465d7f847323340c5974973db30ade538a2"}]},{"sha":"b0f0a465d7f847323340c5974973db30ade538a2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGIwZjBhNDY1ZDdmODQ3MzIzMzQwYzU5NzQ5NzNkYjMwYWRlNTM4YTI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-13T18:27:39Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-13T18:27:39Z"},"message":"fix(infra): authenticate app-token pushes in minimums and SDK pin workflows (#5480)\n\nThe dependency minimums and Code SDK pin workflows can push branches and\nopen PRs again. Before this change, both workflows failed with\n`Permission to langchain-ai/deepagents.git denied to\ngithub-actions[bot]`. The pushes now authenticate as the Org Membership\nApp installation. If the app token is empty, the step stops with a clear\nerror message. A failure in either workflow also files a tracking issue,\nor updates the existing one. This matches the genai-prices bump\nworkflow.\n\n---\n\n## Cause\n\nThis is the same bug that #5474 fixed in `bump_genai_prices.yml`.\n\nThe push step puts the app token in the push URL\n(`https://x-access-token:${GH_TOKEN}@github.com/...`). But\n`actions/checkout` ran first with the default `persist-credentials:\ntrue`. This stores the read-only `GITHUB_TOKEN` as an\n`http.https://github.com/.extraheader` credential. git cannot send two\n`Authorization` headers in one request. The credential in the config\nwins. git drops the app token from the URL. The push runs as\n`github-actions[bot]`. That token has only `contents: read` in these\njobs. GitHub denies the push with a 403. The error names\n`github-actions[bot]`, not the app bot.\n\nObserved failures:\n\n- `raise_langchain_minimums.yml`, run 31374913489. The job raised 18\nminimums and committed them. Then the push failed with a 403.\n- `bump_code_sdk_pin.yml`, run 30938354665. Listed in the #5474\ninvestigation.\n\n## Fix\n\nThe changes match #5474 in both workflows:\n\n- `actions/checkout` now uses `persist-credentials: false`. The clone is\nanonymous. The app token in the push URL is the only credential. The\n`ls-remote`, `fetch`, and `push` commands authenticate as the app\ninstallation.\n- The push step stops immediately if the app token is empty. Before, an\nempty token caused an anonymous 403 with no clear cause.\n\nBoth workflows also get the failure-tracking issue step from\n`bump_genai_prices.yml`. A step with `if: failure()` uses\n`github-script` to file one issue. The step finds the issue again by a\nmarker comment. Later failures add a comment to the existing issue. They\ndo not open a new one. This makes a stopped scheduled workflow visible\nexactly once. Both jobs get `issues: write` for this step. If the\nreporting step itself fails, it writes a warning and lets the job\ncontinue. A reporting failure never hides the real failure.","tree":{"sha":"280388d598182e429828b9640e9786bef6cfdf4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/280388d598182e429828b9640e9786bef6cfdf4f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b0f0a465d7f847323340c5974973db30ade538a2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfgybCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7ZEQABa7lOajgrV2uZyvAvbD95CM\nNyxzRR0xc+Hzf6UvAAqDcf4nC66fVCf2H/WCA+isWCZlzRbP5embzNWiUqJk9N+T\nzdbb5ZxVIm7rQVLKm9ftP+7OLuomp+YBWvkHez4bx+8SdOeEIRZcov9otmMrwCfy\nMQy7EptNbMulGCP1owbHaTBB79oC19ynIG9B2RZVqeBtqy6A0P3PrrMa+CklEHfn\nX4xG4+q0JV9z7H8b226fBSCgzHnVto3RvjzMhoOSElnHtOwPM+ZwPJRLr78LuJEU\nyVeu48zN3ZxqZZJAq9olFmOLH/DrkJ8jGe/yt8jD3fGzEWA5vAkAKw69mtrs/RRU\n448zcP2F/kJXMs1BszdfcIX1L0Y80NgZFSOF3zbLwE6kHxSyDY+je4oAg+HI6b1A\nAKBtDSCcETeE0x/gIJ0N7q7hRY69FbtkzIO9GTxdWV7ibKIZ+07Qu7on19U000Ha\nKUhDEqlLRfgeRkw6LN+sAQbWziNEchnhVAoKk38wrmDBu/o1ANSaNxVuGWgyhq0P\nRTSGJU3pXzeyNHu5s4fhsrZM6LtfS9RIhgTyZXwlDqXiNHrt0sXt10idxBxWwkUp\nd4njHKMDSszArkNrmKkT60tGtBcaWiy6gk9Uihr8iQhEH1X9gWfrjEVtreOD1dRh\n1BgZqkRoDRIisoX/jE5n\n=2Clk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 280388d598182e429828b9640e9786bef6cfdf4f\nparent bcc9db065921d90bb938054bdce14ca322394bb9\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786645659 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786645659 -0700\n\nfix(infra): authenticate app-token pushes in minimums and SDK pin workflows (#5480)\n\nThe dependency minimums and Code SDK pin workflows can push branches and\nopen PRs again. Before this change, both workflows failed with\n`Permission to langchain-ai/deepagents.git denied to\ngithub-actions[bot]`. The pushes now authenticate as the Org Membership\nApp installation. If the app token is empty, the step stops with a clear\nerror message. A failure in either workflow also files a tracking issue,\nor updates the existing one. This matches the genai-prices bump\nworkflow.\n\n---\n\n## Cause\n\nThis is the same bug that #5474 fixed in `bump_genai_prices.yml`.\n\nThe push step puts the app token in the push URL\n(`https://x-access-token:${GH_TOKEN}@github.com/...`). But\n`actions/checkout` ran first with the default `persist-credentials:\ntrue`. This stores the read-only `GITHUB_TOKEN` as an\n`http.https://github.com/.extraheader` credential. git cannot send two\n`Authorization` headers in one request. The credential in the config\nwins. git drops the app token from the URL. The push runs as\n`github-actions[bot]`. That token has only `contents: read` in these\njobs. GitHub denies the push with a 403. The error names\n`github-actions[bot]`, not the app bot.\n\nObserved failures:\n\n- `raise_langchain_minimums.yml`, run 31374913489. The job raised 18\nminimums and committed them. Then the push failed with a 403.\n- `bump_code_sdk_pin.yml`, run 30938354665. Listed in the #5474\ninvestigation.\n\n## Fix\n\nThe changes match #5474 in both workflows:\n\n- `actions/checkout` now uses `persist-credentials: false`. The clone is\nanonymous. The app token in the push URL is the only credential. The\n`ls-remote`, `fetch`, and `push` commands authenticate as the app\ninstallation.\n- The push step stops immediately if the app token is empty. Before, an\nempty token caused an anonymous 403 with no clear cause.\n\nBoth workflows also get the failure-tracking issue step from\n`bump_genai_prices.yml`. A step with `if: failure()` uses\n`github-script` to file one issue. The step finds the issue again by a\nmarker comment. Later failures add a comment to the existing issue. They\ndo not open a new one. This makes a stopped scheduled workflow visible\nexactly once. Both jobs get `issues: write` for this step. If the\nreporting step itself fails, it writes a warning and lets the job\ncontinue. A reporting failure never hides the real failure.","verified_at":"2026-08-13T18:27:42Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b0f0a465d7f847323340c5974973db30ade538a2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b0f0a465d7f847323340c5974973db30ade538a2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b0f0a465d7f847323340c5974973db30ade538a2/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"bcc9db065921d90bb938054bdce14ca322394bb9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bcc9db065921d90bb938054bdce14ca322394bb9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bcc9db065921d90bb938054bdce14ca322394bb9"}]},{"sha":"bcc9db065921d90bb938054bdce14ca322394bb9","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGJjYzlkYjA2NTkyMWQ5MGJiOTM4MDU0YmRjZTE0Y2EzMjIzOTRiYjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-13T18:17:41Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-13T18:17:41Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump uv to 0.12.3 (#5477)\n\nBumps the uv pin in `.github/actions/uv_setup/action.yml` from `0.12.1`\nto [`0.12.3`](https