/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"61ae398a60a2f6c23954d89332950570e0b6b431","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/61ae398a60a2f6c23954d89332950570e0b6b431","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/61ae398a60a2f6c23954d89332950570e0b6b431"}]},{"sha":"61ae398a60a2f6c23954d89332950570e0b6b431","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDYxYWUzOThhNjBhMmY2YzIzOTU0ZDg5MzMyOTUwNTcwZTBiNmI0MzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Johannes du Plessis","email":"johannes@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-13T18:06:57Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-13T18:06:57Z"},"message":"fix(code): stop passing removed `checkpoint_metadata` (#5473)\n\n`dcode --acp` starts successfully with the released `deepagents-acp`\nconstructor.\n\n---\n\nThe ACP persistence integration retained `checkpoint_metadata` after\nthat parameter was removed from `AgentServerACP` before release, causing\nevery ACP startup to exit before initialization. Remove the stale\nargument and bind the existing test double to the real constructor\nsignature so dependency API drift fails the focused test.\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"5cf330c3b2410dabc849348c0672d58ea91827c7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5cf330c3b2410dabc849348c0672d58ea91827c7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/61ae398a60a2f6c23954d89332950570e0b6b431","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfgfBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhnIQABXhBRWF/z78zqCxK4SotyxK\n20YZwwQVhCkNQqE90TwDkQIP/F3deOBsvBaaQNp1fWeKFcnw5zkfJdBVQx4eZCsr\nv7Y0YWh5xivglWdGQhMBQ+8/yzfWoT9mHwyeVxwWBf4HsI9IkjQI1xLO682UQFrr\nuEbrv7vOzfNdXtSacCBEr2O1qiVHK0at+x7prGSxpJHRRY+EiJy5jdvsbZXdOyV9\nT/lT+izRA/00TUWYXqj7RTwyTPTn8RvS+R54m4Fi7NoCpnoRhF/KN1UZWTAlv2+y\nOqi9e6X+a/XRFNFDwGFoj221sanwYvS+24bxCMNYiaNRMo6XleQCe3hRUwU+6SgF\nmb6Y7J+BKkwx62rm1HUn1pIHLOj/0simSMjIXHE6SWUkU/A6F1h0ZM8Y4usODPb0\n1/7YzXYcUJ/M9e48nsgpE2kNSbTK+XkKUVywn/tYvQX3FkomST3NKFqWVhHs/sPy\nRx5HuWfRJyYEwvAqmocoDMNgaiWWZ58VLDiNpAjfyhYYEG7wQ5Mp5vxaPF90zYp3\nm7joM3T1oGtYcWcwlGKZLhUzNsm/gb/csYwTW2LO7KtsGi0uEiZV+UF3k5SWymZ5\nXMb1sBNR6UNa7s/ubfbLmAXQQm4aER6oXP3vblOdHmKYU1VZPmWm6Vq5PTwOnt9D\na5cxR0KYnQg9mVkIzSsN\n=mJuz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5cf330c3b2410dabc849348c0672d58ea91827c7\nparent 4d2db042b279b33d6e0b031341938c3f3ce42d34\nauthor Johannes du Plessis <johannes@langchain.dev> 1786644417 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786644417 -0700\n\nfix(code): stop passing removed `checkpoint_metadata` (#5473)\n\n`dcode --acp` starts successfully with the released `deepagents-acp`\nconstructor.\n\n---\n\nThe ACP persistence integration retained `checkpoint_metadata` after\nthat parameter was removed from `AgentServerACP` before release, causing\nevery ACP startup to exit before initialization. Remove the stale\nargument and bind the existing test double to the real constructor\nsignature so dependency API drift fails the focused test.\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-13T18:07:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/61ae398a60a2f6c23954d89332950570e0b6b431","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/61ae398a60a2f6c23954d89332950570e0b6b431","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/61ae398a60a2f6c23954d89332950570e0b6b431/comments","author":{"login":"johannes117","id":51395795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMzk1Nzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51395795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117","html_url":"https://github.com/johannes117","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/johannes117/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4d2db042b279b33d6e0b031341938c3f3ce42d34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4d2db042b279b33d6e0b031341938c3f3ce42d34","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4d2db042b279b33d6e0b031341938c3f3ce42d34"}]},{"sha":"4d2db042b279b33d6e0b031341938c3f3ce42d34","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDRkMmRiMDQyYjI3OWIzM2Q2ZTBiMDMxMzQxOTM4YzNmM2NlNDJkMzQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]","email":"248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-13T18:05:33Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-13T18:05:33Z"},"message":"chore(deps): bump genai-prices in deepagents-code to 0.1.2 (#5476)\n\nBumps `genai-prices` in `libs/code/uv.lock` from `0.1.1` to `0.1.2` —\nthe newest version permitted by the range declared in\n`libs/code/pyproject.toml`, which is unchanged — via `uv lock\n--upgrade-package genai-prices`.\n\nOpened automatically by `bump_genai_prices.yml`. It runs daily because\ndcode fetches the genai-prices catalog at runtime, so the pinned package\nneeds to stay new enough to parse a freshly fetched snapshot. If a newer\ncompatible version lands before this PR merges, the next daily run\nforce-pushes it onto this branch and rewrites this description.\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a9f4a0c4d5d62f2d0132f2d84659fb8fab06f029","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a9f4a0c4d5d62f2d0132f2d84659fb8fab06f029"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/4d2db042b279b33d6e0b031341938c3f3ce42d34","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfgdtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJ9oQAA2fm382tVKQtLb+wGsAZ2pV\n3fxLQfffp5N8uLsvqe5gcD66DgwzyJsatA3u6nJJmVDU8uc0r9tLGUxQdY4ByRex\nvqglcjn/AwG0Y0d6P74TXDjWgp9Btt8JDNp7DIc079lynKLvyXFlPaRQhyeZ1gaP\ndkt2qPCK/TtVy9+pcti65f7zMrwgA/xWhEddbRV8+PZb0n+YhNqJGsAO7y3RJDcj\nCGVqLE1wDpYEw2icQDgokUOT/N4oVK9PwQrChBNBpJnc0N6BPgwSu6I1AqUNE1xf\n9nlNHU5zvJiWD5du2hFvkhwEbjz9linZIcISdE7BlBtF8dK66LNnoKKxx2NRF2hz\nGYYJfiMvkECOuZCcmf91zr28mlTd+S2drH+rOTl/kTZj+AzipG5+mZnZhyMJR67t\ni+obAJyUA38j3VC8sPpRxi4QNrfQAsyqkmEFBJ9GvjspntaNnrFVriqxdYPB38/W\nSgH5y0b2wPl1d23xW4DPf2xN8IDKjdg5gWCXuQSyhX49jchaLhtGMZ4rCWQAIgP3\ng1UdU+uUTpyKDK/yU0F5vDVMxNBEYcH3Aw/GuQJ+VYPOwDmyOKn6FtgywMNH8/tm\nGzuIdZfeu3bdsgfbfORCQ7zw6Xbmkminih0U5FeUPns8TerSYKpM++N8OqNbaVF3\nlvqEXiemW75QpoRmG6am\n=Rgbh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a9f4a0c4d5d62f2d0132f2d84659fb8fab06f029\nparent ab496c17e1a921b3ec9797f6dc45d27c185e6ae5\nauthor langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1786644333 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786644333 -0700\n\nchore(deps): bump genai-prices in deepagents-code to 0.1.2 (#5476)\n\nBumps `genai-prices` in `libs/code/uv.lock` from `0.1.1` to `0.1.2` —\nthe newest version permitted by the range declared in\n`libs/code/pyproject.toml`, which is unchanged — via `uv lock\n--upgrade-package genai-prices`.\n\nOpened automatically by `bump_genai_prices.yml`. It runs daily because\ndcode fetches the genai-prices catalog at runtime, so the pinned package\nneeds to stay new enough to parse a freshly fetched snapshot. If a newer\ncompatible version lands before this PR merges, the next daily run\nforce-pushes it onto this branch and rewrites this description.\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-13T18:05:36Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4d2db042b279b33d6e0b031341938c3f3ce42d34","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/4d2db042b279b33d6e0b031341938c3f3ce42d34","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/4d2db042b279b33d6e0b031341938c3f3ce42d34/comments","author":{"login":"langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]","id":248757908,"node_id":"BOT_kgDODtO-lA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/2441712?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/langchain-oss-automated-triage","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/langchain-oss-automated-triage%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"ab496c17e1a921b3ec9797f6dc45d27c185e6ae5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ab496c17e1a921b3ec9797f6dc45d27c185e6ae5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ab496c17e1a921b3ec9797f6dc45d27c185e6ae5"}]},{"sha":"ab496c17e1a921b3ec9797f6dc45d27c185e6ae5","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGFiNDk2YzE3ZTFhOTIxYjNlYzk3OTdmNmRjNDVkMjdjMTg1ZTZhZTU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-13T18:01:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-13T18:01:17Z"},"message":"fix(infra): authenticate genai-prices bump push as the app installation (#5474)\n\nFixes #5468\n\nThe daily `genai-prices` bump PR opens again. The push now authenticates\nas the Org Membership App installation, not as `github-actions[bot]`.\nThe PR it opens now triggers `pull_request` workflows, so the required\nchecks run.\n\n---\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe push step put the app token in the push URL:\n`https://x-access-token:${GH_TOKEN}@github.com/...`.\n\nBut `actions/checkout` ran first with its default `persist-credentials:\ntrue`. This stored the read-only `GITHUB_TOKEN` as an\n`http.https://github.com/.extraheader` credential. The run log shows\nthis: `http.https://github.com/.extraheader AUTHORIZATION: basic ***`.\n\ngit cannot send two `Authorization` headers on one request. When a\ncredential is in the config, git uses it and ignores the token in the\nURL. So git sent the `GITHUB_TOKEN` header and dropped the app token.\n\nThe push ran as `github-actions[bot]`. That token has only `contents:\nread` on this job. GitHub denied the push:\n\n```\nremote: Permission to langchain-ai/deepagents.git denied to github-actions[bot].\n```\n\nThe error names `github-actions[bot]`, not the app's bot. This shows the\napp token never reached the remote.\n\n### Why not the other causes\n\n- **Empty app token:** No. The token step succeeded. The step env showed\n`GH_TOKEN: ***` (a value, not empty). The `client-id` matched the repo\nvariable. The token existed but was not used.\n- **App lacks `contents: write`:** No. A valid token with wrong\npermissions would name the app's bot in the error, not\n`github-actions[bot]`.\n\nThis bug is not specific to this workflow. Every workflow that pushes\nwith an `x-access-token` URL after a default `actions/checkout` fails\nthe same way. Examples: `bump_code_sdk_pin.yml` (run 30938354665) and\n`raise_langchain_minimums.yml` (run 31374913489). No app-token push ever\nsucceeded.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `actions/checkout` now uses `persist-credentials: false`. The clone is\nanonymous. The app token in the push URL is now the only credential. The\n`ls-remote`, `fetch`, and `push` all use that URL, so they authenticate\nas the app installation.\n- Added a check: if the app token is empty, the step fails with a clear\nmessage. Before, an empty token caused a confusing anonymous 403.\n\n## What did not change\n\n- The job `permissions:` block is the same: `contents: read`,\n`pull-requests: read`, `issues: write`. The push uses the app token, not\n`GITHUB_TOKEN`.\n- The idempotency logic, the never-force-push-a-human-tip guard, and the\n`--force-with-lease` logic are unchanged.\n- The failure-tracking issue step is unchanged. It still uses `issues:\nwrite`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `actionlint` on the workflow: clean (exit 0).\n- The YAML parses. The push step's script passes `bash -n`.\n- I could not dry-run `workflow_dispatch` from this branch. GitHub\noffers `workflow_dispatch` only for workflows on the default branch. A\nreal dispatch would push the real bump branch. The fix is verified by\nthe credential-resolution logic above, not by a live push.","tree":{"sha":"a3baac5e138b153a7c75e92f9ac4274340cdb89f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a3baac5e138b153a7c75e92f9ac4274340cdb89f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/ab496c17e1a921b3ec9797f6dc45d27c185e6ae5","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfgZtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhDYQAJc86/mmHUT1kfbI/rWQMHSh\n9EtevCNpv85s+D7Vq8vOQy2XwttE7lhlxoqQ3Y1g8DhdgDCcp5EhRKQpXs0b6jrG\n4k+OiNnw3KK57wckcnQUlW4h1o2KtsO38gEBJ9XGvV1o2vmzVgaGlqgDQSBgkqUQ\nBnVKUifOHS9C+oUU7wGDtx2bn09Ajka38WItx4bGlTKwz7vfHP0y01wenPCXKR3G\nTrizJb3QxWFet39Lran7JXpMytmdipEu1cUIGdmuFIlY/cBPJBKuluNMcyZRJ2rB\nEzLaoNKQFmmAfS6bMYTROUbvXEmTSMzT0hLg7a8AY0uVc4Y4baUheJNfq3IaRX+V\n0qOvnRyO3KuCTXsqG6QBHZLiskCcX+aVBCnEzVv4btoWdMKrULIZ0nHh2Xqp84yp\nqCEFNndZ7KAp7CA5fmWqt+aBxTrhEoPqzjRsD/Kd/f3mSvVVjOqIt+cYn7VB1+uY\nWryXPKediwc6D5j96F6fNm8UHraELcVXMKbMgRnMhY5Y4ha7c4RUEH+5s53mdLM5\nu8VmPSZxbvPcAiYyYxTQyWUIOum6xWNQEsnDGcobv71GqG0A/+c8oR8Z5AQF9GcK\nSyKYkiMGZVf2hD3+Mj0WagZnpq7+X6RZCRA3L1y7dVYrFA9m5qHMRVAO/1gO4svU\neIr772vhUt99URwagNyE\n=ET9I\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a3baac5e138b153a7c75e92f9ac4274340cdb89f\nparent 387876a9a7aa18b8c9c6ad6f022351b64916417c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786644077 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786644077 -0700\n\nfix(infra): authenticate genai-prices bump push as the app installation (#5474)\n\nFixes #5468\n\nThe daily `genai-prices` bump PR opens again. The push now authenticates\nas the Org Membership App installation, not as `github-actions[bot]`.\nThe PR it opens now triggers `pull_request` workflows, so the required\nchecks run.\n\n---\n\n## Root cause\n\nThe push step put the app token in the push URL:\n`https://x-access-token:${GH_TOKEN}@github.com/...`.\n\nBut `actions/checkout` ran first with its default `persist-credentials:\ntrue`. This stored the read-only `GITHUB_TOKEN` as an\n`http.https://github.com/.extraheader` credential. The run log shows\nthis: `http.https://github.com/.extraheader AUTHORIZATION: basic ***`.\n\ngit cannot send two `Authorization` headers on one request. When a\ncredential is in the config, git uses it and ignores the token in the\nURL. So git sent the `GITHUB_TOKEN` header and dropped the app token.\n\nThe push ran as `github-actions[bot]`. That token has only `contents:\nread` on this job. GitHub denied the push:\n\n```\nremote: Permission to langchain-ai/deepagents.git denied to github-actions[bot].\n```\n\nThe error names `github-actions[bot]`, not the app's bot. This shows the\napp token never reached the remote.\n\n### Why not the other causes\n\n- **Empty app token:** No. The token step succeeded. The step env showed\n`GH_TOKEN: ***` (a value, not empty). The `client-id` matched the repo\nvariable. The token existed but was not used.\n- **App lacks `contents: write`:** No. A valid token with wrong\npermissions would name the app's bot in the error, not\n`github-actions[bot]`.\n\nThis bug is not specific to this workflow. Every workflow that pushes\nwith an `x-access-token` URL after a default `actions/checkout` fails\nthe same way. Examples: `bump_code_sdk_pin.yml` (run 30938354665) and\n`raise_langchain_minimums.yml` (run 31374913489). No app-token push ever\nsucceeded.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `actions/checkout` now uses `persist-credentials: false`. The clone is\nanonymous. The app token in the push URL is now the only credential. The\n`ls-remote`, `fetch`, and `push` all use that URL, so they authenticate\nas the app installation.\n- Added a check: if the app token is empty, the step fails with a clear\nmessage. Before, an empty token caused a confusing anonymous 403.\n\n## What did not change\n\n- The job `permissions:` block is the same: `contents: read`,\n`pull-requests: read`, `issues: write`. The push uses the app token, not\n`GITHUB_TOKEN`.\n- The idempotency logic, the never-force-push-a-human-tip guard, and the\n`--force-with-lease` logic are unchanged.\n- The failure-tracking issue step is unchanged. It still uses `issues:\nwrite`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `actionlint` on the workflow: clean (exit 0).\n- The YAML parses. The push step's script passes `bash -n`.\n- I could not dry-run `workflow_dispatch` from this branch. GitHub\noffers `workflow_dispatch` only for workflows on the default branch. A\nreal dispatch would push the real bump branch. The fix is verified by\nthe credential-resolution logic above, not by a live push.","verified_at":"2026-08-13T18:01:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ab496c17e1a921b3ec9797f6dc45d27c185e6ae5","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/ab496c17e1a921b3ec9797f6dc45d27c185e6ae5","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/ab496c17e1a921b3ec9797f6dc45d27c185e6ae5/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"387876a9a7aa18b8c9c6ad6f022351b64916417c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/387876a9a7aa18b8c9c6ad6f022351b64916417c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/387876a9a7aa18b8c9c6ad6f022351b64916417c"}]},{"sha":"387876a9a7aa18b8c9c6ad6f022351b64916417c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDM4Nzg3NmE5YTdhYTE4YjhjOWM2YWQ2ZjAyMjM1MWI2NDkxNjQxN2M","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-13T17:58:43Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-13T17:58:43Z"},"message":"chore(infra): comment release outcome on merged release PRs (#5459)\n\nWhen the release pipeline finishes, post the result (published, failed,\nor cancelled, with a link to each run) as a comment on the merged\nrelease PR. Readers see the outcome on the attributing PR without\nopening each run.\n\n---\n\nToday, the release pipeline comments on a merged release PR with links\nto the publish runs it started. That comment does not change. To know if\npublishing succeeded, you must open each linked run.\n\nThis change adds a workflow that runs when the release pipeline ends. It\nposts a new comment on the release PR with the result of each publish\nrun.\n\nHow it works:\n\n- It finds the release PR from the release pipeline's merge commit on\n`main`, the same way the pipeline's first comment does.\n- It finds the publish runs by their exact title (`release(<package>):\n<version>`) and start time, the same way the first comment does. It does\nnot match runs by commit, because the publish run's commit can differ\nfrom the merge commit. A manual re-release of the same package and\nversion in that window is included in the report.\n- Before posting, it checks the PR's comments for an identical result\ncomment. Re-running this workflow does not post twice.","tree":{"sha":"7e794bfd4c2971173ffe3101623de2e9704103aa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7e794bfd4c2971173ffe3101623de2e9704103aa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/387876a9a7aa18b8c9c6ad6f022351b64916417c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfgXTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAs88QAA39PJBYpU6KS/KRV58hI4Q8\nIrtfp1OidhV1Mwx85xr3uA9I/r+6xKXXI+2WdVJzLpYIwKK5cFCGRdUw0Gq82dFu\nttzPFtGp0ccYNSz0CaP5k2GuyMEVMbpyJ+5G7QxjBR1NTegd7TlyjC15U0w/4Ur5\nJk+s4czztomM4tH0x7jyBJmxZ4lqtCkQpibKLkfSdrpQi3kJO4ozoFHrYbkKKIQe\nYDfcJSSJwAjQoQW37pC+q/owyCXPpsJNYuajReBbr8UA8yI63P5YQT+qJSwhCnZ0\n7VIuzImDNGqaj0MmB57l/HlsrW/UnSUe078VW2O/T/7pVnbGLtqR/j2D7l8QJ1dF\nJ9yI5Xd3migisqz63cG0lYmLyd2u+s3JqA9Rjaq4EzfIwbSka6XDqWpRut5h2rqV\nUlH+5+U8lCIwOb8chUFt+8gFQ3tGwQ/jFgLT+JdztnJbaJ3OOWQFw3BaoDlSPUQI\n3kNGw/MeJNg+pXuHGhn85CsjuYzKBG+g2m6jUFjTRLFtMlvojHjwK5gPi5iL7qHh\n2b0spWvAkRGU0KMyZR2aJJr/TsICiCzeesc/QtGjXg47TfTh4OCDw/Ke5tUFYoRH\nALBAjESls7TLTVU2DObgKj24n4DsDS11c88fUIb8mUa5yC9IguQHV+ZKslEEsKb7\nk/SrkraHbB605FfELwyC\n=0pNU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7e794bfd4c2971173ffe3101623de2e9704103aa\nparent f3b4f7d361f936553533a1541c933b7bceb20cc1\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786643923 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786643923 -0700\n\nchore(infra): comment release outcome on merged release PRs (#5459)\n\nWhen the release pipeline finishes, post the result (published, failed,\nor cancelled, with a link to each run) as a comment on the merged\nrelease PR. Readers see the outcome on the attributing PR without\nopening each run.\n\n---\n\nToday, the release pipeline comments on a merged release PR with links\nto the publish runs it started. That comment does not change. To know if\npublishing succeeded, you must open each linked run.\n\nThis change adds a workflow that runs when the release pipeline ends. It\nposts a new comment on the release PR with the result of each publish\nrun.\n\nHow it works:\n\n- It finds the release PR from the release pipeline's merge commit on\n`main`, the same way the pipeline's first comment does.\n- It finds the publish runs by their exact title (`release(<package>):\n<version>`) and start time, the same way the first comment does. It does\nnot match runs by commit, because the publish run's commit can differ\nfrom the merge commit. A manual re-release of the same package and\nversion in that window is included in the report.\n- Before posting, it checks the PR's comments for an identical result\ncomment. Re-running this workflow does not post twice.","verified_at":"2026-08-13T17:58:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/387876a9a7aa18b8c9c6ad6f022351b64916417c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/387876a9a7aa18b8c9c6ad6f022351b64916417c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/387876a9a7aa18b8c9c6ad6f022351b64916417c/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f3b4f7d361f936553533a1541c933b7bceb20cc1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f3b4f7d361f936553533a1541c933b7bceb20cc1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f3b4f7d361f936553533a1541c933b7bceb20cc1"}]},{"sha":"f3b4f7d361f936553533a1541c933b7bceb20cc1","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGYzYjRmN2QzNjFmOTM2NTUzNTMzYTE1NDFjOTMzYjdiY2ViMjBjYzE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-13T17:56:19Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-13T17:56:19Z"},"message":"test(code): close leaked resources behind unraisable warnings (#5472)\n\nThis change closes three resource leaks in the test suite. Each one\nproduces a warning that is reported against the wrong test, which makes\nthe output misleading.\n\n---\n\n**The problem**\n\nTests can leave files and folders open. Python does not close them\nimmediately. It closes them later, during garbage collection, which runs\nat unpredictable times — often in the middle of a different test. The\nwarning is reported there.\n\nSo the test named in the output is whichever test happened to be running\nwhen garbage collection occurred, not the test that left the resource\nopen. The same leak can point at a different test on each run.\n\nThese warnings are printed rather than fatal: `pyproject.toml` sets\n`filterwarnings = [\"error\", ...,\n\"default::pytest.PytestUnraisableExceptionWarning\"]`, and the later\nentry wins. So this is noise and misdirection in the output, not a\nfailing build. Closing the leaks is also what makes it possible to\npromote that filter to `error::` later.\n\n**The three leaks**\n\n1. **An open pipe.** Two test helpers start a subprocess and read its\noutput without closing the pipe.\n2. **A folder that is not removed.** One test stops a server\nmid-startup. Startup has already created a temporary folder, allocated\nbefore the failure and outside the cleanup path, so nothing removes it.\n3. **A log file that stays open.** When `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG` is set,\nthe package opens a log file at import time. A later test clears the\nlogger, dropping the handle without closing it.\n\n**The fix**\n\n- The helpers close the pipe after reading it, and also release the\npipe, pty, and child process if the wait times out.\n- The server test calls `stop()`, which removes the folder.\n- A new fixture closes any tagged debug-log handler left attached,\nsweeping before each test and once at session end. A test covers the\ninvariant that the sweep leaves handlers it does not own untouched.\n\n**On the third leak**\n\nLeaving a handler attached is not itself the bug — the logger holds a\nstrong reference, so the handler is not collected. The failure comes one\nstep later, when a different test clears or replaces that logger's\nhandlers and drops the last reference. That is why the blame lands on an\nunrelated test.\n\nHandlers still attached at interpreter exit are closed cleanly by\n`logging.shutdown()` via `atexit`, so they produce no warning. The\nsession-end sweep is therefore tidiness — the per-test fixture is\nsetup-only, so nothing would otherwise sweep after the final test.","tree":{"sha":"6f3963a0c1a2f5ee5130548891aff442c5c6a591","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/6f3963a0c1a2f5ee5130548891aff442c5c6a591"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f3b4f7d361f936553533a1541c933b7bceb20cc1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfgVDCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAM6QQAD7XYwEoyYK0tr/lwaIp0mJS\nNa/ogn+UdaVS6+BDk40t+ZOhBgIHNEWI6WpddWxlrdIcwFb3gK9VpAIb3LG70+Qk\nf8xbXgTrm3SBY/V0sbrNq3JnyPOPu/3uBa1nKP2cw4FlvLlqXZkgMzK6y4xlmIOS\nnZcxpor8+Vl0bmuwYGQBcrmBdKn0f36ldqKq9zSxtjRz8oLvmUZ+a1t06NRTZ3S3\nxcl1dDtnqvlzxe1VCz6mQupLW1QVuRBXF5UleKz0OrvhlTHQ1tf5Fo+R0sA1Kr9/\nMjc0LmDs2Pr2W60lDlJKWGFYBXqaK5pERiVz5xvKXfA7uHO5Lf6ifdkxcv5RIhx/\nGylSY7RXN/mmSusM5ysZwErukCeGvh//ySo7UuUPKVYElRmFR/q0tazaYfr9qdQb\nIb93iY1rrPGf986ShoE0aQgeNwrKYSwCSUfkmsoIqY74dLk7+xIk/VjCuC2AGpj9\nLrej9EirMt6nrxIgts3WBJIKgod8SYrI0zQ3PhLIVqYaPyGHys8NDX7hvtwJFdT6\nO8oE4CcaRVauOyU/enqV5BgjXr147+e9081by34yHXANS8WMBLWOvGAPCNYgTBf7\nAaWBJIRbg+Uvc++K7owSBHaAXsdoJncqnknFYjuwWK0V8tXyDeGeJ/QH+7IbBQyf\n3j3pjUSGVyh2/XNnkOt5\n=1n5V\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 6f3963a0c1a2f5ee5130548891aff442c5c6a591\nparent 8d4cabc23585bc35fb10da9049c150e3e35e460e\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786643779 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786643779 -0700\n\ntest(code): close leaked resources behind unraisable warnings (#5472)\n\nThis change closes three resource leaks in the test suite. Each one\nproduces a warning that is reported against the wrong test, which makes\nthe output misleading.\n\n---\n\n**The problem**\n\nTests can leave files and folders open. Python does not close them\nimmediately. It closes them later, during garbage collection, which runs\nat unpredictable times — often in the middle of a different test. The\nwarning is reported there.\n\nSo the test named in the output is whichever test happened to be running\nwhen garbage collection occurred, not the test that left the resource\nopen. The same leak can point at a different test on each run.\n\nThese warnings are printed rather than fatal: `pyproject.toml` sets\n`filterwarnings = [\"error\", ...,\n\"default::pytest.PytestUnraisableExceptionWarning\"]`, and the later\nentry wins. So this is noise and misdirection in the output, not a\nfailing build. Closing the leaks is also what makes it possible to\npromote that filter to `error::` later.\n\n**The three leaks**\n\n1. **An open pipe.** Two test helpers start a subprocess and read its\noutput without closing the pipe.\n2. **A folder that is not removed.** One test stops a server\nmid-startup. Startup has already created a temporary folder, allocated\nbefore the failure and outside the cleanup path, so nothing removes it.\n3. **A log file that stays open.** When `DEEPAGENTS_CODE_DEBUG` is set,\nthe package opens a log file at import time. A later test clears the\nlogger, dropping the handle without closing it.\n\n**The fix**\n\n- The helpers close the pipe after reading it, and also release the\npipe, pty, and child process if the wait times out.\n- The server test calls `stop()`, which removes the folder.\n- A new fixture closes any tagged debug-log handler left attached,\nsweeping before each test and once at session end. A test covers the\ninvariant that the sweep leaves handlers it does not own untouched.\n\n**On the third leak**\n\nLeaving a handler attached is not itself the bug — the logger holds a\nstrong reference, so the handler is not collected. The failure comes one\nstep later, when a different test clears or replaces that logger's\nhandlers and drops the last reference. That is why the blame lands on an\nunrelated test.\n\nHandlers still attached at interpreter exit are closed cleanly by\n`logging.shutdown()` via `atexit`, so they produce no warning. The\nsession-end sweep is therefore tidiness — the per-test fixture is\nsetup-only, so nothing would otherwise sweep after the final test.","verified_at":"2026-08-13T17:56:23Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f3b4f7d361f936553533a1541c933b7bceb20cc1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f3b4f7d361f936553533a1541c933b7bceb20cc1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f3b4f7d361f936553533a1541c933b7bceb20cc1/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos