ommits/8dfe282006108dd0c47c50d5a1e3a41558e14723","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8dfe282006108dd0c47c50d5a1e3a41558e14723"}]},{"sha":"8dfe282006108dd0c47c50d5a1e3a41558e14723","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDhkZmUyODIwMDYxMDhkZDBjNDdjNTBkNWExZTNhNDE1NThlMTQ3MjM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-13T00:39:30Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-13T00:39:30Z"},"message":"fix(code): queue `/copy` during active generation (#5447)\n\n`/copy` now waits for active generation to finish before copying the\nlatest assistant message, and its success message now reads `Copied\nlatest response to clipboard.`\n\n---\n\nClassifying the command as queue-bound prevents it from racing an\nin-progress response and copying the prior completed response (which can\nbe confusing if you were expecting it to copy the in-progress\ngeneration).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d6cdd47e-3cb7-51d8-983c-4501047ec603)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"c1a8c8e58018a5e798a31e00cbfd8a9f1cf3627a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/c1a8c8e58018a5e798a31e00cbfd8a9f1cf3627a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/8dfe282006108dd0c47c50d5a1e3a41558e14723","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfRJCCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAin4QAE0A/wRvV+91+piBXKoPFtfn\no3ZAznkmYQGa1ZBjR5xMyY9ZG4gs2XihRtWkwfKdh7uG1+LG2UqyYoPJ0hsFxWP7\n1fp5uNh6RFcINwwoDh2qlworuVdMzU2ZijJGgz6oDSzKUG2EXsXwV1O3b14ZkWA+\nVQwy/H8d4OG5CEsX/5DmP0oxAONCYzvbpZAsfarr72EP430Zsv1GsgdlWpiWvw81\ng6dBn4LEu7xVSHhRR5b3L5/pwzzdOgeNHo/cbI1zU0XIrn6kMXrqtFwQhGoovyoR\nlrqSLa3RBtsRsBHqs6f/GPEjPop4UIMMM/sSsfuAeEh8u6/k8WPvywY78ac+cwE0\n+Zl7BbiYB27xGnWlP/JL0NVeFcVOsy/xZ8HDasXTSMwti2PpyLOQexgMxNhRuXkp\nR2EvX7NcTdWhPD4WyTS8oMs1iWEKP/F9EsFivtIbaxgP/YTbO7zgWAXuf8IvOfCt\n5+afvD047ssH9JTpUMgbtUmhjicVAZ1TEMZfOcYQDduHyBC4Rs0NzK6btsKjjstd\n+UOBA6e0Ez+BtK9LO1AFS30TpRhyQohGm61xuRH+2oAvrcvKNZyIYX+JHRyq8jl2\npMPNH+ToAna9Y2EDsR7y2qg5naY2yxmXyl2ME8RGJU8GQDtVyDUK91mJNHmtdT7g\n4sg2nHcQWz6dvXpsQYDu\n=h5kz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree c1a8c8e58018a5e798a31e00cbfd8a9f1cf3627a\nparent b630fb32e0510b434a7a7f273d7f730778bb55d2\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786581570 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786581570 -0700\n\nfix(code): queue `/copy` during active generation (#5447)\n\n`/copy` now waits for active generation to finish before copying the\nlatest assistant message, and its success message now reads `Copied\nlatest response to clipboard.`\n\n---\n\nClassifying the command as queue-bound prevents it from racing an\nin-progress response and copying the prior completed response (which can\nbe confusing if you were expecting it to copy the in-progress\ngeneration).\n\nMade by [Open\nSWE](https://openswe.vercel.app/agents/d6cdd47e-3cb7-51d8-983c-4501047ec603)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-13T00:39:33Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8dfe282006108dd0c47c50d5a1e3a41558e14723","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/8dfe282006108dd0c47c50d5a1e3a41558e14723","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/8dfe282006108dd0c47c50d5a1e3a41558e14723/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"b630fb32e0510b434a7a7f273d7f730778bb55d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b630fb32e0510b434a7a7f273d7f730778bb55d2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b630fb32e0510b434a7a7f273d7f730778bb55d2"}]},{"sha":"b630fb32e0510b434a7a7f273d7f730778bb55d2","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGI2MzBmYjMyZTA1MTBiNDM0YTdhN2YyNzNkN2Y3MzA3NzhiYjU1ZDI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-12T21:12:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-12T21:12:17Z"},"message":"feat(infra): post a timeline comment when `@release-bot draft` regenerates notes (#5456)\n\nRe-running `@release-bot draft` on a release PR now posts a short\ntimeline comment linking to the regenerated notes, so the refresh is\nvisible without re-opening the original comment.\n\n---\n\nRe-drafting edits the bot's curated-notes comment in place, and GitHub\nsurfaces comment edits quietly: no notification, no timeline entry. From\nthe timeline the PR looked unchanged, so a maintainer who re-ran `draft`\nwith steering instructions had no signal that the notes actually\nregenerated.\n\nThe upsert helper now reports whether it created or edited the draft\ncomment, and the draft job posts the pointer only after an in-place\nedit. First-time drafts (including the automatic `ready_for_review`\ndraft) post nothing extra — a brand-new comment already shows up in the\ntimeline. The notice is best-effort: if posting it fails, the draft\nstill succeeds and the failure lands as a workflow warning. The notice\nbody never mentions `@release-bot`, so it cannot re-trigger the command\nflow.\n\nExample — maintainer re-runs `draft` with steering instructions:\n\n1. Bot edits its existing curated-notes comment in place (no timeline\nentry).\n2. Bot posts a new timeline comment:\n\n> The curated release-notes comment on this PR was regenerated in place;\nreview the latest draft in [the original comment](#issuecomment-…).","tree":{"sha":"a968e334968b6a41937002e3888f932e5786bbe2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/a968e334968b6a41937002e3888f932e5786bbe2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/b630fb32e0510b434a7a7f273d7f730778bb55d2","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfOGxCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuYwQAJVLbs9hijPokYVcdKpdPvZT\nx5t1ZIDG4/tLgGGmkyzbcz+yHnIB5uEf6NUKUZlcDD1mHEfvc4EpF1LoIizJcxXl\naFbA086llBaC5+viIHBCpCKjls30wkAZoL05Y2vfSg6VP4h1++FY28LVS6oSRqlv\nDDh2eScn89MWbiNPE5zEvI0uNx2QQJeFsEGZ2lduLHwTMfqbXxddQLrLuJn4Q5KH\nJjW1D+1jT0YCseo1RvuRzBgcZSnalosEcU0FFlx+fmBbtthKxAhGO6+5Zu+b4ioJ\nUEaFc+KMZ1C+VquZFnxvVkaziSm1KGn+fB228RVwDjfjQcBaYg1dzk9b3lP1JBNl\nFlIE2Ail6Jrnzpw+5EvChBBfL1S3jzldJFOlGQ11vzndxiB+u2XcTWYCdbqFphwM\n+kKaq3kDJUCcEig5lxKzD678FpcBq1L9yxJLqE6HS+IQZKn+hyC6aF2gM+UVLME9\nvJ2gB/LFMPIT+g3+rVuq4AN4QW2r+GhmrYfElvvI39+E7A81FOLqrUFQRZPJR/r2\nGJwCRnhPyQmpzu9UVZalJ14V4mb0VoY5LElzqIdR0r5ciN/pzHc5JPW6aLcZ4H+v\ncMWcGHYkt+awGjTI1VhLE3lFGGzWNdZqcHMgXt4AZ+PIelp8r0sCY7qcXg9/iRz4\n2ssavpqWMfZvhjBjw4g0\n=1iH6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree a968e334968b6a41937002e3888f932e5786bbe2\nparent 3dd151d19ab0e687e8f36a79169c698fd4a16436\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786569137 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786569137 -0700\n\nfeat(infra): post a timeline comment when `@release-bot draft` regenerates notes (#5456)\n\nRe-running `@release-bot draft` on a release PR now posts a short\ntimeline comment linking to the regenerated notes, so the refresh is\nvisible without re-opening the original comment.\n\n---\n\nRe-drafting edits the bot's curated-notes comment in place, and GitHub\nsurfaces comment edits quietly: no notification, no timeline entry. From\nthe timeline the PR looked unchanged, so a maintainer who re-ran `draft`\nwith steering instructions had no signal that the notes actually\nregenerated.\n\nThe upsert helper now reports whether it created or edited the draft\ncomment, and the draft job posts the pointer only after an in-place\nedit. First-time drafts (including the automatic `ready_for_review`\ndraft) post nothing extra — a brand-new comment already shows up in the\ntimeline. The notice is best-effort: if posting it fails, the draft\nstill succeeds and the failure lands as a workflow warning. The notice\nbody never mentions `@release-bot`, so it cannot re-trigger the command\nflow.\n\nExample — maintainer re-runs `draft` with steering instructions:\n\n1. Bot edits its existing curated-notes comment in place (no timeline\nentry).\n2. Bot posts a new timeline comment:\n\n> The curated release-notes comment on this PR was regenerated in place;\nreview the latest draft in [the original comment](#issuecomment-…).","verified_at":"2026-08-12T21:12:20Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b630fb32e0510b434a7a7f273d7f730778bb55d2","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/b630fb32e0510b434a7a7f273d7f730778bb55d2","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/b630fb32e0510b434a7a7f273d7f730778bb55d2/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3dd151d19ab0e687e8f36a79169c698fd4a16436","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3dd151d19ab0e687e8f36a79169c698fd4a16436","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3dd151d19ab0e687e8f36a79169c698fd4a16436"}]},{"sha":"3dd151d19ab0e687e8f36a79169c698fd4a16436","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDNkZDE1MWQxOWFiMGU2ODdlOGYzNmE3OTE2OWM2OThmZDRhMTY0MzY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-12T20:54:56Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-12T20:54:56Z"},"message":"docs(infra): document how to observe a `@release-bot` run (#5457)\n\nDocuments where to find the Actions run after commenting `@release-bot\ndraft` or `@release-bot apply` on a release PR.\n\n---\n\nThe workflow triggers on `issue_comment`, not the PR's head branch, so\nit never appears as a PR status check — an agent or maintainer looking\nonly at the PR's check list would conclude nothing ran. The new\nsubsection under \"Curated Release Notes\" points readers to the Actions\ntab (\"📝 Curate release notes\"), the equivalent `gh run list` invocation,\nthe bot's PR feedback comments as a passive signal, and the per-PR\nqueuing behavior when commands are posted back-to-back.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <215916821+open-swe[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1769e79f2a6678b194622d92fa15d0bb8af0877b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1769e79f2a6678b194622d92fa15d0bb8af0877b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/3dd151d19ab0e687e8f36a79169c698fd4a16436","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfN2gCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAASaoQAKQRL0RHDEg9LRpXWnEXhS49\n+oigvsLqWvpEkJB5WvMMwSmqoW3HBx0evNsIA1yiHxlRSB6tobxYDY/g5rj/XHC2\nfgkkP0L92xEtdScXzm1Qv2G3PA9bXO/RmARIePPAJrJB0f1fnECv12tUat0jjagu\ngJ2qPBKK7k3Z7iAQrM+8V3x/+Ie/2YU7aCDfpnD/SJK+qGZLwjIMC4B4STyBfc2T\nP6HbxiuVKAv+nwKOPxN2aIscnQs0mNs64J1VUF5ZtEqT6K7mkK/t1wSxasqa9+qr\nWc524buaw3Fza9ZKC5zqbsAfFURtlmrvT8SrS8LukpMlPAFGidNSvlwwcYN8qXX2\nyNRSOLvkBGXnnOjX7WOpw1t7DisUOT4dM64Q5XTDy1CE8xdxc/r/zY1PXQqfy7iW\nDBhQqtPFHyLW0hZtv0bNeC/s5HXqXw/0lhBdWwjHwe0rGVvymOU/KIUIQdwWlvUx\nsMrRr7u7v09ZgGz4LojPZtyTLQSJbLYoUHrZV4kieBdSr5PvEabGQriDbwa1/HWV\nGqqgBiK9AZG7T3wG04Y5wx3qMh1Xh+1IEU57Xy698bR66PviT8z3qS/m3ods1yje\ndqABPcDGVMec2U6JPHNF1gtX6pWXGBepYeGU9Y3ltL2lAN8+eYtSLOcZpV7Itt7M\nZQiua09xBld4xh6oyE97\n=FpX1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1769e79f2a6678b194622d92fa15d0bb8af0877b\nparent faf14770da1764788807d06a8046145db85f806f\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786568096 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786568096 -0700\n\ndocs(infra): document how to observe a `@release-bot` run (#5457)\n\nDocuments where to find the Actions run after commenting `@release-bot\ndraft` or `@release-bot apply` on a release PR.\n\n---\n\nThe workflow triggers on `issue_comment`, not the PR's head branch, so\nit never appears as a PR status check — an agent or maintainer looking\nonly at the PR's check list would conclude nothing ran. The new\nsubsection under \"Curated Release Notes\" points readers to the Actions\ntab (\"📝 Curate release notes\"), the equivalent `gh run list` invocation,\nthe bot's PR feedback comments as a passive signal, and the per-PR\nqueuing behavior when commands are posted back-to-back.\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <215916821+open-swe[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","verified_at":"2026-08-12T20:54:59Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3dd151d19ab0e687e8f36a79169c698fd4a16436","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3dd151d19ab0e687e8f36a79169c698fd4a16436","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3dd151d19ab0e687e8f36a79169c698fd4a16436/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"faf14770da1764788807d06a8046145db85f806f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/faf14770da1764788807d06a8046145db85f806f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/faf14770da1764788807d06a8046145db85f806f"}]},{"sha":"faf14770da1764788807d06a8046145db85f806f","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGZhZjE0NzcwZGExNzY0Nzg4ODA3ZDA2YTgwNDYxNDVkYjg1ZjgwNmY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-12T20:42:45Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-12T20:42:45Z"},"message":"chore(infra): clarify `dangerous-nonmain-release` input description (#5455)\n\nThe old wording was ambiguous: \"backports and hotfixes\" could read as if\nthe input applied to hotfixes generally, but hotfix commits are normally\nlayered on top of the release-please squash-merge commit on `main` and\nreleased via the standard `release_commit` path. The non-main toggle is\nonly for the cases where the release genuinely cannot come from `main` —\na backport release cut from a version branch, or a hotfix that for some\nreason lives off `main`.","tree":{"sha":"38cdb1e12ce74f09eceecf613ff4ae6a97b798a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/38cdb1e12ce74f09eceecf613ff4ae6a97b798a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/faf14770da1764788807d06a8046145db85f806f","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfNrFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdnEQABAXYhwZV2NzvTXix+Kj4nE/\nK3ZkSSLrAXOJOC109yUufEX0mIOdQXLamGriboHAls5whrzLf5WfHpFXLywR0ld0\njyDo4PsknKdncgoRPOAW0e+zuK5kD4/bOf/ZDiNdM8ICUCpwwQoq3xZp0y0NQsR5\nbz1eer+OeP6NWE6ibdpABKbBaRWPGNidjoUyZEMXZtS6myJKJzemrR6/cZiknBMf\nfX1I42ZxnG0aGzd/vKWxAX3aOyfOzUkm7g3Hg/fre0tBSsi+Kvd2bPjdIRsj9TGb\nZ4zOx3ZDge6vHYdBa+VCRTYHev9E+i3BjXQEX7/xWcO3FEKWf2h/V0MIHU3XFXe3\n1akItc1y9Jb6sOKop/XMwaTqdPzegV5koc5fB92WfDxeB+dWTMJ2RXcBcFjQ7mQI\n7sEorLkCjYDnsh0Z08c0FY+y1csztS4C3LeHcL6SJPQSQXSXBGVCqFkF0MIeJlsm\n8vT8sDC4Zjixc7mdUwYBGhyVj59kQWEWu3m+Df5xxwcES/9OUH2R+aPDC4LnCcl7\nVeaDe0lu+/DxdOBkqIEXT1SThNbHLiBcziAUrRM6MTM5S3CSn2tPsFZHrdXzrbU3\nSdfTW9M9OnFcVdwnDRN4KLC8PLG1UG7BKEGawvUirHZwqJbqbeuLePHtvAfmSS+C\nkvOARF8pdbNJ6P5vOr6z\n=JEkv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 38cdb1e12ce74f09eceecf613ff4ae6a97b798a1\nparent 59c81641cf3c53b9d1574627eb15e888007dfaf9\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786567365 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786567365 -0700\n\nchore(infra): clarify `dangerous-nonmain-release` input description (#5455)\n\nThe old wording was ambiguous: \"backports and hotfixes\" could read as if\nthe input applied to hotfixes generally, but hotfix commits are normally\nlayered on top of the release-please squash-merge commit on `main` and\nreleased via the standard `release_commit` path. The non-main toggle is\nonly for the cases where the release genuinely cannot come from `main` —\na backport release cut from a version branch, or a hotfix that for some\nreason lives off `main`.","verified_at":"2026-08-12T20:42:48Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/faf14770da1764788807d06a8046145db85f806f","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/faf14770da1764788807d06a8046145db85f806f","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/faf14770da1764788807d06a8046145db85f806f/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"59c81641cf3c53b9d1574627eb15e888007dfaf9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/59c81641cf3c53b9d1574627eb15e888007dfaf9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/59c81641cf3c53b9d1574627eb15e888007dfaf9"}]},{"sha":"59c81641cf3c53b9d1574627eb15e888007dfaf9","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDU5YzgxNjQxY2YzYzUzYjlkMTU3NDYyN2ViMTVlODg4MDA3ZGZhZjk","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-12T20:07:42Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-12T20:07:42Z"},"message":"fix(evals): override `filelock` to `>=3.30.3` to clear harbor build-lock deadlocks (#5452)\n\n## Problem\n\nUnified evals run\n[31541400926](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/31541400926)\nlost **97 of 147 context trials** across all five models. Every shard\njob still reported ✅, so the failure was only visible in LangSmith and\nthe retained `exception.txt` files.\n\n91 of those trials died during environment setup with:\n\n```\nRuntimeError: Deadlock: lock '.../harbor-prebuilt-harbor-docker-egress-control-sidecar-*/.harbor-docker-build.lock'\nis already held by a different BaseAsyncFileLock instance in this task.\n```\n\nThis is\n[tox-dev/filelock#675](https://github.com/tox-dev/filelock/issues/675):\nin filelock 3.29.7 the reentrant-deadlock registry is a thread-local,\nbut the check runs on the event-loop thread, so every asyncio task on\nthat loop shares it. An `AsyncFileLock` acquire then raises a spurious\n\"Deadlock\" whenever a *different task* already holds the path. Fixed\nupstream in **3.30.3**.\n\nHarbor takes exactly that lock in `ensure_docker_image_built` around the\negress-control sidecar build. Every `cb-cloud-*` context task sets\n`network_mode = \"allowlist\"`, so on a cold runner the first trial holds\nthe lock through the image build and every trial starting after it dies\nimmediately. Lite runs 1 task/shard × 3 rollouts, so exactly one rollout\nper task survived and `avg@k` collapsed to `pass@k / 3`.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd `filelock>=3.30.3` to the existing `[tool.uv] override-dependencies`\nblock in `libs/evals`, and re-lock (3.29.7 → 3.32.2).\n\nAn override is required because `deepagents-code` declares\n`filelock>=3.29.7,<3.30`, and since 3.29.7 is the last 3.29 release that\nrange admits only the broken version. That cap is deliberately left\nalone: nothing outside harbor uses `AsyncFileLock`, and\n`deepagents-code` uses only the synchronous `FileLock`, so the bug never\naffected it.\n\n## Testing\n\nDrove harbor's real `ensure_docker_image_built` from 3 staggered\nconcurrent tasks against a live docker build, clearing the built image\nand build cache between arms so neither could early-return on a cache\nhit:\n\n| filelock | result |\n|---|---|\n| 3.29.7 | 1/3 succeeded, 2 raised `RuntimeError: Deadlock` |\n| 3.32.2 | 3/3 succeeded |\n\nThe 1-of-3 result reproduces the CI signature exactly. Note that the\nfull `-n 3 --env docker` path cannot run on macOS: `DockerEnvironment`\nonly enables egress control on Linux or when a kernel probe passes, and\nDocker Desktop's LinuxKit kernel lacks `CONFIG_NFT_FIB_INET`, so\nallowlist tasks are rejected before the sidecar is ever built. An\nend-to-end context run on a Linux runner is still worth doing on this\nbranch.","tree":{"sha":"32cb68460f0a70038b87959719b6122547842a82","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/32cb68460f0a70038b87959719b6122547842a82"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/59c81641cf3c53b9d1574627eb15e888007dfaf9","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfNKOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdS4QAAKZD64Ts7QwopzgaocJPvyK\nZ8ez4mCuMFbPSQz5MxYlVDwgyuciHQMFm2DnGPYPx0W46dNKbrk9X7gKW2oTm4qI\nIlNINGnukIMtIdbyiaZsEyrS6DuiQufXH2qKkjE8XUXCaDDmmm318jXLrGjD5yMJ\nAEWTlTjSna4eD7JQiQxc7FYqctYm1QEt1cmr+f5Ed8rgWeBDHueMsabwpRzY09dI\nWSftCWVtfUd/q9IS5FIl7Uymq/1kYJPjXJmPZqlpmxbxlgkK2KAtbinYnviS7iYE\nay31wHJ1eOGq6znVNz8RjhH4tQnP0ETLlpdxTCPvcuxn/DLjdyfB8ErvNoCejODx\nIhmYxD8dMTXmMp8EWax8WvjapBEebTAcnjc/ZUS3DNMahc0KTuSKE2NgV3lRxv87\nxv3FLsi9JgxH5jRq9Wc1LoUPVGR+7CcePwt80wbYgFvCokGKbUvriFr47rBvCxzw\nzMEsJwegX6elya0Rh2tcPtEA90xFjwOpiwh3c2grIQBe3WpW5BlziR0UUOj7cj/9\nmU/mm07oOos/eDKtv0Pg96aH98kQmx1FlQw5ZCZ6bSbvGtFtPepbwO6fbq3xMUqU\nUxkOAbmI38cS1AQleittIz5Ta29EOrL/E/VJiQCiqa1QsdsCM+9cyLEKMIjo8esO\nazenJspMofjRxs62GWNS\n=5iNI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 32cb68460f0a70038b87959719b6122547842a82\nparent 80fe3d3cbcd23b8ebbc2b1b0d67d7ea318d11ef6\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1786565262 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786565262 -0400\n\nfix(evals): override `filelock` to `>=3.30.3` to clear harbor build-lock deadlocks (#5452)\n\n## Problem\n\nUnified evals run\n[31541400926](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/actions/runs/31541400926)\nlost **97 of 147 context trials** across all five models. Every shard\njob still reported ✅, so the failure was only visible in LangSmith and\nthe retained `exception.txt` files.\n\n91 of those trials died during environment setup with:\n\n```\nRuntimeError: Deadlock: lock '.../harbor-prebuilt-harbor-docker-egress-control-sidecar-*/.harbor-docker-build.lock'\nis already held by a different BaseAsyncFileLock instance in this task.\n```\n\nThis is\n[tox-dev/filelock#675](https://github.com/tox-dev/filelock/issues/675):\nin filelock 3.29.7 the reentrant-deadlock registry is a thread-local,\nbut the check runs on the event-loop thread, so every asyncio task on\nthat loop shares it. An `AsyncFileLock` acquire then raises a spurious\n\"Deadlock\" whenever a *different task* already holds the path. Fixed\nupstream in **3.30.3**.\n\nHarbor takes exactly that lock in `ensure_docker_image_built` around the\negress-control sidecar build. Every `cb-cloud-*` context task sets\n`network_mode = \"allowlist\"`, so on a cold runner the first trial holds\nthe lock through the image build and every trial starting after it dies\nimmediately. Lite runs 1 task/shard × 3 rollouts, so exactly one rollout\nper task survived and `avg@k` collapsed to `pass@k / 3`.\n\n## Fix\n\nAdd `filelock>=3.30.3` to the existing `[tool.uv] override-dependencies`\nblock in `libs/evals`, and re-lock (3.29.7 → 3.32.2).\n\nAn override is required because `deepagents-code` declares\n`filelock>=3.29.7,<3.30`, and since 3.29.7 is the last 3.29 release that\nrange admits only the broken version. That cap is deliberately left\nalone: nothing outside harbor uses `AsyncFileLock`, and\n`deepagents-code` uses only the synchronous `FileLock`, so the bug never\naffected it.\n\n## Testing\n\nDrove harbor's real `ensure_docker_image_built` from 3 staggered\nconcurrent tasks against a live docker build, clearing the built image\nand build cache between arms so neither could early-return on a cache\nhit:\n\n| filelock | result |\n|---|---|\n| 3.29.7 | 1/3 succeeded, 2 raised `RuntimeError: Deadlock` |\n| 3.32.2 | 3/3 succeeded |\n\nThe 1-of-3 result reproduces the CI signature exactly. Note that the\nfull `-n 3 --env docker` path cannot run on macOS: `DockerEnvironment`\nonly enables egress control on Linux or when a kernel probe passes, and\nDocker Desktop's LinuxKit kernel lacks `CONFIG_NFT_FIB_INET`, so\nallowlist tasks are rejected before the sidecar is ever built. An\nend-to-end context run on a Linux runner is still worth doing on this\nbranch.","verified_at":"2026-08-12T20:07:46Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/59c81641cf3c53b9d1574627eb15e888007dfaf9","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/59c81641cf3c53b9d1574627eb15e888007dfaf9","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/59c81641cf3c53b9d1574627eb15e888007dfaf9/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"80fe3d3cbcd23b8ebbc2b1b0d67d7ea318d11ef6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/80fe3d3cbcd23b8ebbc2b1b0d67d7ea318d11ef6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/80fe3d3cbcd23b8ebbc2b1b0d67d7ea318d11ef6"}]},{"sha":"80fe3d3cbcd23b8ebbc2b1b0d67d7ea318d11ef6","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDgwZmUzZDNjYmNkMjNiOGViYmMyYjFiMGQ2N2Q3ZWEzMThkMTFlZjY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-08-12T20:06:31Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-12T20:06:31Z"},"message":"hotfix(code): skip checkout `pyproject.toml` test when running from a built wheel (#5453)\n\nA unit test that assumed a source checkout now skips when running from\nan installed wheel, unblocking the `deepagents-code` release pipeline.\n\n---\n\nThe test asserts a checkout-only file can be read, but the release\npipeline runs tests against the built wheel, where that file doesn't\nexist. It now checks for the file first and `pytest.skip`s when it's\nabsent; checkout behavior is unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"64102f4b7c0261376f69860492ce0cc248d4c314","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/64102f4b7c0261376f69860492ce0cc248d4c314"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/80fe3d3cbcd23b8ebbc2b1b0d67d7ea318d11ef6","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfNJHCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwT0QADaLABh2Q96BZlhW8ouhWmwR\n+Z2CcuCw68gjUHgd/Mr9jqQAahzP2CRsS3qeQYoHdGr9TvGe5oYlHkVqptcxyWa8\nrB08ExEvL/s7C2C1eXuRbg+rEZLta5FndCpTD9ELAtRDhmZPc3sIhC/c70Nt2Ivx\n36Wf3DUl5ABtZIlu3rw9HHe/1rr1X86iwkng1vlcWhJHnlgA+L/qk23vd4ois+AQ\nAM7uAdcfM3Yk6q8kM582O4cICjeqg9/4Lgwm4tW32vaGXY6mz0vYu5glYbIQmYuU\n4U0O69vD2VEfwI12iPEKwkRp68+mRua9jecZajYKow6drc7/1Vc99GNN/+yQjiyP\nkm6rAIyCGpqBkQOlRaF60dngPCm46a4rFs+G/kyJzVbtLGFkSybTbmGcyLN6cVf2\n/G8yz6R+36m5rXCIekm8mi5zGJX1X5PlVKuqjsw05teIt4KwsU6YqpgHLE5VXPHd\ndXFUXkpvwQMcKPVqVF4kHmMfTmSfzVLtcKx/3L54yAXG9vBSoEfON4I/oj3rHMZc\nMuIQC97TVzXkbchsq60yg/vWL7P/RmkovfWwJbOC6gDaTihax/jAIA7tICTIfsi9\nApb84GdjG6GIbkgxDkVrEv+njRbs1eNYtsDvB3cZMf08bfXpDwR6tnZJ4/j68jH3\nxAZkXcpOsJpIPGcmbAIZ\n=Hlq2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 64102f4b7c0261376f69860492ce0cc248d4c314\nparent 3f62cd7998561495d33502dd6481baadbb6c24ee\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1786565191 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786565191 -0700\n\nhotfix(code): skip checkout `pyproject.toml` test when running from a built wheel (#5453)\n\nA unit test that assumed a source checkout now skips when running from\nan installed wheel, unblocking the `deepagents-code` release pipeline.\n\n---\n\nThe test asserts a checkout-only file can be read, but the release\npipeline runs tests against the built wheel, where that file doesn't\nexist. It now checks for the file first and `pytest.skip`s when it's\nabsent; checkout behavior is unchanged.","verified_at":"2026-08-12T20:06:35Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/80fe3d3cbcd23b8ebbc2b1b0d67d7ea318d11ef6","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/80fe3d3cbcd23b8ebbc2b1b0d67d7ea318d11ef6","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/80fe3d3cbcd23b8ebbc2b1b0d67d7ea318d11ef6/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"3f62cd7998561495d33502dd6481baadbb6c24ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/3f62cd7998561495d33502dd6481baadbb6c24ee","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/3f62cd7998561495d33502dd6481baadbb6c24ee"}]},{"sha":"3f62cd7998561495d33502dd6481baadbb6c24ee","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDNmNjJjZDc5OTg1NjE0OTVkMzM1MDJkZDY0ODFiYWFkYmI2YzI0ZWU","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-08-12T19:23:20Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-12T19:23:20Z"},"message":"release(deepagents-code): 0.1.55 (#5396)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. Publish reads the merged CHANGELOG via `release.yml`,\nnot this PR description — keep them aligned anyway so the PR stays an\naccurate historical record for reviewers and anyone returning later._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.55](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.54...deepagents-code==0.1.55)\n(2026-08-12)\n\n### Features\n\n- Added a `/context` usage report for inspecting context consumption\n([#5407](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5407)).\n- Added a cache and context status row for at-a-glance session state\n([#5408](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5408)).\n- Added configurable warnings when a session exceeds the configured cost\nthreshold\n([#5405](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5405)).\n- Added support for persisting and reconfiguring ACP sessions\n([#5366](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5366)).\n- Added automatic updates for installed plugins\n([#5368](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5368)).\n- Added a toggle for diff line numbers\n([#5427](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5427)).\n- `Ctrl+S` in `/auto model` now stores `[models].auto_classifier`\n([#5313](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5313)).\n\n### Fixes\n\n- Restored edit diffs in resumed threads\n([#5391](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5391)).\n- Added a resume hint after crashes\n([#5412](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5412)).\n- Clarified the project hooks trust prompt and stopped prompting for\nuser hooks\n([#5426](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5426)).\n- Cleared dynamic subagents on the next turn\n([#5437](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5437)).\n- Improved grouped tool summaries by counting distinct targets\n([#5409](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5409)).\n- Improved ask-user choice wrapping and selection styling\n([#5442](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5442)).\n- Serialized `dcode` self-upgrades across processes\n([#5252](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5252)).\n- Added warnings for stale dependencies in editable installs\n([#5386](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5386)).\n- Hid incomplete extras from version output\n([#5352](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5352)).\n- Removed the optional-provider startup tip\n([#5421](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5421)).\n- Removed the “Message restored to input” toast\n([#5253](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5253)).\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757908+langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"29418c2a07e65c12d8ea745f3f03bcfe6d81bf3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/29418c2a07e65c12d8ea745f3f03bcfe6d81bf3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/3f62cd7998561495d33502dd6481baadbb6c24ee","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqfMgoCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEz8QAKffw8wYlPtDLYwcv2vnHIE3\nk0ZVSWGPgJUlAoSs3CwJeJRljgVdbmuryo2sKVVGj1uQX5IUaQIcNf7+zZJkfmlS\nZJJ3S3RVouPDj2tMRxl4LYBVcSLp2wEADE5giphNZot5sI0kNQ+a1li4XR/FlaP0\nAxXNvRXht7xX3ecTSTeaWJR0+wLMRTi1ETmb85gPzUqyyE+1Qh2qexdUE7Fm2jd1\nkuh2OuPsD5eD70v1GagjH+chIKayo4RB+9nKWq3PuEOXseOpoPKsjv6Tccumw9t4\nGs+KOkcCSO3qOKQ74hNX2OB1m4Cg/TWLo3LTlxwrBvZGxsnRsdxkNXws7xmmBK54\nnZLnvSCF8eE0TiW2z6QAkWWk35PhvEzt00n/eoG5rbLSTidXGSLcZy6tVCucsV61\nmWkF+ayPKyn+BT+prViNijG2FQ/KIbLISY9d0gc3MZ/slYnJkl6w6c3ebOm0UVal\nGHJOe1fDTFh5BA9LVPHIZHtxg5SBjBLeb4abNFLdjkWA3NojUur3EoyHd0DWw5gw\nIPs1P5sezjSVE7K8IvTnDaXryrrK9hu93i8KH++efu8On9XTIlgnxFrjKk7jFZ+i\n2WZxeYd9VCVUlhZ/SKWICEA6Kh2PBGPhPVJlDxkIs/q0zvLX9Ce0ZJnH4AUJB9Wv\nmmEj6JJboTdfolhBc1sU\n=2X89\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 29418c2a07e65c12d8ea745f3f03bcfe6d81bf3b\nparent 6cf062bfa22d1a34d895e0418e4e32a49f97d8dd\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1786562600 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786562600 +0000\n\nrelease(deepagents-code): 0.1.55 (#5396)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Release notes preview: keep this section in sync with the package\n`CHANGELOG.md`. Publish reads the merged CHANGELOG via `release.yml`,\nnot this PR description — keep them aligned anyway so the PR stays an\naccurate historical record for reviewers and anyone returning later._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.1.55](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents-code==0.1.54...deepagents-code==0.1.55)\n(2026-08-12)\n\n### Features\n\n- Added a `/context` usage report for inspecting context consumption\n([#5407](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5407)).\n- Added a cache and context status row for at-a-glance session state\n([#5408](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5408)).\n- Added configurable warnings when a session exceeds the configured cost\nthreshold\n([#5405](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5405)).\n- Added support for persisting and reconfiguring ACP sessions\n([#5366](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5366)).\n- Added automatic updates for installed plugins\n([#5368](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5368)).\n- Added a toggle for diff line numbers\n([#5427](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5427)).\n- `Ctrl+S` in `/auto model` now stores `[models].auto_classifier`\n([#5313](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5313)).\n\n### Fixes\n\n- Restored edit diffs in resumed threads\n([#5391](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5391)).\n- Added a resume hint after crashes\n([#5412](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5412)).\n- Clarified the project hooks trust prompt and stopped prompting for\nuser hooks\n([#5426](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5426)).\n- Cleared dynamic subagents on the next turn\n([#5437](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5437)).\n- Improved grouped tool summaries by counting distinct targets\n([#5409](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5409)).\n- Improved ask-user choice wrapping and selection styling\n([#5442](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5442)).\n- Serialized `dcode` self-upgrades across processes\n([#5252](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5252)).\n- Added warnings for stale dependencies in editable installs\n([#5386](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5386)).\n- Hid incomplete extras from version output\n([#5352](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5352)).\n- Removed the optional-provider startup tip\n([#5421](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5421)).\n- Removed the “Message restored to input” toast\n([#5253](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/5253)).\n\n_End release notes preview._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: langchain-oss-automated-triage[bot] <248757